E["npc:brave-moonhorn"] = {t="npc",n="Brave Moonhorn",z="thousandneedles",s="Brave Moonhorn is a tauren scout stationed at the top of the Great Lift on the southern border of the Barrens. From this precipice, he keeps watch over the entry to Thousand Needles and alerts travelers to the local dangers ahead.",h="Brave Moonhorn is a tauren scout stationed at the top of the Great Lift on the southern border of the Barrens.",sec={{t="Sentinel of the Lift",b="Perched above the sheer drops of Thousand Needles, Brave Moonhorn stands guard where the northern plains meet the canyonlands. His primary role is keeping watchful eyes on regional threats moving through the canyon floor below, particularly the hostile centaur clans. Anyone looking to descend into the needles often crosses paths with him first, receiving crucial warnings before they step onto the massive platforms of the Great Lift.",sp=0},{t="Uneasy Shadows",b="Beyond the constant threat of roving centaur, Moonhorn harbors deep misgivings about his fellow tauren from the Grimtotem tribe. He cautions traveling Horde allies to keep their distance from them, noting their increasingly erratic and suspicious behavior around Thousand Needles. To ensure the defense of the region, he dispatches couriers to Freewind Post to deliver warnings to Cliffwatcher Longhorn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brave Moonhorn?",a="Brave Moonhorn is a tauren warrior and scout tasked with watching the approach to the Great Lift connecting the Barrens to Thousand Needles. He monitors enemy activity and warns passing travelers of nearby hazards.",al={"brave moonhorn role","who is moonhorn","lift tauren guard"}},{q="Why does Moonhorn warn against the Grimtotem?",a="Moonhorn has noticed the Grimtotem clan acting strange and unpredictable in the surrounding canyon. While nominally part of the tauren community, their aggressive insularity makes them untrustworthy to guards keeping order along the trail.",al={"grimtotem warning","why avoid grimtotem","moonhorn grimtotem"}},{q="What message does he want delivered to Freewind Post?",a="He carries urgent warnings regarding escalating centaur activity in Thousand Needles and asks dependable Horde runners to relay this intelligence to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post.",al={"freewind post message","what is moonhorn's message","message to freewind post lore"}},{q="Where is Brave Moonhorn located?",a="He stands near the edge of the plateau at the top of the Great Lift, right along the boundary separating the Southern Barrens from Thousand Needles.",al={"where is moonhorn","brave moonhorn location","great lift guard"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Moonhorn serves as an early sentry for the Horde, directing new arrivals in the canyon toward safety and the fortified heights of Freewind Post.",["race:Tauren"]="Moonhorn's deep wariness of the Grimtotem reflects the simmering friction and distrust between traditional tribes loyal to Cairne Bloodhoof and the secretive Grimtotem clan."},kw={"brave moonhorn","centaur","cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","great lift","grimtotem","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:4542","subzone:great-lift","subzone:freewind-post","npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","zone:thousandneedles","topic:grimtotem-tribe","topic:centaur","topic:tauren"},src={"Brave Moonhorn"}}
E["npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn"] = {t="npc",n="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",z="thousandneedles",s="Cliffwatcher Longhorn is the stoic tauren leader stationed high atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Tasked with safeguarding the isolated Horde outpost, he coordinates defenses against encroaching Galak centaur and monitors the suspicious machinations of the Grimtotem tribe.",h="Cliffwatcher Longhorn is the stoic tauren leader stationed high atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Mesas",b="Perched upon the soaring rock spires of Thousand Needles, Freewind Post relies on sharp eyes and steady leadership to survive. Cliffwatcher Longhorn oversees the day-to-day security of this precarious settlement. With hostile forces gathering on the canyon floor below and along neighboring ridges, Longhorn acts as the settlement's primary coordinator for scouting reports and defensive military efforts.",sp=0},{t="Centaur Hostility and Grimtotem Intrigue",b="Longhorn contends with threats on multiple fronts. Down in the canyon, the aggressive Galak centaur relentlessly probe the perimeter, prompting him to dispatch adventurers to push them back and curb their numbers. Even more troubling to him, however, are the Grimtotem tauren. Deeply distrustful of their secretive camp near the post, Longhorn arranges reconnaissance to seize their hidden notes, uncovering troubling evidence of internal treachery, including the violent crimes of Arnak Grimtotem.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cliffwatcher Longhorn?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn is the tauren authority figure in command of Freewind Post, the Horde's towering outpost in Thousand Needles. He organizes scouts, defense patrols, and responses to local threats.",al={"cliffwatcher longhorn info","who is longhorn","freewind post leader"}},{q="Where can I find Cliffwatcher Longhorn?",a="He is located atop the main mesa of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, accessible by taking the lift up from the canyon floor and crossing the wooden bridges.",al={"cliffwatcher longhorn location","where is longhorn"}},{q="Why is Longhorn concerned about the centaur?",a="Reports brought in by scouts like Brave Moonhorn show an alarming surge in Galak centaur hostility. Longhorn orders proactive strikes to pacify the clan and prevent them from overwhelming the outpost's approaches.",al={"why kill centaur","pacify the centaur lore","centaur threat thousand needles"}},{q="What is his interest in the Grimtotem tribe?",a="While technically living among the Horde, the Grimtotem clan behaves with open secrecy and malice. Longhorn suspects foul play and commissions adventurers to steal their hidden notes to discover what they are plotting.",al={"longhorn grimtotem","grimtotem spying reason"}},{q="Who is Arnak Grimtotem and why does Longhorn want him?",a="Arnak Grimtotem carried out a violent attack against the post's inhabitants. Longhorn issues a bounty on his head to ensure Arnak faces justice for his treachery.",al={"wanted arnak grimtotem","arnak bounty lore"}},{q="Does Cliffwatcher Longhorn have any family?",a="Yes, his brother Nataka Longhorn is stationed far to the west at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace. Preoccupied with duty, Cliffwatcher rarely finds the opportunity to write him.",al={"longhorn brother","nataka longhorn brother"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, Longhorn represents the frontier spirit of the Shu'halo, keeping watch over contested sacred mesas while navigating the bitter, unresolved friction with the Grimtotem tribe.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post is the vital link securing supply lines across southern Kalimdor, and Longhorn ensures the Horde retains its precarious foothold amidst hostile centaur territory."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","brave moonhorn","cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","galak","grimtotem","nataka longhorn","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","npc:brave-moonhorn","quest:4542","quest:4841","quest:5064","quest:5147","zone:desolace"},src={"Cliffwatcher Longhorn"}}
E["npc:dorn-plainstalker"] = {t="npc",n="Dorn Plainstalker",z="thousandneedles",s="Dorn Plainstalker is a solitary tauren elder residing in the Weathered Nook overlooking the canyons of Thousand Needles. He serves as an overseer of traditional rite of passage trials, challenging Horde adventurers to prove their character and fortitude. Through trials of faith, endurance, strength, and lore, he tests whether travelers are worthy servants of the Earth Mother and their people.",h="Dorn Plainstalker is a solitary tauren elder residing in the Weathered Nook overlooking the canyons of...",sec={{t="Hermit of the High Cliffs",b="Secluded in a shallow cave high atop the canyon ridges of the Weathered Nook, Dorn Plainstalker lives apart from the bustle of Freewind Post. Reaching his mountain redoubt requires winding along the sheer northern cliffs overlooking the towering mesas below. From this quiet vantage point, Dorn maintains ancient customs and judges those who seek guidance in the harsh southern barrens.",sp=0},{t="The Four Trials",b="Dorn Plainstalker guides pilgrims through a demanding series of tests meant to measure the core virtues of a tauren champion: faith, endurance, strength, and lore. Rather than mere exercises in brute force, these trials force aspirants to confront fear, leap blindly into the unknown, outlast cunning wilderness predators, and ponder the sacred history of Kalimdor before claiming their final passage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dorn Plainstalker?",a="Dorn Plainstalker is a tauren hermit and elder who dwells in the Weathered Nook, a secluded cliffside shelter high above Thousand Needles. He administers traditional trials of passage to aspiring Horde champions.",al={"who is dorn","dorn lore","dorn plainstalker"}},{q="Where can I find Dorn Plainstalker?",a="He is located in a cave at the Weathered Nook. From Freewind Post, head north to the high cliff walls bordering the canyon, then follow the ridge east until you discover a ramp ascending into his mountain sanctuary.",al={"where is dorn","how to reach dorn plainstalker","weathered nook location"}},{q="What are the trials Dorn administers?",a="Dorn oversees four sacred tests: the Test of Faith, Test of Endurance, Test of Strength, and Test of Lore. Completing them proves a traveler's courage, physical resolve, combat skill, and respect for tradition.",al={"dorn plainstalker quests","test of faith","trials of passage thousand needles"}},{q="What is the Test of Faith?",a="The Test of Faith requires the pilgrim to step off a dizzying cliff plank into the chasm below, demonstrating absolute trust and overcoming primal fear.",al={"leap of faith thousand needles","test of faith dorn"}},{q="Why does Dorn live alone in a cave?",a="Dorn adheres to ascetic tauren spiritual traditions. By dwelling alone in the heights of the Weathered Nook, away from the daily trade and defense of Freewind Post, he maintains an untroubled place of contemplation and trial for seekers.",al={"why is dorn isolated","dorn plainstalker background"}},{q="Is Dorn affiliated with Freewind Post?",a="While he lives outside Freewind Post itself, Dorn is a loyal member of the Horde and the tauren tribes, assisting brave travelers who wander through the windswept canyons.",al={"freewind post elder","is dorn horde"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren wandering through Thousand Needles, Dorn represents the continuation of nomadic ancestral traditions and spiritual rites that test one's balance with the Earth Mother.",["faction:Horde"]="Dorn welcomes all Horde champions willing to brave his trials, ensuring that warriors, hunters, and shamans of every race prove their mettle in Kalimdor's rugged wilds."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","freewind post","tauren trial","test of endurance","test of faith","test of lore","test of strength","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"subzone:weathered-nook","quest:1149","quest:1150","quest:1151","quest:1152","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren"},src={"Dorn Plainstalker"}}
E["npc:elder-morningdew"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Morningdew",z="thousandneedles",s="Elder Morningdew is an ancient night elf spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival in Thousand Needles. She offers wisdom and ancestral blessings to travelers who seek her out amid the arid canyons and dried salt flats of the Shimmering Flats.",h="Elder Morningdew is an ancient night elf spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="An Honored Spirit of the Festival",b="Throughout the Lunar Festival, the spirits of revered night elf and tauren ancestors manifest across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms to celebrate wisdom, legacy, and peace. Elder Morningdew is one such apparition, visiting Thousand Needles to greet honoring pilgrims. Bound by neither faction nor mortal conflict, she bestows her coin of ancestry upon any adventurer respectful enough to seek her counsel and receive her blessing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Morningdew?",a="Elder Morningdew is a night elf ancestral spirit who manifests during the annual Lunar Festival. She waits in Thousand Needles to be honored by travelers from both the Alliance and the Horde.",al={"elder morningdew lore","who is morningdew","morningdew identity"}},{q="What is the purpose of seeking her out?",a="Adventurers seek her out during the Lunar Festival to pay their respects to the ancestors, receiving a Coin of Ancestry and a blessing of wisdom in exchange for honoring her spirit.",al={"why find elder morningdew","morningdew purpose","lunar festival elder"}},{q="Does she belong to the Alliance or Horde?",a="Like all Lunar Festival elders, Elder Morningdew stands neutral to mortal politics. Both Alliance and Horde adventurers can approach her peacefully to pay their respects.",al={"is morningdew hostile","elder morningdew faction","can horde talk to morningdew"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, seeking out ancient elders like Morningdew is a sacred duty of reverence, connecting modern night elves with the honored spirits who came before them.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren honor ancestral spirits deeply, making encounters with elders across Kalimdor a natural extension of their cultural reverence for past wisdom."},kw={"ancestor","elder","elder morningdew","ghost","lunar festival","morningdew","night elf","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:8724","zone:thousandneedles","topic:night-elf"},src={"Elder Morningdew"}}
E["npc:elder-skyseer"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Skyseer",z="thousandneedles",s="Elder Skyseer is the spirit of an ancestral tauren residing atop the towering bluffs of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. As an honoured elder returned from the spirit world, he observes the ongoing journeys of the Horde and remains deeply tied to the resting grounds of his people.",h="Elder Skyseer is the spirit of an ancestral tauren residing atop the towering bluffs of Freewind Post in...",sec={{t="A Spirit of Freewind Post",b="Perched high above the salt canyons of Thousand Needles, Elder Skyseer lingers at the windswept mesa settlement of Freewind Post. While the Grimtotem and bloodhoof tauren bustle around the outpost's perilous bridges and wooden platforms, Skyseer watches over the realm as an ancestor who has crossed beyond the mortal veil. He serves as an ancestral beacon for travelers seeking the wisdom of past generations, offering his blessings to those who honor old traditions.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Ancestral Lands",b="Though his spirit commonly manifests among the wind-carved needles, Skyseer's roots are bound to the sacred soil of Mulgore. His presence is tied to Red Rocks, the ancient burial grounds of the tauren people where great leaders and fallen chieftains are interred. Spirits like Skyseer reveal how thin the veil between the physical realm and the ancestral spirits remains for the tauren, guiding future generations through remembrance and ritual.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Skyseer?",a="Elder Skyseer is an ancestral tauren spirit who appears at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. He is one of the revered elders whose spirits watch over modern travelers, offering ancestral guidance to those who seek him out.",al={"elder skyseer lore","who is skyseer","skyseer npc"}},{q="Why is Elder Skyseer a ghost?",a="He is an ancient ancestor who has passed on from the mortal world. Tauren culture maintains a deep spiritual connection to their forebears, and certain prominent elders linger or return in spirit form to guide the living.",al={"why is skyseer dead","is elder skyseer dead","ghost tauren freewind"}},{q="What is his connection to Mulgore?",a="Skyseer's spirit is also tied to Red Rocks in Mulgore, the sacred ancestral burial grounds of the tauren. He appears there in reverence to the fallen chieftains and traditions of the tribes.",al={"skyseer red rocks","skyseer mulgore connection"}},{q="Where can I find Elder Skyseer?",a="Elder Skyseer is located at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, lingering atop the fortified mesa settlement high above the canyon floor.",al={"elder skyseer location","find skyseer","where is skyseer"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren, encountering Elder Skyseer is a direct communion with an ancestor, embodying the spiritual reverence taught at Red Rocks and across the plains of Mulgore.",["class:Shaman"]="As spiritual mediators who speak to the elements and spirits, shamans recognize in Elder Skyseer the enduring wisdom of ancestors who continue to watch over the living."},kw={"ancestor","elder skyseer","freewind post","red rocks","tauren ghost","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:red-rocks","zone:mulgore","topic:tauren","quest:8682"},src={"Elder Skyseer"}}
E["npc:elu"] = {t="npc",n="Elu",z="thousandneedles",s="Elu is an apprentice wind rider stationed atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Eager to begin his formal training and take to the skies, he tasks Horde travelers with retrieving wild wyvern eggs from nearby roosts.",h="Elu is an apprentice wind rider stationed atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="An Eager Apprentice",b="Perched high above the salt flats and canyon floor at Freewind Post, Elu spends his days tending to the settlement's aerial mounts while dreaming of his own flight. As a young tauren apprentice, he longs to join the ranks of the master wind riders who patrol the towering mesas of Kalimdor. Before he can begin true flight training, however, he must prove his capability by supplying the roost with fresh wyvern stock, sending capable adventurers to harvest intact eggs from the fierce wild wyverns nesting at Highperch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elu?",a="Elu is a tauren wind rider apprentice stationed at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, responsible for helping secure and raise new mounts for the Horde's aerial network.",al={"elu freewind post","who is elu","tauren apprentice elu"}},{q="Why does Elu need wyvern eggs?",a="Elu is tasked with replenishing the stable of wyverns for the master wind riders. Raising the beasts from freshly collected eggs ensures they can be properly trained and bonded as trusted mounts for the Horde.",al={"why wyvern eggs","elu wyvern quest","elu quest goal"}},{q="Where does Elu send adventurers to find eggs?",a="He directs adventurers to Highperch, a dangerous mesa in western Thousand Needles where colonies of wild wyverns fiercely guard their nests.",al={"where are wyvern eggs","where is highperch","elu egg location"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren adventurers, assisting Elu supports a fellow tribesman striving to master the ancient and vital art of wyvern handling high above their ancestral canyon lands.",["faction:Horde"]="Gathering wyvern eggs for Elu directly strengthens the Horde's courier and transport network, keeping remote outposts across Kalimdor connected by air."},kw={"elu","freewind post","highperch","thousand needles","wind rider","wyvern","wyvern eggs"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","quest:4767","subzone:highperch","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Elu"}}
E["npc:fizzle-brassbolts"] = {t="npc",n="Fizzle Brassbolts",z="thousandneedles",s="Fizzle Brassbolts is a prominent gnomish engineer stationed out on the baked salt flats of the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles. Alongside his rival, the goblin Pozzik, Fizzle co-founded the raceway to pit gnomish precision engineering against reckless goblin ingenuity in high-speed rocket car races. He constantly seeks parts, fuel, and strange desert reagents to keep his racing team running.",h="Fizzle Brassbolts is a prominent gnomish engineer stationed out on the baked salt flats of the Mirage Raceway...",sec={{t="A Matter of Principle and Pistons",b="Out in the shimmering heat of the Shimmering Flats, political alliances and ancient grudges yield to the roar of motorized engines. Fizzle Brassbolts arrived here with one goal in mind: proving once and for all that gnomish craftsmanship is vastly superior to crude goblin tinkering. Together with his goblin counterpart Pozzik, he helped lay out the Mirage Raceway, bringing race cars, pit crews, and spectators to an otherwise desolate basin.",sp=0},{t="Tinkering on the Flats",b="Racing across dry salt beds at breakneck speeds requires constant improvisation. As an avid member of the Mechanical Engineers' Guild of Azeroth (MEGA), Fizzle does not shy away from unorthodox experiments. Whether testing volatile mixtures concocted from local creature venom or contracting travelers to fetch replacement mechanical parts, Fizzle is determined to keep his driver's wheels turning faster than any explosive goblin contraption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fizzle Brassbolts?",a="Fizzle Brassbolts is a master gnomish engineer and lead organizer for the Alliance racing crew stationed at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles.",al={"who is fizzle","fizzle brassbolts lore","gnome at raceway"}},{q="Why did Fizzle come to the Shimmering Flats?",a="He came to settle a technical debate with the goblin engineer Pozzik over whose race boasts superior engineering. Together, they established the Mirage Raceway to test their rocket cars head-to-head on the flat salt basin.",al={"why is fizzle here","raceway purpose","why raceway built"}},{q="What is MEGA?",a="MEGA stands for the Mechanical Engineers' Guild of Azeroth. Fizzle is a dedicated member, representing the guild's commitment to meticulous design and technical refinement.",al={"fizzle guild","mechanical engineers guild","what is mega"}},{q="Why does Fizzle need creature venom for race cars?",a="Fizzle experiments constantly with local reagents to formulate powerful engine fluids, additives, and accelerants capable of giving his rocket cars an edge over Pozzik's machines.",al={"salt flat venom quest","venom racing fuel","why does he need venom"}},{q="Does Fizzle fight against the goblins?",a="Not with weapons. While deep professional jealousy exists between them, Fizzle and Pozzik maintain an uneasy, neutral truce at the raceway to focus purely on high-speed competition.",al={"is fizzle hostile to goblins","fizzle pozzik fight"}},{q="Who is Pilot Longbeard?",a="Pilot Longbeard is a dwarven aviator and personal friend of the Brassbolts family who shares a fondness for dangerous machinery and desert tracks.",al={"pilot longbeard connection","fizzle pilot friend"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Fizzle carries the honor of all Gnomeregan into the desert, dead-set on proving gnomish precision outperforms goblin recklessness.",["profession:Engineering"]="Fellow engineers will appreciate Fizzle's dedication to optimizing rocket propulsion and drafting cutting-edge automotive designs under harsh desert conditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though operating in a neutral speed zone, Fizzle provides a friendly face and mechanical work for Alliance wanderers passing south toward Tanaris."},kw={"brassbolts","fizzle","mega","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","npc:pozzik","quest:1104","zone:thousandneedles","npc:pilot-longbeard","topic:gnome","topic:goblin","zone:tanaris"},src={"Fizzle Brassbolts"}}
E["npc:hagar-lightninghoof"] = {t="npc",n="Hagar Lightninghoof",z="thousandneedles",s="Hagar Lightninghoof is a tauren scout stationed high atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Driven by rumors of a strange clutch hidden in the canyon depths, he investigates reports of an alien egg guarded fiercely by local wind serpents.",h="Hagar Lightninghoof is a tauren scout stationed high atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="The Strange Clutch",b="While stationed among the towering bluffs of Freewind Post, Hagar Lightninghoof caught wind of rumors regarding an unnatural egg nestled deep inside a cavern below. The local wind serpents guarded the nest with unusual ferocity, keeping curious scouts at bay. Seeking an adventurer bold enough to braze the serpents' den, Hagar hopes to study the specimen firsthand and discern what manner of beast could warrant such defensive instincts from the canyon's natural predators.",sp=0},{t="A Myth Hatched",b="When an adventurer finally recovers the egg and brings it to Freewind Post, it hatches directly in front of Hagar, revealing a young wind serpent resembling the legendary Arikara—a revered spirit known in tauren folklore as the embodiment of vengeance. Realizing the grave cultural and spiritual significance of the creature's return, Hagar wastes no time dispatching the traveler to consult with the elder Motega Firemane.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Hagar Lightninghoof?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof is a tauren quest giver residing at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. He investigates anomalous wildlife in the canyons, particularly an unusual wind serpent egg reported deep within a nearby cavern.",al={"who is hagar","hagar lightninghoof role","hagar lore"}},{q="Where can Hagar Lightninghoof be found?",a="He is located atop Freewind Post, the central Horde outpost perched upon the massive rock needles of central Thousand Needles.",al={"where is hagar","hagar lightninghoof location","freewind post hagar"}},{q="What is the 'alien egg' Hagar is looking for?",a="The alien egg is an unusual clutch guarded by wind serpents in a subterranean den. Upon being delivered to Hagar, it immediately hatches into Young Arikara, revealing it to be the brood of a legendary wind serpent.",al={"alien egg","what is the egg","wind serpent egg"},sp=1},{q="Who does Hagar send you to after the egg hatches?",a="Recognizing the hatchling as Arikara from tauren legend, Hagar sends the adventurer to speak with Motega Firemane, an elder at Freewind Post who possesses deeper wisdom regarding the spirit of vengeance.",al={"who do i turn serpent wild into","hagar follow up quest","where to go after hagar"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, assisting Hagar leads to the stirring realization that ancient legends of Arikara, the winged manifestation of vengeance, are living reality in the canyons below.",["faction:Horde"]="Stationed high above the canyon floor at Freewind Post, Hagar relies on capable Horde warriors to brave perilous dens that normal scouts cannot safely breach."},kw={"alien egg","arikara","freewind post","hagar","lightninghoof","motega firemane","thousand needles","wind serpent"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","quest:4821","quest:4865","npc:motega-firemane","quest:5088","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Hagar Lightninghoof"}}
E["npc:kanati-greycloud"] = {t="npc",n="Kanati Greycloud",z="thousandneedles",s="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren hunter stationed at Whitereach Post within Thousand Needles. Alongside his hunting companions, he musters what defense he can while enduring constant hostility from the local Galak centaur.",h="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren hunter stationed at Whitereach Post within Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Precarious Perch",b="Kanati Greycloud makes his camp at Whitereach Post, high atop the sandstone spires of western Thousand Needles. While the canyon offers abundant game and open vistas, it is hemmed in by the Galak centaur, whose warbands contest every inch of the arid flats below. Together with other tauren hunters, Kanati keeps watch over the canyon floor, striving to preserve the post against the brutal depredations of the surrounding marauders.",sp=0},{t="Centaur Ambush",b="The Galak centaur do not merely seek to isolate Whitereach Post; they intend to annihilate its defenders outright. Messengers sent between centaur camps carry explicit orders targeting Kanati and his companions for assassination. It falls to visiting travelers to intercept these marching orders and stand shoulder-to-shoulder with Kanati when the Galak raiding parties descend upon the mesa to cut down the outpost's hunters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kanati Greycloud?",a="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren hunter based at Whitereach Post in western Thousand Needles, where he maintains a camp and defends against predatory local threats.",al={"who is kanati","kanati greycloud lore","whitereach post tauren"}},{q="Where can I find Kanati Greycloud?",a="Kanati is located at Whitereach Post, an elevated tauren encampment situated along the northern bluffs in the western portion of Thousand Needles.",al={"kanati location","where is kanati","where is greycloud"}},{q="Why are the Galak centaur trying to kill him?",a="The Galak centaur seek total dominance over the canyons of Thousand Needles and actively target Horde outposts. Intercepted orders reveal a coordinated plot by the centaur to assassinate Kanati and break the post's defenses.",al={"why centaur attack kanati","galak assassination plot","protect kanati why"}},{q="Is Kanati related to other Greyclouds?",a="He shares his surname with Tor Greycloud and Kar Greycloud, two tauren found elsewhere in the Kalimdor wilderness, though the exact familial bond between them is not detailed.",al={"greycloud family","tor greycloud relative","kar greycloud"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren traversing Thousand Needles, aiding Kanati at Whitereach Post is a vital defense of tribal kin against their ancient, bitter enemies, the centaur.",["faction:Horde"]="Whitereach Post serves as a critical vantage point over the needle canyons; keeping Kanati alive ensures Horde scouts retain eyes on centaur troop movements."},kw={"assassination plot","centaur","galak","greycloud","kanati","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","quest:4881","topic:centaur","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Kanati Greycloud"}}
E["npc:kravel-koalbeard"] = {t="npc",n="Kravel Koalbeard",z="thousandneedles",s="Kravel Koalbeard is a scheming dwarven entrepreneur and con artist stationed out at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. Rather than cheering purely for the love of the sport, he views the fierce gnome and goblin racing rivalry as a golden opportunity to fill his pockets. From scavenging stray machine parts to fixing race results through blackmail and booze, Kravel is always hunting for his next profitable scheme.",h="Kravel Koalbeard is a scheming dwarven entrepreneur and con artist stationed out at the Mirage Raceway in the...",sec={{t="A Con Artist in the Flats",b="While most spectators and crew members at the Mirage Raceway are consumed by mechanical rivalries and the roar of rocket engines, Kravel Koalbeard has his eyes squarely on everyone's coin purses. He is an opportunist who operates in the dusty cracks of the raceway encampment, quick to offer contracts and favors that rarely have clean motives. Kravel sees the high-stakes friction between gnome and goblin engineers not as an inspiring competition, but as a fertile ground for extortion, sabotage, and theft.",sp=0},{t="Rigging the Track",b="Kravel's operations stretch far beyond picking up discarded salvage on the salt flats. To manipulate odds and ensure outcomes tip his way, Kravel is known to send willing adventurers on illicit errands—peddling rumors, running blackmail schemes, and even inebriating pit crews right before a showdown. Whether plying goblin mechanics with potent spirits or slipping strong drinks to gnomish pilots, Kravel will stoop to whatever underhanded trick is necessary to line his pockets on race day.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kravel Koalbeard?",a="Kravel Koalbeard is a dwarf schemer and opportunist stationed at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. He uses the rivalry between gnomes and goblins to line his pockets through salvage, race-fixing, and extortion.",al={"who is kravel","kravel koalbeard identity","mirage raceway dwarf"}},{q="What does Kravel Koalbeard do at the Mirage Raceway?",a="Kravel hires travelers to run underhanded errands around the track. His schemes include collecting scavenged rocket car parts, digging up blackmail material, and sabotaging racing teams by getting their mechanics and pilots drunk to sway race outcomes.",al={"kravel purpose","what does kravel want","kravel schemes"}},{q="Why is Kravel trying to get race crews drunk?",a="Kravel wagers heavily on the outcome of the rocket car races. By getting either the gnomes or the goblins intoxicated before race time, he rigs the contest to favor whatever outcome makes him the most profit.",al={"get the gnomes drunk quest","get the goblins drunk","kravel sabotage"}},{q="Where can Kravel Koalbeard be found?",a="He is located in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles, lingering right around the bustling pit camps of the Mirage Raceway.",al={"kravel location","where is kravel","kravel thousand needles"}},{q="Does Kravel have ties outside Thousand Needles?",a="Yes. His shady dealings involve contacts in the goblin port of Booty Bay, including dealings tied to Wharfmaster Dizzywig, rumormongers, and exotic brews from Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"kravel booty bay","kravel connections"}},{q="Will Kravel work with both Alliance and Horde?",a="Like many figures operating in neutral venues like the Mirage Raceway, Kravel is interested in gold rather than faction loyalties. He will happily employ both Alliance and Horde adventurers to carry out his schemes.",al={"is kravel alliance only","can horde talk to kravel"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Unlike the honest miners, prospectors, and mountaineers of Ironforge, Kravel is an unabashed rogue and swindler who embarrasses traditional dwarven values.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes should keep a close eye on their drinks and blueprints around Kravel, who is just as eager to drug gnomish pilots as he is to sabotage their machines.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues will find Kravel's line of work familiar: theft, sabotage, blackmail, and manipulating greedy targets from the shadows."},kw={"blackmail","koalbeard","kravel","mirage raceway","rocket car","sabotage","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1110","quest:1492","subzone:booty-bay","topic:dwarf","topic:gnome","topic:goblin"},src={"Kravel Koalbeard"}}
E["npc:lakota-windsong"] = {t="npc",n="Lakota Windsong",z="thousandneedles",s="Lakota Windsong is a young tauren held captive atop the bluffs of Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles. After rejecting an unwanted proposal from Arnak Grimtotem, she was abducted by force and awaits rescue from the Grimtotem tribe's clutches.",h="Lakota Windsong is a young tauren held captive atop the bluffs of Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Deadly Courtship",b="Not long after the Third War, Lakota Windsong was pursued by Arnak Grimtotem. Unwilling to join his clan or accept his courtship, she turned down his proposal. Arnak refused to take no for an answer; he returned under cover of night, slaughtered Lakota's brother when he tried to intervene, and carried her off into the jagged heights of Thousand Needles. Confined high above the canyon floor at Darkcloud Pinnacle, she remains trapped under heavy guard while Arnak still insists on making her his bride.",sp=0},{t="Descent to Safety",b="Surrounded by treacherous Grimtotem bandits, Lakota cannot fight her way down the cliffs alone. Only a brave escort can lead her across the suspension bridges and down the winding paths to the canyon basin below. Once she breaks free of Darkcloud Pinnacle, Lakota flees toward the safety of Freewind Post, carrying word of her rescue to Thalia Amberhide and the defenders stationed there.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Lakota Windsong being held at Darkcloud Pinnacle?",a="She refused a marriage proposal from Arnak Grimtotem. Rather than accept her refusal, Arnak murdered her brother and abducted Lakota, dragging her to the Grimtotem stronghold at Darkcloud Pinnacle in hopes of forcing her hand.",al={"why is lakota captured","who kidnapped lakota","why is lakota in darkcloud pinnacle"}},{q="Where does Lakota go once she is rescued?",a="After reaching the base of Darkcloud Pinnacle safely, Lakota makes her way to Freewind Post, where she can find refuge among the Horde defenders and report her ordeal to Thalia Amberhide.",al={"where does lakota run","where does she go after escort","lakota destination"},sp=1},{q="Who is Arnak Grimtotem?",a="Arnak is a violent warrior of the treacherous Grimtotem clan who murdered Lakota's brother and abducted her when she declined to marry him.",al={"who is arnak","who kidnapped her","arnak lore"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Lakota's ordeal is a stark reminder of the treachery festering among the Grimtotem, whose defiance of Cairne Bloodhoof's leadership regularly turns violent.",["faction:Horde"]="Rescuing Lakota strikes a blow against Grimtotem dominance over Thousand Needles and secures safe passage for travelers resting at Freewind Post."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","darkcloud pinnacle","free at last","freewind post","lakota windsong","thalia amberhide","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:4904","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","npc:thalia-amberhide","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Lakota Windsong"}}
E["npc:mad-magus-tirth"] = {t="npc",n="Mad Magus Tirth",z="thousandneedles",s="Magus Tirth is an eccentric human wizard dwelling out on the salt flats of the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles. Known locally for breeding chickens and tormenting his polymorphed apprentice, he is also a scholar of formidable arcane lore who has squandered valuable tomes on racing bets.",h="Magus Tirth is an eccentric human wizard dwelling out on the salt flats of the Mirage Raceway in Thousand...",sec={{t="A Wizard in the Dust",b="While most mages of his caliber study in the libraries of Dalaran or Stormwind, Magus Tirth has taken up residence amid the grease and roar of the Shimmering Flats. Surrounded by speeding rocket cars, Tirth peddles chickens to passersby and spends his days barking orders at 'Plucky' Johnson, his unfortunate former apprentice whom he keeps trapped in poultry form. Despite this eccentric demeanor, Tirth possesses genuine arcane mastery, having authored esoteric texts on magical power before losing them to reckless wagers on the speedway.",sp=0},{t="Rituals and Debts",b="Tirth's scholarly legacy includes 'Rituals of Power', an arcane manual sought after by practicing mages. Unfortunately for aspiring spellcasters, Tirth no longer owns his own masterwork. Crushed under gambling debts accrued at the Mirage Raceway, the mage sold the tome to an agent of the Scarlet Crusade to square his losses, forcing apprentices and seekers of knowledge to track the book down into hostile territory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Magus Tirth out in the desert?",a="Tirth lives on the Shimmering Flats beside the Mirage Raceway, drawn by the spectacle and the gambling. Rather than pursuing scholarly life in a major city, he watches the gnome and goblin racers, sells chickens, and indulges his vices.",al={"why is tirth here","magus tirth shimmering flats","tirth location"}},{q="Who is the chicken next to him?",a="The chicken is 'Plucky' Johnson, Magus Tirth's former apprentice. Tirth magically polymorphed Johnson into a chicken and spends much of his time tormenting him, commanding him to dance out on the salt flats.",al={"who is plucky","plucky johnson","tirth chicken apprentice"}},{q="What is the book Rituals of Power?",a="Rituals of Power is an advanced treatise on arcane energy authored by Magus Tirth. It is an essential text for mages looking to advance their craft, though Tirth parted with it to pay off his mounting racing debts.",al={"rituals of power","tirth book","mage quest book"}},{q="Who did Tirth sell his book to?",a="To settle gambling losses accumulated at the Mirage Raceway, Tirth sold his copy of Rituals of Power to a member of the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"who has rituals of power","tirth debts","scarlet crusade book"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Tirth is an important figure for mages seeking to deepen their understanding of arcane power, as he authored the vital treatise 'Rituals of Power'."},kw={"ancona chicken","magus tirth","mirage raceway","plucky","plucky johnson","rituals of power","shimmering flats","thousand needles","tirth"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1950","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Mad Magus Tirth"}}
E["npc:magistrix-elosai"] = {t="npc",n="Magistrix Elosai",z="thousandneedles",s="Magistrix Elosai is a blood elf researcher staying at Freewind Post in the jagged canyons of Thousand Needles. Having been exiled by her peers, she dedicates her solitude to brewing a remedy for her people's devastating addiction to magic.",h="Magistrix Elosai is a blood elf researcher staying at Freewind Post in the jagged canyons of Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="An Exile's Cure",b="Perched upon the high mesas of Freewind Post, Magistrix Elosai works far from the remnants of her homeland. Exiled for pursuing an unorthodox solution to the magical hunger consuming the blood elves, she seeks to craft a tonic capable of breaking their reliance on arcane energy. Her lonely experiments in Kalimdor reflect the desperate lengths to which individual sin'dorei will go to master the addiction born from the loss of the Sunwell.",sp=0},{t="A Tragic Miscalculation",b="Elosai's search for salvation ends in personal disaster. When she finally tests her refined concoction, the brew does not cleanse her arcane craving; instead, it rapidly accelerates the affliction. Consumed by the uncontrolled magical degeneration, Elosai transforms into a withered Wretched, devastated by the realization that her years of research have failed and wondering if her people's curse can ever truly be overcome.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Magistrix Elosai?",a="Magistrix Elosai is a blood elf researcher residing on the eastern edge of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. She was cast out by her fellows for attempting to invent a cure for the blood elves' addiction to magic.",al={"elosai","magistrix elosai lore","who is the elf in freewind post"}},{q="Why is a blood elf in Thousand Needles?",a="Elosai was exiled from blood elf society due to her obsession with finding an alternative cure for their magical withdrawal. She relocated to the remote Horde outpost of Freewind Post to pursue her alchemical research in peace.",al={"why is elosai here","why freewind post","elosai exile"}},{q="What happens when she tests her tonic?",a="Rather than satisfying or neutralizing her addiction, Elosai's experimental tonic dramatically accelerates it. The mixture overwhelms her system, transforming her into a degraded Wretched.",al={"what happens to elosai","elosai test","testing the tonic result"},sp=1},{q="What is a Wretched?",a="A Wretched is a blood elf who has succumbed to magical obsession and lost control of their addiction. Consuming reckless amounts of raw arcane power deforms their minds and bodies, leaving them frail, feral, and desperate for magic.",al={"what are the wretched","wretched elf","wretched blood elf"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Mages familiar with the volatile nature of arcane withdrawal will recognize the grim tragedy in Elosai's failed attempt to artificially dampen mana dependency.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post grants shelter to strange visitors, but Elosai's tragic fate demonstrates the deep perils that blood elves carry with them even when welcomed by Horde outposts."},kw={"blood elf","elosai","freewind post","magic addiction","magistrix","thousand needles","tonic","wretched"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","quest:9431","quest:9434"},src={"Magistrix Elosai"}}
E["npc:motega-firemane"] = {t="npc",n="Motega Firemane",z="thousandneedles",s="Motega Firemane is a tauren scholar stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. Dedicated to cataloging the dangerous wildlife of the canyon, he finds his studies disrupted by a vengeful wind serpent spirit and the reckless misadventures of his young assistant.",h="Motega Firemane is a tauren scholar stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="Scholar of the Canyons",b="Four years following the Third War, Motega Firemane journeyed south into Thousand Needles to observe and record the distinct beasts surviving among the towering mesas. Accompanied by his youthful assistant, Pao'ka Swiftmountain—whose protective father was reluctant to let him leave Mulgore—Motega set up camp alongside Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post. While his original calling was quiet natural observation, the harsh perils of the canyon floor continually demand a more martial approach to survival.",sp=0},{t="The Wrath of Arikara",b="Motega's peaceful research was upended when word arrived from Freewind Post that Arikara, a ferocious and legendary winged serpent spirit, had returned to the canyons seeking vengeance against Cairne Bloodhoof. Perplexed by why such a creature held a vendetta against the High Chieftain, Motega acted swiftly to protect the Horde. He instructed scouts to gather Incendia agave from the canyon basin and carry it to Elder Magatha Grimtotem in Thunder Bluff to be enchanted into a sacred powder. Using this preparation, hunters summoned and slew the serpent spirit, returning its hide to Whitereach Post as proof that Cairne was safe.",sp=1},{t="Guardian of Whitereach",b="Arikara was not the only hazard challenging Motega's stay at Whitereach Post. Local Galak centaur continuously probed the camp, even scheming an assassination plot against Kanati Greycloud and his followers. To worsen matters, young Pao'ka wandered away from the safety of the campfire and vanished into the wyvern-infested heights of Highperch. Though frustrated by the young brave's thoughtlessness, Motega was immensely relieved when Horde travelers escorted the youth back alive.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Motega Firemane?",a="Motega Firemane is a tauren researcher stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. He came to the canyons to study the local wildlife alongside fellow braves and his assistant, Pao'ka Swiftmountain.",al={"motega firemane lore","who is motega","whitereach motega"}},{q="Where can Motega Firemane be found?",a="He is located at Whitereach Post, a small Horde campsite nestled along the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, situated north of the shimmering salt flats.",al={"motega location","where is motega firemane","motega firemane map"}},{q="Why is Motega concerned about Arikara?",a="Arikara is a vengeful serpent spirit that has manifested in Thousand Needles targeting Cairne Bloodhoof. Though baffled as to why the spirit bears a grudge against the High Chieftain, Motega takes the threat seriously and directs hunters to summon and eliminate the creature.",al={"who is arikara","why kill arikara","arikara cairne"},sp=1},{q="What role does Magatha Grimtotem play in Motega's plans?",a="Motega tasks adventurers with collecting Incendia agave and carrying it to Magatha Grimtotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Magatha uses her shamanic knowledge to enchant the plant into a sacred powder capable of summoning the elusive Arikara.",al={"magatha incendia powder","motega and magatha","sacred fire quest lore"},sp=1},{q="What happened to Motega's companion, Pao'ka?",a="Pao'ka Swiftmountain strayed into the dangerous wyvern roosts of Highperch and became lost. Motega was anxious over the youth's fate, especially given how reluctant Pao'ka's father had been to allow the journey, but travelers successfully escorted him back to Whitereach Post.",al={"pao'ka swiftmountain","missing tauren highperch","homeward bound quest"},sp=1},{q="What other dangers does Whitereach Post face?",a="Beyond rogue spirits and predators, the camp is actively targeted by the nearby Galak centaur, who orchestrate ambushes and plot assassinations against Kanati Greycloud and the other tauren stationed at the post.",al={"whitereach post threats","centaur at whitereach","galak centaur plot"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Motega represents the Horde's expansion into the untamed regions of Kalimdor, maintaining a tenuous research outpost while safeguarding High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof from spiritual threats.",["race:Tauren"]="Through his reverence for nature and dutiful devotion to Cairne Bloodhoof, Motega embodies the tauren ethos of studying the Earth Mother's creatures while defending the tribe against ancient spirits.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters find common ground with Motega, who relies on skilled trackers to harvest canyon flora, track wyverns in Highperch, and stalk the mighty spirit Arikara."},kw={"arikara","cairne bloodhoof","kanati greycloud","magatha grimtotem","motega firemane","pao'ka swiftmountain","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","npc:pao-ka-swiftmountain","npc:kanati-greycloud","npc:magatha-grimtotem","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","subzone:highperch","npc:hagar-lightninghoof"},src={"Motega Firemane"}}
E["npc:pao-ka-swiftmountain"] = {t="npc",n="Pao'ka Swiftmountain",z="thousandneedles",s="Pao'ka Swiftmountain is a young tauren naturalist stranded among the wild wyverns of Highperch in Thousand Needles. Having traveled south under the guidance of Motega Firemane, his youthful curiosity got the better of him when he ventured too close to a nesting site and ended up cornered in the cliffs.",h="Pao'ka Swiftmountain is a young tauren naturalist stranded among the wild wyverns of Highperch in Thousand...",sec={{t="A Naturalist in Trouble",b="Pao'ka came to the canyon country of Thousand Needles alongside Motega Firemane, eager to catalog and study the dangerous beasts of the canyons. His father had been reluctant to let his son go on such a perilous journey, and Pao'ka's recent misadventure proves those concerns were warranted. Fascinated by the magnificent wyverns inhabiting Highperch, the young scholar crept up the mountain trail behind a solitary tauren totem. Unsurprisingly, the territorial beasts took offense to his intrusion, driving him deep into the crags where he found himself trapped and terrified, unable to slip past the swooping predators to return to Whitereach Post.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pao'ka Swiftmountain?",a="Pao'ka is a young tauren scholar who accompanied Motega Firemane to Thousand Needles to study regional wildlife, only to become trapped by territorial wyverns on Highperch.",al={"who is pao'ka","paoka swiftmountain","who is the tauren at highperch"}},{q="Where can Pao'ka Swiftmountain be found?",a="He is stranded atop Highperch in Thousand Needles. Reaching him requires finding a towering tauren totem near the cliffs, where a narrow path behind it climbs up the mountainside into the wyvern roosts.",al={"where is paoka","highperch path","how to find paoka"}},{q="Why is he hiding in Highperch?",a="His fascination with wyverns led him too close to one of their nests. The angry beasts chased him away and cut off his retreat, forcing him into hiding for several days.",al={"why is paoka trapped","why did wyverns attack paoka"}},{q="What happens after you help him escape?",a="Once escorted safely out of the nesting grounds, Pao'ka flees back to Motega Firemane at Whitereach Post, desperately hoping his mentor will not report the blunder to his father.",al={"homeward bound outcome","does paoka make it back"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Pao'ka represents the next generation of tauren scholars exploring Kalimdor; keeping him alive maintains strong ties with the elders at Whitereach Post.",["race:Tauren"]="Wyverns are deeply revered by the tauren as allies and faithful mounts, making Pao'ka's poorly planned intrusion both embarrassing and dangerous."},kw={"highperch","homeward bound","motega firemane","pao'ka swiftmountain","thousand needles","whitereach post","wyverns"},rel={"subzone:highperch","quest:4770","npc:motega-firemane","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Pao'ka Swiftmountain"}}
E["npc:parqual-fintallas"] = {t="npc",n="Parqual Fintallas",z="thousandneedles",s="Parqual Fintallas is a Forsaken scholar and former human historian of Lordaeron, currently residing in the Undercity's Apothecarium. Despite the grim surroundings of his undead existence, he retains a polite demeanor and an enduring passion for ancient lore, often assisting travelers sent to consult his deep historical expertise.",h="Parqual Fintallas is a Forsaken scholar and former human historian of Lordaeron, currently residing in the...",sec={{t="Scholar of Lost Lordaeron",b="In life, Parqual was a respected human scholar who resided in Lordaeron's Capital City with his family, immersing himself in historical texts. When the plague of undeath struck, Parqual was among the many citizens slain and raised, only to eventually break free under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. While the Forsaken largely embrace cold pragmatism and turn away from their former lives, Parqual retains his scholarly passion and pleasant manners, quietly longing for the historical tomes and memories of the world that once was.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of Ancient Lore",b="Parqual dwells among the bubbling vats and alchemists of the Apothecarium in the Undercity. Despite his macabre surroundings, he remains an invaluable font of knowledge regarding Azeroth's history. When adventurers undertake rigorous intellectual trials—such as the elusive 'Test of Lore'—they are directed to Parqual to retrieve answers and historical records that few others in the Horde possess.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Parqual Fintallas?",a="Parqual Fintallas can be found standing in the Apothecarium within the Undercity, the capital city of the Forsaken situated beneath the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"parqual fintallas location","where is parqual","parqual undercity"}},{q="What is Parqual Fintallas known for?",a="Parqual was an accomplished historian in life who knew almost everything there was to know about the kingdom of Lordaeron. Even in undeath, he serves as an intellectual authority, assisting adventurers seeking obscure historical texts and ancient knowledge.",al={"who is parqual","what does parqual do","parqual fintallas lore"}},{q="Why is Parqual involved in the Test of Lore?",a="The Test of Lore requires adventurers to demonstrate knowledge and retrieve esoteric records from around Azeroth. Parqual serves as an important contact because of his unmatched scholarly background and access to historical tomes in Lordaeron.",al={"parqual test of lore","test of lore undercity","parqual fintallas quest"}},{q="Does Parqual share the hostile demeanor of most Forsaken?",a="Unlike many bitter and cynical Forsaken, Parqual is remarkably gentle and polite. He greets adventurers with genuine warmth, noting how nice it is whenever someone takes the time to speak with him.",al={"is parqual friendly","parqual personality"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Parqual is a rare reminder of the kingdom of Lordaeron's intellectual past, clinging quietly to scholarship and civilized conversation amidst the bleakness of the Apothecarium.",["faction:Horde"]="When Horde adventurers face trials of the mind rather than the blade, Parqual provides the deep historical wisdom needed to uncover Azeroth's ancient truths."},kw={"apothecarium","fintallas","historian","lordaeron","parqual","scholar","test of lore","undercity"},rel={"quest:1152","zone:undercity","subzone:apothecarium","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Parqual Fintallas"}}
E["npc:pilot-longbeard"] = {t="npc",n="Pilot Longbeard",z="thousandneedles",s="Pilot Longbeard is a dwarven aviator stationed in the Hall of Arms within Ironforge's Military Ward. Though currently grounded in the mountain city, he maintains close ties with gnomish tinkerers and fellow flight enthusiasts operating far away in the Shimmering Flats.",h="Pilot Longbeard is a dwarven aviator stationed in the Hall of Arms within Ironforge's Military Ward.",sec={{t="A Grounded Aviator",b="Found amongst the martial displays and weaponsmiths of Ironforge's Military Ward, Pilot Longbeard represents the daring airborne tradition of Khaz Modan. While his duties keep him within the fortress city, Longbeard keeps an eager ear out for innovations and news from fellow mechanics across the continent, including the Brassbolts brothers tinkering out on the salt flats of Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Connections Across Continents",b="Longbeard serves as a point of contact for adventurous travelers heading south into Kalimdor. He frequently directs promising recruits and couriers toward the Shimmering Deep and the salt flats of Thousand Needles, where gnomish inventors push mechanical boundaries alongside their goblin rivals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Pilot Longbeard?",a="He is located inside the Hall of Arms in the Military Ward of Ironforge, standing near the trainers and military displays.",al={"pilot longbeard location","where is longbeard ironforge","how to find pilot longbeard"}},{q="What is Pilot Longbeard's role?",a="Pilot Longbeard is a quest giver who directs Alliance adventurers toward ventures abroad, particularly connecting travelers with his friends, the Brassbolts brothers, out in Thousand Needles.",al={"what does longbeard do","pilot longbeard quest","why talk to longbeard"}},{q="Who are the Brassbolts brothers to Longbeard?",a="They are gnomish tinkerers and associates of Longbeard operating in the Shimmering Flats, bound by a shared passion for engineering and experimental machinery.",al={"brassbolts connection","why does longbeard know brassbolts","longbeard shimmering deep"}},{q="Is Pilot Longbeard related to Furen Longbeard?",a="They share the prominent Longbeard clan name in Ironforge, suggesting clan kinship, though Pilot Longbeard focuses on aviation and engineering connections rather than smithing.",al={"furen longbeard brother","longbeard family dwarf","is he related to furen"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Pilot Longbeard exemplifies the dwarven adventurous spirit, bridging traditional Ironforge martial service with the excitement of gnomish aviation and mechanics.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an aviator with contacts among gnome tinkerers, Longbeard appreciates the mechanical ingenuity required to keep machinery flying and racing."},kw={"brassbolts","dwarf aviator","hall of arms","ironforge","military ward","pilot longbeard","shimmering deep","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:military-ward","quest:1179","quest:467","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:shimmering-deep","npc:furen-longbeard","topic:dwarf"},src={"Pilot Longbeard"}}
E["npc:pozzik"] = {t="npc",n="Pozzik",z="thousandneedles",s="Pozzik is an esteemed goblin tinkerer and racer stationed at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles. Once one of the most respected engineers in Undermine, he now dedicates his technical genius to constructing experimental rocket cars and settling the ultimate debate of engineering supremacy against his gnome counterpart.",h="Pozzik is an esteemed goblin tinkerer and racer stationed at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats in...",sec={{t="A Master of Undermine",b="Before retiring to the harsh salt flats of Thousand Needles, Pozzik built a legendary reputation on the Isle of Kezan. As one of the most respected tinkerers out of Undermine, his technical expertise spans complex internal combustion, propulsion, and hazardous chassis construction. Rather than settling into comfortable obscurity, however, Pozzik took his mechanical mastery into the desert to push high-speed machinery far past its breaking point.",sp=0},{t="The Duel on the Salt Flats",b="At the Mirage Raceway, Pozzik teamed up with his perennial gnome counterpart, Fizzle Brassbolts. Despite the historic rivalry between goblin explosives and delicate gnomish calibration, the two worked together to construct the sprawling racetrack across the dried lakebed. They field opposing racing outfits, testing prototype rocket cars to definitively prove whose racial design philosophy dominates the track. Naturally, Pozzik is always on the lookout for resourceful adventurers willing to acquire parts and shave weight off his designs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pozzik?",a="Pozzik is a veteran goblin tinkerer formerly from Undermine, now leading one side of the rocket-racing competition at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles.",al={"pozzik","who is pozzik","pozzik lore"}},{q="Why is Pozzik out in Thousand Needles?",a="After retiring from formal work in Undermine, Pozzik came to the Shimmering Flats to build and race experimental rocket cars across the vast, uninterrupted salt flats.",al={"why is pozzik here","pozzik shimmering flats"}},{q="What is his relationship with Fizzle Brassbolts?",a="Fizzle Brassbolts is Pozzik's longstanding gnomish rival and racetrack co-founder. Though they work side-by-side maintaining the Mirage Raceway, they constantly compete to prove goblin engineering is superior to gnomish craftsmanship.",al={"pozzik and fizzle","pozzik gnome rival"}},{q="Does Pozzik work for the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Pozzik is entirely neutral, working as an independent goblin entrepreneur at the raceway. He is willing to do business and offer tasks to both Alliance and Horde travelers.",al={"is pozzik neutral","pozzik faction"}},{q="What kind of projects is Pozzik working on right now?",a="Pozzik is obsessed with squeezing more speed out of his rocket cars. He develops multi-engine racing chassis, gathers rare lightweight ores, and sends explorers out for salvaged parts and components.",al={"pozzik quests","what does pozzik build"}},{q="What is MEGA?",a="MEGA stands for the Mechanical Engineers' Guild of Azeroth, a professional organization of top-tier tinkerers and machinists of which Pozzik is a member.",al={"what is mega","mechanical engineers guild of azeroth"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For engineers of either persuasion—goblin or gnomish—Pozzik represents the absolute pinnacle of high-risk, high-velocity applied mechanics.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes visiting the track will find in Pozzik their favorite foil: a boisterous goblin engineer convinced that brute thrust outmatches delicate precision."},kw={"fizzle brassbolts","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","tinker","undermine"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","npc:fizzle-brassbolts","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1176","topic:goblin","zone:tanaris"},src={"Pozzik"}}
E["npc:thalia-amberhide"] = {t="npc",n="Thalia Amberhide",z="thousandneedles",s="Thalia Amberhide is a tauren residing at Freewind Post in the jagged canyon of Thousand Needles. A loyal friend to her kin, she waits with mounting concern for the safe return of Lakota Windsong from the clutches of the Grimtotem clan.",h="Thalia Amberhide is a tauren residing at Freewind Post in the jagged canyon of Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Friend at the Post",b="Perched atop the towering bluffs of Freewind Post, Thalia Amberhide is a quiet presence among the bustling tauren settlement. Her heart is heavy with worry for her close companion, Lakota Windsong, who was taken captive by Arnak Grimtotem and his treacherous kin. Thalia relies on passing Horde adventurers who brave the canyon depths to find Lakota, break her bonds, and guide her safely back up the lifts to the haven of the mesa.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thalia Amberhide?",a="Thalia Amberhide is a tauren living at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. She is a loyal friend to Lakota Windsong, another tauren who has run afoul of the treacherous Grimtotem clan.",al={"thalia amberhide","who is thalia"}},{q="Where can Thalia Amberhide be found?",a="She can be found up on the high mesa of Freewind Post, located in the middle of Thousand Needles. Travelers must take the massive wooden elevators from the canyon floor to reach the settlement.",al={"thalia location","where is thalia amberhide"}},{q="What is Thalia's connection to Lakota Windsong?",a="Thalia is a close friend of Lakota Windsong. When Lakota is captured by Arnak Grimtotem, Thalia serves as the welcoming contact at Freewind Post once an adventurer successfully helps Lakota escape her captors.",al={"thalia and lakota","who is lakota windsong"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, aiding Thalia and rescuing Lakota strikes directly at the sinister treachery of the Grimtotem tribe, defending their fellow kin against clan discord.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post is a crucial Horde waypoint in Thousand Needles, and helping Thalia Amberhide safeguards the settlement against Grimtotem aggression."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","freewind post","grimtotem","lakota windsong","thalia amberhide","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:lakota-windsong","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","quest:4904","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Thalia Amberhide"}}
E["npc:wizlo-bearingshiner"] = {t="npc",n="Wizlo Bearingshiner",z="thousandneedles",s="Wizlo Bearingshiner is an enterprising goblin tinkerer stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. Ever keen to harness unusual power sources and volatile alchemical concoctions, he looks to adventurous travelers to assist with his ambitious mechanical experiments. His inventive curiosity frequently pits goblin technical ambition against the dangerous wildlife and mystical energies of the region.",h="Wizlo Bearingshiner is an enterprising goblin tinkerer stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="An Engineer at the Post",b="Perched alongside the Tauren at Whitereach Post high above the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, Wizlo Bearingshiner represents typical goblin industriousness. While the local grimtotem and wildlife present constant hazards below, Wizlo remains laser-focused on acquiring components for his latest gadgets. He operates with typical goblin pragmatism, willing to trade coin and knowledge with anyone willing to brave the harsh canyon to gather field materials.",sp=0},{t="Unconventional Power Sources",b="Wizlo's tinkerings are far from mundane; he often seeks unconventional methods to supercharge his devices. Rather than relying solely on conventional fuels or standard parts, his schemes involve experimenting with potent alchemical mixtures and unusual energetic catalysts, such as his notorious Hypercapacitor Gizmo. His willingness to mix mystical resources, including waters drawn from night elven moonwells, with raw mechanical engineering highlights the reckless innovation goblins are famous for.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Wizlo Bearingshiner?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner is a goblin engineer and quest giver stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. He recruits adventurers to retrieve specialized reagents and test volatile mechanical inventions.",al={"wizlo bearingshiner","who is wizlo","whitereach goblin"}},{q="Where can I find Wizlo Bearingshiner?",a="He is located atop the bluffs at Whitereach Post in northern Thousand Needles, a camp overlooking the sweeping canyon basin.",al={"wizlo location","where is wizlo","find wizlo"}},{q="What kind of experiments does he run?",a="Wizlo focuses on unorthodox engineering projects, including calibrating devices like his Hypercapacitor Gizmo and brewing curious tonics infused with potent mystical waters.",al={"wizlo quests","what does wizlo do","wizlo gadgets"}},{q="Why is a goblin working with the Horde at Whitereach Post?",a="Goblins frequently set up shop wherever commerce, adventure, and opportunity intersect. Whitereach Post offers Wizlo safety on high ground and a convenient staging point to employ passing mercenaries.",al={"why is wizlo here","is wizlo horde","goblin at whitereach"}},{q="Does Wizlo belong to the Steamwheedle Cartel?",a="Like many independent goblin tinkerers in Kalimdor's frontier, Wizlo operates with neutral, commercial aims, focusing strictly on business, invention, and personal profit.",al={"wizlo faction","steamwheedle wizlo","wizlo cartel"}},{q="What is the Hypercapacitor Gizmo?",a="The Hypercapacitor Gizmo is one of Wizlo's specialized mechanical devices designed to draw or regulate intense electrical and kinetic energy during his field experiments.",al={"hypercapacitor gizmo","wizlo device","gizmo quest"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will appreciate Wizlo's eccentric drive to push mechanical design past safe tolerances, especially through volatile devices like the Hypercapacitor Gizmo.",["faction:Horde"]="While making camp at Whitereach Post alongside the local Tauren, Horde travelers can easily employ Wizlo's mechanical expertise to secure useful gadgets."},kw={"goblin engineer","hypercapacitor gizmo","thousand needles","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","quest:5151","quest:9433","quest:9434","topic:goblin","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale"},src={"Wizlo Bearingshiner"}}
E["npc:wizzle-brassbolts"] = {t="npc",n="Wizzle Brassbolts",z="thousandneedles",s="Wizzle Brassbolts is an Alliance gnome engineer stationed alongside his fellow tinkerers out on the salt flats of Thousand Needles. Working with the gnomish racing team at the Mirage Raceway, he seeks durable local materials to reinforce their experimental rocket cars.",h="Wizzle Brassbolts is an Alliance gnome engineer stationed alongside his fellow tinkerers out on the salt...",sec={{t="Tinkering on the Salt Flats",b="Out in the shimmering heat of the Shimmering Flats, the rivalry between gnomish and goblin engineering takes the form of high-speed rocket car races. Wizzle Brassbolts works as part of the gnomish raceway crew, striving to keep their vehicles intact against blistering speeds and abrasive salt. To bolster their machines, he recruits adventurers to hunt the local wildlife—such as the sturdy turtles wandering the basin—harvesting thick shells and natural plating to reinforce the team's chassis.",sp=0},{t="Friends in Distant Places",b="Wizzle maintains close ties with friends across the continents, including fellow tinkerers and aerial scouts like Pilot Longbeard. Whether trading supplies, sharing schematics, or sending couriers back and forth with custom-machined parts, Wizzle keeps the gnomish team supplied despite their remote, inhospitable testing ground in the Southern Barrens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wizzle Brassbolts?",a="Wizzle Brassbolts is located at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats, in the southeastern reaches of Thousand Needles. He stands among the gnomish pit crew and their machinery.",al={"wizzle location","where is wizzle brassbolts","wizzle brassbolts map"}},{q="Why is Wizzle collecting turtle shells?",a="High-speed racing across the abrasive salt flats wrecks lightweight metal plating. Wizzle uses the rock-hard shells of native salt-flat turtles to craft reinforced, heat-resistant armor and components for the gnomish team's race cars.",al={"hardened shells quest","why does wizzle want shells","turtle shells raceway"}},{q="Who are the Brassbolts brothers?",a="The Brassbolts are a family of gnomish tinkerers and machinists. They collaborate on engineering ventures and keep in contact across distant Alliance and neutral outposts, sharing parts and technical expertise.",al={"brassbolts family","the brassbolts brothers","wizzle brothers"}},{q="Is Wizzle friendly to Horde players?",a="While the Mirage Raceway itself maintains a neutral truce between the goblin and gnome racing syndicates, Wizzle Brassbolts is aligned with the Alliance and offers his tasks specifically to Alliance adventurers.",al={"can horde talk to wizzle","wizzle brassbolts horde"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizzle exemplifies the gnomish engineering philosophy: pushing high-velocity machines to their limits and relying on unusual structural reinforcements when metal sheets fail.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes visiting the Shimmering Flats will find in Wizzle a kindred spirit, stubbornly determined to defeat the reckless contraptions of the Steamwheedle goblins using superior craft."},kw={"brassbolts","mirage raceway","pilot longbeard","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","wizzle"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","quest:1105","quest:1179","npc:pilot-longbeard","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},src={"Wizzle Brassbolts"}}
E["quest:1100"] = {t="quest",n="Lonebrow's Journal",z="thousandneedles",s="Lonebrow's Journal is an Alliance quest initiated by finding a weathered book held in the hand of a dead dwarf at the base of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles. The notes detail his final journey and prompt the finder to deliver the volume west to a night elf druid stationed on the Feralas border.",h="Lonebrow's Journal is an Alliance quest initiated by finding a weathered book held in the hand of a dead...",sec={{t="A Fallen Explorer",b="Near the base of the Great Lift, the massive mechanical elevator connecting the Barrens to the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, lies the body of Henrig Lonebrow. Clutched in his hand is a personal journal detailing his travels through this rugged territory. Left behind in a hostile desert dominated by centaur and tauren, his corpse serves as a grim warning of how unforgiving the canyon can be to isolated travelers.",sp=0},{t="A Dying Request",b="Reading through Henrig's journal reveals his intended path and final wish. Rather than leaving his findings to decay in the canyon, the explorer hoped his records would reach friendly hands. Following the road straight west across Thousand Needles leads out of the dry gullies and toward Thalanaar, the night elf outpost guarding the border to Feralas, where the druid Falfindel Waywarder awaits news of the traveler.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Kraul",b="When Falfindel Waywarder reviews Lonebrow's notes, the explorer's fate becomes intertwined with a larger menace in Southern Kalimdor. Henrig's observations point toward the bramble-choked warrens of Razorfen Kraul back to the north, revealing that a dangerous crone leads the quilboar dwelling inside.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find Henrig Lonebrow's body?",a="His body lies at the foot of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles. From the bottom of the western elevator ramp, head roughly twenty-five feet forward toward a low rock ledge, where his corpse rests with the journal in hand.",al={"henrig lonebrow location","where is lonebrow journal","lonebrow body","find lonebrow"}},{q="Who do I deliver the journal to?",a="Deliver the journal to Falfindel Waywarder, a night elf druid stationed at Thalanaar. Thalanaar is situated along the main westward road right on the border between Thousand Needles and Feralas.",al={"who gets lonebrow journal","where to turn in lonebrow","lonebrow turn in","falfindel location"}},{q="Who was Henrig Lonebrow?",a="Henrig Lonebrow was a dwarven traveler venturing through central Kalimdor. He perished near the base of the Great Lift, leaving behind a weathered journal detailing his observations of the surrounding lands and dangerous quilboar movements.",al={"who is henrig lonebrow","lonebrow backstory","who is lonebrow"}},{q="What does this quest lead to?",a="Turning in the journal to Falfindel Waywarder unlocks the quest 'The Crone of the Kraul', which directs Alliance adventurers to venture into the Razorfen Kraul dungeon.",al={"lonebrow follow up","quest after lonebrow journal","lonebrow quest chain"},sp=1},{q="Can Horde players pick up the journal?",a="No. The journal and its subsequent quest chain are strictly for Alliance players, leading directly to the Alliance border post at Thalanaar.",al={"is lonebrow journal alliance only","can horde do lonebrow journal","horde lonebrow"}},{q="Why was Lonebrow heading toward Thalanaar?",a="Thalanaar is the nearest Alliance outpost in the region, serving as a sanctuary between Thousand Needles and the wilds of Feralas. Lonebrow intended to share his regional observations with the night elves stationed there.",al={"why thalanaar","why send book to druid","lonebrow purpose"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Henrig Lonebrow's demise serves as a somber reminder of the dangers dwarven explorers face far from Ironforge in the wild corners of Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="With few outposts between Theramore and Thalanaar, recovering Lonebrow's journal ensures vital intelligence reaches Alliance allies before it is lost to the canyon.",["class:Druid"]="Falfindel Waywarder in Thalanaar monitors unnatural shifts in the local ecosystem, making Lonebrow's notes regarding the quilboar in Razorfen of direct interest to the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"falfindel","feralas","great lift","henrig","journal","lonebrow","razorfen kraul","thalanaar","thousand needles","waywarder"},rel={"quest:1101","npc:falfindel-waywarder","subzone:great-lift","subzone:thalanaar","zone:thousandneedles","zone:razorfenkraul","zone:feralas","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Henrig Lonebrow's Journal",["end"]="Falfindel Waywarder",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1100},src={"Lonebrow's Journal (quest)"}}
E["quest:1104"] = {t="quest",n="Salt Flat Venom",z="thousandneedles",s="Out on the blinding salt expanse of the Shimmering Flats, gnome engineer Fizzle Brassbolts searches for unusual ingredients to supercharge his rocket car. Convinced that the intensely saline venom of local scorpids will produce an ultra-hot burning propellant, he tasks passing adventurers with braving the stinging beasts.",h="Out on the blinding salt expanse of the Shimmering Flats, gnome engineer Fizzle Brassbolts searches for...",sec={{t="A Volatile Recipe",b="The Mirage Raceway is an endless battle of high-speed technical supremacy between gnomish precision and goblin audacity. For Fizzle Brassbolts, standard hydrocarbons and clockwork parts simply are not enough to outpace the competition. He envisions a custom fuel mixture tailored to burn far hotter than conventional propellants, driving their rocket cars across the dried salt lake at blistering speeds.",sp=0},{t="Saline Venom of the Salt Flats",b="Fizzle's breakthrough relies on the dangerous native fauna of the Shimmering Flats. The local scorpids have evolved to survive in an arid, salt-encrusted wasteland, resulting in an exceptionally saline venom. Rather than fearing its deadly toxicity, Fizzle sees it as a raw chemical payload. Once boiled, refined, and treated with exotic catalytic agents, he believes the salty venom will deliver the explosive combustion required to leave the goblin pit crews in the dust.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Fizzle Brassbolts want scorpid venom?",a="Fizzle is inventing a new rocket car fuel that burns extremely hot. He believes the unusually high salt content found in the venom of native Shimmering Flats scorpids is the vital chemical component needed to complete his explosive mixture.",al={"why scorpid venom","what is venom for","fizzle fuel recipe"}},{q="Where can the necessary scorpids be found?",a="Scorpids wander all across the open expanses of the Shimmering Flats, particularly prowling the western flats and the desert sands away from the central racetrack.",al={"scorpid location","where are scorpids","salt flat venom mobs"}},{q="What will Fizzle do with the venom once collected?",a="Fizzle intends to boil down the venom, treat it with a skipper-otomer, and blend it with a nega-catalyst to produce his high-octane rocket propellant—assuming he can find where he misplaced his notes.",al={"how is venom turned to fuel","fuel process"}},{q="Can members of both the Alliance and Horde help Fizzle?",a="Yes. The Mirage Raceway is managed under a neutral truce between the gnomes and goblins, allowing adventurers of either faction to assist the pit crews without political interference.",al={"is this quest neutral","horde or alliance"}},{q="Why are gnomes and goblins racing in Thousand Needles?",a="The Shimmering Flats provide a vast, perfectly flat, and unobstructed bed of hard-packed salt, making it the ideal proving ground for experimental, high-speed rocket cars and dragsters.",al={"why raceway here","why mirage raceway"}},{q="Does the fuel actually make the car fly?",a="While Fizzle enthusiastically claims the car will 'fly,' gnomish rocket vehicles on the salt flats are designed to skim the ground at breakneck speeds, though catastrophic liftoffs and crashes are never out of the question.",al={"does car fly","fizzle rocket car result"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Fizzle represents classic gnomish ambition: relentless tinkering, questionable chemical safety, misplaced notes, and the constant urge to outshine goblin mechanics.",["profession:Engineering"]="Using organic toxins treated with catalysts like skipper-otomers highlights the creative and volatile experiments common in competitive vehicle engineering."},kw={"fizzle brassbolts","fuel","mirage raceway","rocket car","salty scorpid venom","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:fizzle-brassbolts","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},m={start="Fizzle Brassbolts",level="30",id=1104},src={"Salt Flat Venom"}}
E["quest:1105"] = {t="quest",n="Hardened Shells",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, the gnome tinkerer Wizzle Brassbolts worries his brother's potent new rocket fuel will dissolve their racer from the inside out. To prevent a catastrophe on the salt flats, Wizzle enlists passersby to harvest hardened shells from the local tortoises to craft an impervious fuel tank.",h="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, the gnome tinkerer Wizzle Brassbolts worries his brother's...",sec={{t="Volatile Innovations",b="Out in the blinding heat of the Shimmering Flats, the rivalry between gnome and goblin engineers pushes mechanical ambition to reckless extremes. Wizzle Brassbolts and his brother are determined to dominate the Mirage Raceway with their custom rocket car. However, his brother's experimental fuel mixture is showing signs of being far too potent. Fearing that the corrosive concoction will melt straight through the vehicle's standard chassis and tanks, Wizzle scrambles to find a container tough enough to survive the run.",sp=0},{t="Desert Armored Solutions",b="Rather than relying on refined metals that might dissolve under chemical strain, Wizzle turns to the natural adaptations of the salt flats. The native tortoises roaming Thousand Needles possess shells remarkably resistant to harsh elements and mechanical wear. By gathering these hardened carapaces, Wizzle hopes to fashion custom fuel tanks resilient enough to hold the volatile mixture without blowing the rocket car to pieces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Wizzle need tortoise shells instead of metal?",a="His brother is brewing an experimental rocket fuel that is corrosive enough to dissolve metal. Wizzle believes the natural, ultra-hard shells of the local tortoises will withstand the chemical wear better than standard tanks.",al={"why turtle shells","why tortoise shells","fuel tank shell"}},{q="Who is Wizzle Brassbolts?",a="Wizzle is a gnome engineer stationed at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. He works alongside his brother to build and fine-tune their high-speed rocket car to outrace their goblin competitors.",al={"wizzle","who is wizzle"}},{q="Where can the tortoises be found?",a="The tortoises wander openly across the vast salt pan of the Shimmering Flats, with particularly dense gatherings basking near the old shipwreck in the northeastern section.",al={"tortoise location","where are the turtles","where to get hardened shells"}},{q="Is this an Alliance or Horde quest?",a="It is completely neutral. The Mirage Raceway operates outside faction warfare, focusing on engineering competitions, allowing both Alliance and Horde adventurers to assist Wizzle.",al={"is hardened shells neutral","alliance or horde"}},{q="What happens once the shells are delivered?",a="Wizzle eagerly begins fabricating them into reinforced fuel tanks, though he quickly realizes the shells are so durable he will likely ruin an entire toolbox carving them into shape.",al={"wizzle shell result","what does wizzle do with shells"},sp=1},{q="Why is fuel tank failure such a concern on the flats?",a="Rocket cars travel at terrifying speeds across the salt. A tank failure caused by acidic fuel would ignite mid-run, destroying the vehicle and incinerating the pilot.",al={"rocket car danger","why worried about fuel"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Using organic armor plates to house volatile compounds is unorthodox, highlighting the eccentric trial-and-error approach gnomish tinkerers rely on under pressure.",["race:Gnome"]="Brotherly ingenuity and reckless scientific ambition meet head-on here, capturing the gnomish drive to out-innovate goblin rivals no matter the logistical hurdle."},kw={"hardened shells","mirage raceway","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","tortoise","wizzle brassbolts"},rel={"npc:wizzle-brassbolts","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},m={start="Wizzle Brassbolts",level="30",id=1105},src={"Hardened Shells"}}
E["quest:1110"] = {t="quest",n="Rocket Car Parts",z="thousandneedles",s="Rocket Car Parts is an errand undertaken for the opportunistic dwarf merchant Kravel Koalbeard on the blinding salt pans of the Shimmering Flats. Rather than letting the violently scattered debris of high-speed racer crashes go to waste, Koalbeard pays wanderers to comb the desert floor and recover wrecked mechanisms to resell directly to the rival gnome and goblin pit crews.",h="Rocket Car Parts is an errand undertaken for the opportunistic dwarf merchant Kravel Koalbeard on the...",sec={{t="Debris on the Salt Flats",b="The Shimmering Flats serve as the proving ground for the fierce technological rivalry between goblin and gnomish engineers. High-velocity experimental rocket cars routinely suffer catastrophic malfunctions, leaving twisted gears, cylinders, and jagged sheets of metal scattered wide across the vast white desert. While the pit crews focus solely on building and tuning the next machine, the desert floor has quietly become a scrap yard of experimental engineering.",sp=0},{t="Koalbeard's Salvage Enterprise",b="Rather than competing directly on the track, the dwarf entrepreneur Kravel Koalbeard recognized a lucrative middleman opportunity at the Mirage Raceway. Gnome and goblin mechanics burn through parts at a furious pace and are constantly desperate for spare mechanisms to slap onto their vehicles. Koalbeard hires travelers to gather thirty bundles of shattered debris, turning devastating crashes into fresh inventory and neatly profiting off the drivers' misfortunes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kravel Koalbeard?",a="Kravel Koalbeard is a shrewd dwarf merchant stationed at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. He runs various entrepreneurial schemes around the track, primarily focusing on scavenging, odd jobs, and turning the rivalries of gnomes and goblins into personal profit.",al={"kravel koalbeard","who gives rocket car parts","raceway dwarf"}},{q="Why are there so many rocket car parts scattered on the ground?",a="The Mirage Raceway is an active testing and racing track where goblin and gnomish engineers push experimental rocket vehicles to dangerous limits. Violent wrecks and sudden explosions happen regularly across the salt pans, throwing structural fragments, gears, and cylinders across the expanse.",al={"why are there car parts in the desert","shimmering flats debris","broken rocket cars"}},{q="What does Kravel do with the wrecked parts?",a="Koalbeard cleans up the collected scrap and pawns it straight back to the gnomish and goblin race teams. The crews constantly burn through materials and are eager to buy back whatever contraptions and metal scraps they can bolt onto their next prototypes.",al={"what does kravel want with parts","why collect car parts"}},{q="Where are these parts located?",a="The parts lie scattered throughout the open desert floor across the Shimmering Flats, surrounding the central racing camp. They appear as discarded mechanical scrap heaps, twisted gears, cylinders, and flattened metal plates.",al={"where to find rocket car parts","parts locations","car parts shimmering flats"}},{q="Does this quest tie into other tasks around the raceway?",a="Yes. Scavenging the flats pairs naturally with culling local wildlife for other raceway patrons, such as gathering venom from scorpid stingers, harvesting turtle shells, and thinning out the local buzzards and basilisks while traversing the wide salt pans.",al={"raceway quests","shimmering flats hunting quests","quests to do with rocket car parts"}},{q="What happens to the drivers involved in these wrecks?",a="Rocket car racing is notoriously lethal. When sorting through the salvaged scrap, Koalbeard casually notices a severed ear crushed between metal plates, highlighting the grim reality that many pilots do not walk away from high-speed test runs.",al={"do drivers survive crashes","squashed ear","pilot deaths raceway"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Combing the salt flats reveals the reckless ingenuity of rival goblin and gnomish designs, where unstable rocket boosters and improvised chassis frequently end in spectacular structural failures.",["race:Dwarf"]="While many Ironforge dwarves look to the raceway for mechanical innovation or excavation, Kravel Koalbeard embodies a thoroughly mercenary streak, interested strictly in the coin salvage operations bring.",["race:Gnome"]="Recovering these parts highlights the relentless, if occasionally disastrous, drive of gnomish engineers attempting to outpace and out-innovate their goblin competitors on the open track."},kw={"crashes","gnome","goblin","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","rocket car parts","salvage","scrap","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","npc:kravel-koalbeard","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1104","quest:1105","quest:1176","topic:goblin"},m={level="31",id=1110},src={"Rocket Car Parts (quest)"}}
E["quest:1149"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Faith",z="thousandneedles",s="The Test of Faith is a spiritual rite administered by the hermit Dorn Plainstalker high above the canyon floor of Thousand Needles. It challenges Horde adventurers to prove their resolve by stepping off a precarious wooden plank into the open chasm below.",h="The Test of Faith is a spiritual rite administered by the hermit Dorn Plainstalker high above the canyon...",sec={{t="A Measure of the Spirit",b="Dorn Plainstalker dwells in a secluded vantage overlooking the wind-carved spires of Thousand Needles, pondering the facets that make up a living being: the mind, the body, and the spirit. Rather than relying on simple tribal traditions, Dorn administers his own trials to measure what truly lies within an adventurer. He posits that while conviction can take many forms, the essential quality is simply having the fortitude to believe in something strongly enough to risk one's life on it.",sp=0},{t="The Leap into the Void",b="The trial is deceptively direct. Transported to the sheer summit of one of the towering stone needles, the supplicant stands atop weathered wooden planks suspended over empty air. To pass, one must conquer self-preservation and step off into the abyss without any tangible guarantee of survival. Those who jump find their descent broken by arcane or spiritual forces and are whisked back to safety, having demonstrated that their spirit is tempered enough to face unforeseen trials ahead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dorn Plainstalker?",a="Dorn Plainstalker is a tauren hermit residing in a remote cliffside camp above Thousand Needles. He serves as a spiritual proctor, seeking out adventurers of the Horde to test the various aspects of their mortal makeup: faith, endurance, and strength.",al={"dorn plainstalker lore","who gives test of faith","quest giver thousand needles"}},{q="Will jumping off the plank kill me?",a="No. While the drop off the needle spire looks entirely fatal, the trial functions as an act of trust. Once you step off the wooden planks, magical warding catches you mid-fall and teleports you directly back to Dorn Plainstalker's cave unscathed.",al={"do i die jumping","will fall damage kill me test of faith","is test of faith dangerous"},sp=1},{q="What happens after passing the Test of Faith?",a="Proving your faith is merely the opening rite in Dorn's series of trials. Once your spirit is deemed receptive, Dorn immediately challenges your physical resilience in the Test of Endurance.",al={"what comes after test of faith","test of faith chain","dorn plainstalker next quest"},sp=1},{q="Why does Dorn say failure means realizing the vastness of the Nether?",a="It is Dorn's grim philosophical reminder of mortality. In his eyes, those who lack the inner fire to commit fully to the challenge risk losing their lives—and their souls—to the endless void beyond the living world.",al={"vastness of the nether meaning","dorn plainstalker nether quote"}},{q="Can Alliance adventurers take this test?",a="No. Dorn Plainstalker only extends his wisdom and spiritual guidance to champions aligned with the Horde traversing the dangerous canyons of southern Kalimdor.",al={"is test of faith horde only","can alliance do test of faith"}},{q="Where does the Test of Faith take place?",a="The trial begins at Dorn's camp in the Thousand Needles canyon walls, which magically connects to the dizzying precipice of an isolated stone spire jutting out over the gorge floor.",al={"test of faith location","where is the plank thousand needles"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the Shu'halo, undergoing rites of passage across Kalimdor's sacred geography is an ancient tradition, and Dorn's trial demands a visceral display of trust in the unseen.",["class:Priest"]="Priests who spend their days cultivating faith in higher powers find themselves challenged to put their theoretical convictions into literal physical motion.",["faction:Horde"]="The trials reflect the core values binding the fledgling Horde together in Kalimdor: absolute conviction, resilience against hostile environments, and unyielding will."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","horde","leap of faith","planks","test of endurance","test of faith","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","quest:1150","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},m={start="Dorn Plainstalker",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1149},src={"Test of Faith (quest)"}}
E["quest:1150"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Endurance",z="thousandneedles",s="The Test of Endurance is the second rite in a series of spiritual trials overseen by Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles. Having already proven their courage of spirit, Horde adventurers are tasked with pushing their physical endurance to the limit by infiltrating Roguefeather Den and drawing out the fierce harpy leader, Grenka Bloodscreech.",h="The Test of Endurance is the second rite in a series of spiritual trials overseen by Dorn Plainstalker in...",sec={{t="Testing the Body",b="Dorn Plainstalker, dwelling at the Weathered Nook, takes it upon himself to temper young warriors before they venture into the wider, harsher world. Where the initial rite proved that a traveler possessed unshakable faith and steady nerve, this trial tests physical fortitude. In Dorn's philosophy, true readiness requires harmony between spiritual devotion, mental discipline, and the sheer stamina to survive sustained brutality.",sp=0},{t="Incursion into Roguefeather Den",b="The chosen arena for this trial is Roguefeather Den, a treacherous cavern tucked within Screeching Canyon west of Freewind Post. Swarming with hostile harpies, the cave poses severe danger to solitary wanderers. To complete the trial, challengers must carve their way deep into the subterranean roost, sabotage the harpies' gathered provisions, and weather the flock's ferocious retaliation until the matriarch Grenka Bloodscreech herself takes the field.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Test of Endurance?",a="The quest is offered by Dorn Plainstalker, an elder tauren stationed at the Weathered Nook in the canyon bluffs of Thousand Needles.",al={"quest giver test of endurance","who starts test of endurance","dorn plainstalker quest"}},{q="Where is Roguefeather Den located?",a="Roguefeather Den lies high along the southern canyon walls of Thousand Needles, west of Freewind Post. Travelers must ascend a winding path through Screeching Canyon to reach the cave entrance overlooking the salt plains.",al={"roguefeather den location","where is harpy cave","screeching canyon ramp"}},{q="How do you summon Grenka Bloodscreech?",a="Grenka Bloodscreech appears after you fight your way to the deepest chambers of Roguefeather Den and vandalize the cache of food and supplies stored there by the harpies, provoking her into defending her roost.",al={"summon grenka","how to spawn grenka bloodscreech","find grenka"}},{q="What comes after the Test of Endurance?",a="Returning Grenka's severed claw to Dorn Plainstalker proves your physical stamina, prompting him to send you on the next challenge in his sequence: the Test of Strength.",al={"next quest after endurance","what follows test of endurance","dorn plainstalker next test"}},{q="Why does Dorn test adventurers who aren't tauren?",a="Dorn believes it is his calling to mentor all youth of the Horde, regardless of race or tribe. He views untested pride as a death sentence in the wider world, insisting that every warrior demonstrate readiness across body, mind, and spirit.",al={"why does dorn help horde","dorn plainstalker philosophy","tauren trials for other races"}},{q="What was the trial before this one?",a="Before testing the body's endurance, Dorn requires challengers to undertake the Test of Faith, a perilous leap of devotion that tests whether an adventurer's spirit will falter in the face of fear.",al={"previous quest","test before endurance","first trial"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, Dorn Plainstalker's trials reflect traditional rites of passage, testing whether an initiate's physical stamina matches the spiritual guidance of the Earth Mother.",["faction:Horde"]="Dorn offers these challenges to all Horde races, believing that young warriors from every tribe must be tempered against hardship before facing the perils of Kalimdor."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","freewind post","grenka bloodscreech","roguefeather den","screeching canyon","test of endurance","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","quest:1149","quest:1151","subzone:roguefeather-den","subzone:weathered-nook","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:harpy"},m={start="Dorn Plainstalker",level="29",faction="Horde",id=1150},src={"Test of Endurance"}}
E["quest:1151"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Strength",z="thousandneedles",s="The Test of Strength is the third trial overseen by the tauren mystic Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles. To prove their physical prowess, Horde champions are tasked with hunting down Rok'Alim the Pounder, an ancient, free-roaming rock elemental, and returning with remnants of his shattered form.",h="The Test of Strength is the third trial overseen by the tauren mystic Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="Remnants of the Black Empire",b="Long ago, during the reign of the Old Gods, primordial elementals blanketed the surface of the world, serving their dark masters. When those ancient entities were overthrown and sealed beneath the earth, the elemental spirits lost their tether to this realm, largely fading from physical existence unless bound and summoned by modern spellcraft. A few entities, however, were stubborn and potent enough to linger on Azeroth indefinitely without magical anchors. Rok'Alim the Pounder is one such relic, wandering the arid canyons of Thousand Needles as a living echo of that primordial age.",sp=0},{t="The Pounder of Thousand Needles",b="The local centaur clans gave Rok'Alim his moniker on account of the deafening, earthquake-like crashes produced when his stone fists strike the canyon floor. Anyone foolish or bold enough to stray into his roaming path is hammered into dust. Because Rok'Alim represents raw, unbridled physical mass, Dorn Plainstalker directs initiates to break the beast as a direct measure of their warrior spirit, demanding fragments of the elemental's stony heart as proof of victory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this quest begin and end?",a="The quest is offered and completed by Dorn Plainstalker, a tauren elder stationed at the Weathered Nook, a secluded canyon camp nestled high among the spires of Thousand Needles.",al={"quest giver","where to turn in","dorn location"}},{q="What is Rok'Alim the Pounder?",a="Rok'Alim is an ancient rock elemental who has endured in Kalimdor since the era of the Old Gods. Unlike modern summoned elementals, he possesses enough innate power to remain physically manifest on Azeroth entirely on his own.",al={"who is rokalim","what kind of mob is rokalim","elemental lore"}},{q="Why do the centaur call him 'the Pounder'?",a="The centaur tribes in the canyon dubbed him the Pounder because of the thunderous, rolling shockwaves his stone fists unleash when smashing anything in his path.",al={"the pounder nickname","centaur name for rokalim"}},{q="Where can Rok'Alim be found in the canyon?",a="Rok'Alim wanders the northwestern stretches of Thousand Needles, generally patrolling open ground south of the main road that cuts through the canyon floor.",al={"rokalim spawn","where is rokalim"}},{q="What place does this quest hold in the overall trial chain?",a="Test of Strength is the third trial in the chain. It follows the Test of Faith and the Test of Endurance, and directly precedes the final trial, the Test of Lore.",al={"quest chain order","what comes next","what comes before"}},{q="Why does Dorn require an elemental to be slain instead of a beast or enemy?",a="Dorn chooses Rok'Alim because the elemental is a pure manifestation of living stone and unyielding, primordial force. Conquering such an opponent proves physical superiority over the raw, unbending earth itself.",al={"why kill an elemental","purpose of test of strength"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren pilgrims, facing down an untamed spirit of stone is a traditional test of harmony and physical will, demonstrating the hunter's capacity to endure and overcome the harshest forces of the Earth Mother.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman recognize Rok'Alim not just as an obstacle, but as a dangerous, unbound manifestation of earth whose refusal to yield disturbs the local balance of spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="Completing the Weathered Nook rites earns the respect of the Thunder Bluff elders and cements an adventurer's reputation across Kalimdor."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","old gods","rock elemental","rok'alim","test of strength","the pounder","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","subzone:weathered-nook","quest:1150","quest:1152","quest:1149","zone:thousandneedles","topic:old-god","topic:centaur"},m={start="Dorn Plainstalker",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1151},src={"Test of Strength"}}
E["quest:1152"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="Following trials of faith, endurance, and strength in Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker directs Horde champions northward to Stonetalon Mountains. There, a wise shaman named Braug Dimspirit waits to administer the Test of Lore. This trial shifts the focus from physical resolve to an understanding of the world's deep history and widespread suffering.",h="Following trials of faith, endurance, and strength in Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker directs Horde...",sec={{t="From Faith to Lore",b="In the sheltered refuge of the Weathered Nook, Dorn Plainstalker pushes initiates through demanding trials meant to test their spiritual conviction, physical endurance, and martial prowess. Yet brute strength and blind faith alone do not make a true champion of the Horde. Dorn recognizes his own boundaries as a teacher and sends those who have proven themselves to Stonetalon Mountains, where an elder shaman can test their intellect and worldliness.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Stonetalon",b="The journey takes travelers north across the dry scrub of the Barrens and into the crags of Stonetalon. High in the mountains, near the entrance to Talondeep Path—the cavern cutting through the rock toward Ashenvale—sits the hermitage of Braug Dimspirit. He watches over an embattled frontier where goblin logging ventures despoil the forests and hostile night elves fiercely defend their ancestral borders.",sp=0},{t="A Broader Perspective",b="Upon meeting Braug, the true purpose of the test becomes apparent. Rather than asking for blind factional pride, Braug reflects on the tragic state of Azeroth. He observes that while the orcs and Forsaken receive relentless blame for war and corruption, almost every civilization shares responsibility for the land's plight. Goblins tear down ancient timber, and night elves harbor deep distrust for the younger races. The Test of Lore demands that a champion see beyond immediate enmities and grasp the broader history of a wounded world.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Test of Lore?",a="It is an instructional trial within a larger rite of passage designed by tauren elders. Initiates must prove that they possess not only physical might and faith, but also historical awareness and an understanding of Azeroth's shared past.",al={"test of lore meaning","what is this quest"}},{q="Where can I find Braug Dimspirit?",a="Braug Dimspirit resides in the Stonetalon Mountains, situated near Windshear Crag right by the entrance to the Talondeep Path cave that connects Stonetalon to Ashenvale.",al={"braug dimspirit location","where is braug"}},{q="Why does Dorn Plainstalker send you away?",a="Dorn oversees the trials of faith, endurance, and strength in Thousand Needles, but he admits that the lore of the world is not his domain to teach. He directs worthy initiates to Braug, a shaman with the necessary wisdom to test the mind.",al={"why stonetalon","why dorn sends you"}},{q="What threats should travelers look out for on the way?",a="Dorn specifically warns that night elves prowl the borderlands near Ashenvale and Stonetalon, viewing Horde presence as an intrusion. The surrounding area in Windshear Crag is also rife with volatile goblin logging operations.",al={"dangers to braug","talondeep path danger"}},{q="What is Braug Dimspirit's view of the world's conflicts?",a="Braug believes that all mortal races share blame for the world's suffering. While the orcs and Forsaken are frequently demonized by rivals, he points out that goblin greed and night elven arrogance have inflicted equal harm across Kalimdor and Lordaeron.",al={"braug dimspirit philosophy","what does braug believe"}},{q="What is the Talondeep Path?",a="Talondeep Path is a prominent mountain tunnel system linking Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains with the ancient woodland borders of southern Ashenvale.",al={"what is talondeep path","talondeep cave"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The trials embody traditional tauren philosophies, valuing spiritual harmony and historical understanding above raw bloodlust.",["class:Shaman"]="Braug Dimspirit represents the shamanic worldview that reads the land's suffering through the reckless deeds of mortals, from goblin exploitation to ancient elven isolation.",["faction:Horde"]="Braug's trial forces Horde champions to reflect candidly on their own allies' reputations, reminding them that neither the orcs nor the Forsaken are solely responsible for the land's troubles."},kw={"braug dimspirit","dorn plainstalker","stonetalon mountains","talondeep path","test of lore","thousand needles","weathered nook","windshear crag"},rel={"quest:1151","quest:1149","npc:dorn-plainstalker","subzone:weathered-nook","subzone:talondeep-path","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Dorn Plainstalker",["end"]="Braug Dimspirit",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1152},src={"Test of Lore"}}
E["quest:1154"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="The Test of Lore is a trial set by Braug Dimspirit at the entrance to Talondeep Path, testing a Horde adventurer's mind rather than their physical endurance. To pass, the seeker must venture deep into the haunted barrow dens of Ashenvale, recover an ancient tome of dragon history, and study its contents before being quizzed.",h="The Test of Lore is a trial set by Braug Dimspirit at the entrance to Talondeep Path, testing a Horde...",sec={{t="A Shift in the Trials",b="After proving their physical endurance and unwavering faith across the salt flats and plateaus of Thousand Needles, candidates under Dorn Plainstalker's series of trials are sent north to Braug Dimspirit in the Stonetalon Mountains. Stationed near the mouth of Talondeep Path, Braug dismisses the earlier challenges as simple physical exercises. To truly serve the Horde with distinction, an adventurer requires a sharp and disciplined intellect, prepared to understand ancient histories rather than merely striking down beasts.",sp=0},{t="The Shadows of Dor'Danil",b="Braug directs petitioners to venture through Talondeep Path into the forested reaches of southern Ashenvale. There, hidden beneath the canopy south of Splintertree Post, lies the Dor'Danil Barrow Den. The subterranean sanctuary is a perilous ruin haunted by fallen night elf druids and the vicious creatures that slaughtered them. Rested upon a stony podium deep in the lower chambers lies the prize: 'Legacy of the Aspects', a rare manuscript detailing the ancient creation and corruption of the great Dragon Aspects.",sp=0},{t="Study or Suffer",b="Securing the tome is only half of Braug's trial. Before surrendering the volume, the seeker must commit its teachings to memory. Braug immediately takes the book upon delivery and tests the seeker's recall regarding the Titan-forged protectors and the cataclysmic betrayal that birthed Deathwing. Those who fail to study or guess poorly find themselves abruptly banished across Kalimdor to Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, forced to trek back to Stonetalon in disgrace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Braug Dimspirit?",a="Braug Dimspirit is an elder orc overseer stationed near the entrance to Talondeep Path in the Stonetalon Mountains. He serves as an examiner following Dorn Plainstalker's earlier trials, testing whether Horde champions possess the intellect and knowledge necessary to complement their raw martial prowess.",al={"braug dimspirit","who gives test of lore","stonetalon quest giver"}},{q="Where is the book Legacy of the Aspects located?",a="The book rests inside the Dor'Danil Barrow Den in southern Ashenvale, located almost directly south of Splintertree Post. It sits on a stone podium situated upon a central platform in the subterranean depths of the barrows.",al={"legacy of the aspects location","where is the book","dor danil book spot"}},{q="What lurks inside Dor'Danil Barrow Den?",a="The barrow den was once a sanctuary for night elf druids, but tragedy struck the hollows. It is now overrun by the restless spirits of dead druids and the lethal invaders that butchered them, presenting a deadly maze for any trespasser.",al={"dor danil enemies","who guards the book","ashenvale barrow den"}},{q="Why does Braug make me read the book before turning it in?",a="Braug insists on confiscating the book the moment you hand it over. Once it is in his hands, he questions you directly on its contents. If you answer incorrectly, he magically teleports you all the way to Camp Taurajo in the Barrens, forcing a long run back.",al={"why read legacy of aspects","quiz test of lore","what happens if i fail the question"},sp=1},{q="How does this quest fit into the broader trial series?",a="This trial follows the Test of Faith initiated by Dorn Plainstalker at the Weathered Nook in Thousand Needles. Where Dorn tested your nerve and survival against deadly odds, Braug assesses your lore-keeping and historical awareness.",al={"test of faith chain","what comes before test of lore","dorn plainstalker trials"}},{q="What is the subject matter of the Legacy of the Aspects?",a="The manuscript chronicles the mythic history of the Titans empowering the five great Dragon Aspects to safeguard Azeroth. Crucially, it touches upon the fall of Neltharion the Earth-Warder and his transformation into the monstrous destroyer known as Deathwing.",al={"legacy of the aspects story","book lore","what is the book about"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The trial reflects the Horde's need for warriors who can understand Kalimdor's deep history and navigate the perilous elven ruins of Ashenvale without succumbing to ignorance.",["class:Druid"]="Venturing into the Dor'Danil Barrow Den brings druidic travelers face-to-face with the tragedy of corrupted and slain night elf brethren who once slept in communion with the Emerald Dream."},kw={"ashenvale","braug dimspirit","camp taurajo","deathwing","dor'danil barrow den","dorn plainstalker","legacy of the aspects","talondeep path","test of lore"},rel={"quest:1152","quest:1149","subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den","subzone:talondeep-path","npc:dorn-plainstalker","npc:deathwing","topic:titan","subzone:camp-taurajo"},m={start="Braug Dimspirit",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1154},src={"Test of Lore (2)"}}
E["quest:1159"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="This leg of the Test of Lore sends Horde adventurers across the Great Sea to the ruins of Lordaeron. Having answered Braug Dimspirit's initial riddle in the heights of Thousand Needles, you are directed to seek a former human scholar among the Forsaken in the Undercity.",h="This leg of the Test of Lore sends Horde adventurers across the Great Sea to the ruins of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="A Scholarly Alliance",b="After proving your mettle and unraveling the history of the tauren and their centaur foes in the arid canyons of Thousand Needles, Braug Dimspirit admits his own knowledge has limits. Rather than keeping the trial confined to Kalimdor, Braug demonstrates the broad, surprising reach of the Horde's ties by pointing you toward the undead capital beneath the ruins of Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="The Sceptical Historian",b="In the damp corridors of the Apothecarium dwells Parqual Fintallas. Once an esteemed human chronicler of the northern kingdoms, Parqual's pursuit of knowledge survived the Scourge and his transformation into one of the Forsaken. Confronted by an outsider claiming to have completed the spiritual and physical trials of Thousand Needles, Parqual refuses to believe you are anything more than an opportunistic mercenary until you prove your worth to him directly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does a tauren trial send me all the way to Undercity?",a="Braug Dimspirit acknowledges that true mastery of lore extends beyond the history of Kalimdor. He directs you to Parqual Fintallas, a renowned human scholar whose knowledge survived the fall of Lordaeron into undeath, to test your understanding of broader world history.",al={"why go to undercity","why lordaeron","braug sending to undead"}},{q="Where exactly is Parqual Fintallas located?",a="Parqual Fintallas resides in the Undercity, specifically standing along the southern bridge in the Apothecarium quarter.",al={"where is parqual","parqual location","find fintallas"}},{q="Who was Parqual Fintallas in life?",a="In life, Parqual Fintallas was an accomplished human historian within the kingdom of Lordaeron. After succumbing to the Plague of Undeath and joining Sylvanas's Forsaken, he maintained his scholarly pursuits, turning his intellect toward different, darker inquiries.",al={"parqual fintallas lore","who is parqual","fintallas backstory"}},{q="Why doesn't Parqual believe Braug sent me?",a="Parqual is deeply skeptical of outsiders. He finds it incredible that an ordinary adventurer could leap from the spires of Thousand Needles, defeat primeval elementals, and retrieve ancient relics, assuming instead you merely overheard rumors in a tavern.",al={"why is parqual rude","parqual reaction","parqual doesn't believe me"}},{q="What larger trial is this quest part of?",a="This quest is the midpoint of the Test of Lore chain, which itself evolved out of the trial initiated by Dorn Plainstalker at the Weathered Nook. It assesses whether an initiate possesses not just combat prowess and courage, but the intellect and historical awareness worthy of a Horde champion.",al={"what chain is this","test of faith chain","what is test of lore"}},{q="What comes next after reaching Parqual?",a="Before Parqual will deign to ask you his own historical riddle, he demands you undertake an errand on his behalf in the Eastern Kingdoms to verify that you are truly the capable hero Braug claims you to be.",al={"what next after parqual","next quest after undercity","after talking to fintallas"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Meeting Parqual highlights that despite their rot and undeath, Forsaken scholars like him retained the vast academic traditions and records of the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron.",["race:Tauren"]="For a tauren initiate, leaving the open plains and high mesas of Kalimdor to navigate the poisonous, claustrophobic sewers of Undercity makes this journey as much a cultural trial as a historical one.",["faction:Horde"]="This quest demonstrates the cross-continental cooperation binding the newly forged Horde, pairing tauren wisdom seekers with the grim archivists of Lordaeron."},kw={"apothecarium","braug dimspirit","dorn plainstalker","lordaeron","parqual fintallas","test of lore","thousand needles","undercity","weathered nook"},rel={"quest:1152","npc:parqual-fintallas","zone:undercity","subzone:apothecarium","quest:1149","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:weathered-nook","npc:dorn-plainstalker"},m={start="Braug Dimspirit",["end"]="Parqual Fintallas",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1159},src={"Test of Lore (4)"}}
E["quest:1176"] = {t="quest",n="Load Lightening",z="thousandneedles",s="Pozzik, the head goblin engineer out at the Mirage Raceway, needs materials to shave critical ounces off his rocket-car chassis. Rather than relying purely on heavy metal plating, the goblins salvage hollow bones from local desert vultures to build sturdy, ultralight steering and structural rigs.",h="Pozzik, the head goblin engineer out at the Mirage Raceway, needs materials to shave critical ounces off his...",sec={{t="Every Ounce Counts",b="Across the blinding white expanse of the Shimmering Flats, the rivalry between goblin and gnomish engineers is decided by fractions of a second. Raw engine thrust is useless if a racer is weighed down by excessive bulk. While gnome teams obsess over intricate gears and brass fittings, the goblin crew led by Pozzik seeks ruthless pragmatic efficiency: stripping out dense iron framing and replacing it with lighter, hollow structural components wherever the frame permits.",sp=0},{t="Desert Scavenging for Speed",b="Rather than shipping expensive, specialized composites out to Thousand Needles, Pozzik turns to the surrounding salt wastes. Salt Flats vultures are plentiful, their skeletons honed by flight to possess hollow, honeycombed cores that provide great tensile strength with almost no mass. By substituting worked vulture bones into the racer's steering rig and minor braces, Pozzik's mechanics aim to keep their machines nimble enough to outmaneuver the gnomes without shaking apart at top speed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Pozzik want vulture bones for a race car?",a="Goblin engineering favors ingenuity and opportunistic materials. Vulture bones are hollow and naturally lightweight, offering an ideal strength-to-weight ratio to reinforce delicate parts like steering rigs without weighing down the racer.",al={"vulture bones purpose","why bones","pozzik bones"}},{q="Who is Pozzik?",a="Pozzik is the lead goblin racing mechanic and team leader stationed at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. He directs the goblin pits against their bitter rivals, the gnomes.",al={"pozzik","pozzik lore","who is the goblin engineer"}},{q="Where are these vultures found?",a="The scavengers and vultures circle the open expanse of the Shimmering Flats, particularly around the gigantic skeletal remains scattered in the northeastern stretches of the salt basin.",al={"vulture location","where to find hollow bones","shimmering flats scavengers"}},{q="What is the Mirage Raceway?",a="The Mirage Raceway is a neutral racing ground established on the expansive dry salt lake of Thousand Needles. Goblins and gnomes compete there in high-speed, dangerous experimental rocket-car races.",al={"raceway lore","what is mirage raceway","shimmering flats track"}},{q="Are the gnomes doing the same thing?",a="While the gnomes also look for ways to streamline their racers, their engineering tradition leans toward precision clockwork and complex metals rather than the goblins' scrappy, salvage-based modifications.",al={"gnome racers","gnome vs goblin","are gnomes using bones"}},{q="Does this work help with Pozzik's larger racing effort?",a="Yes. Proving your reliability by lightening the racer earns Pozzik's trust, leading to further work involving track rivalries and official goblin sponsorship out on the flats.",al={"quest continuation","what comes next","goblin sponsorship"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Pozzik's reliance on avian bone frames showcases quintessential goblin ingenuity: functional, improvised, and surprisingly effective at reducing curb weight.",["race:Gnome"]="Watching goblins literally lash scavenged bird carcasses into mechanical steering rigs is bound to scandalize any classically trained Tinker Town engineer."},kw={"bones","load lightening","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","vulture"},rel={"npc:pozzik","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin"},m={start="Pozzik",level="30",faction="Neutral",id=1176},src={"Load Lightening"}}
E["quest:1179"] = {t="quest",n="The Brassbolts Brothers",z="thousandneedles",s="Pilot Longbeard in Ironforge needs a courier to deliver a crate of reinforced siege engine helmets across the sea to Kalimdor. His friends, the Brassbolts brothers, are testing high-speed rocket cars in the Shimmering Flats and urgently need head protection for their accident-prone test drivers.",h="Pilot Longbeard in Ironforge needs a courier to deliver a crate of reinforced siege engine helmets across the...",sec={{t="A Long-Distance Favor",b="While stationed among his aerial machinery in Ironforge, the dwarven aviator Pilot Longbeard received an urgent request from the Shimmering Flats in southern Kalimdor. His friends, a pair of inventive gnomes known as the Brassbolts brothers, had taken up residence on the vast salt pans to race experimental machinery. Longbeard is tied down by military and piloting duties, leaving him unable to deliver the supplies himself.",sp=0},{t="Safety at High Velocity",b="The Brassbolts' rocket car has turned out to be extraordinarily fast—so fast that their test drivers keep wiping out across the salt beds and suffering severe concussions. Longbeard procures a crate of heavy-duty dwarven Siege Engine helmets to protect their craniums. Delivering the crate gives the gnomes the leverage they need to coax reluctant pilots back behind the wheel of their volatile speed machine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pilot Longbeard?",a="Pilot Longbeard is a dwarven aviator located in Ironforge. An acquaintance of the Brassbolts brothers, he acts as their supply contact back in the Eastern Kingdoms, procuring heavy dwarven gear they cannot easily manufacture out in the field.",al={"pilot longbeard","quest giver","who gives this quest"}},{q="Who are the Brassbolts brothers?",a="The Brassbolts brothers, including Wizzle Brassbolts, are ambitious gnomish engineers who established a presence at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. They spend their days designing and tuning cutting-edge rocket cars to outrace goblin competitors.",al={"brassbolts brothers","wizzle brassbolts","gnome brothers"}},{q="Where is the Shimmering Flats?",a="The Shimmering Flats is an expansive, sun-baked salt plain located in southern Kalimdor, past the tall canyon pillars of Thousand Needles. Its sheer, obstacle-free expanse makes it an ideal proving ground for experimental high-speed vehicles.",al={"shimmering flats location","where to deliver","where is race track"}},{q="Why do the gnomes need Siege Engine helmets?",a="The Brassbolts' rocket car achieves immense speeds, but its steering and stability leave much to be desired. Driver crashes and concussions became so frequent that no test pilots were willing to get behind the wheel without substantial dwarven head protection.",al={"why helmets","crash helmets","rocket car crashes"}},{q="Why doesn't Longbeard deliver them himself?",a="Pilot Longbeard is tied down by his military obligations and duties in Ironforge. Because making the long voyage across the Great Sea to southern Kalimdor would abandon his post, he relies on traveling adventurers to haul the heavy crate.",al={"why not longbeard","longbeard duties"}},{q="Can Horde players complete this task?",a="No. This quest originates with Pilot Longbeard in the Alliance capital of Ironforge and is exclusive to Alliance couriers, although the Mirage Raceway itself welcomes both factions.",al={"is this alliance only","horde version","faction"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The Brassbolts' pursuit of pure velocity showcases classic gnomish ambition, where mechanical innovation takes absolute precedence over minor details like braking and driver longevity.",["race:Dwarf"]="Only sturdy dwarven Siege Engine armor is thick enough to survive a full-throttle gnomish rocket collision out on the salt flats.",["profession:Engineering"]="A quintessential engineering supply run, bridging dwarven heavy-armor craftsmanship with gnomish high-velocity propulsion experiments."},kw={"brassbolts","ironforge","mirage raceway","pilot longbeard","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","wizzle brassbolts"},rel={"npc:wizzle-brassbolts","npc:pilot-longbeard","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},m={start="Pilot Longbeard",["end"]="Wizzle Brassbolts",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1179},src={"The Brassbolts Brothers"}}
E["quest:1950"] = {t="quest",n="Get the Scoop",z="thousandneedles",s="Magus Tirth has locked a crucial spellbook inside his magically sealed strongbox, but he cannot recall the activation phrase to open it. To retrieve the tome, you must locate his missing apprentice somewhere around the Shimmering Flats racetrack and pry the forgotten words from him.",h="Magus Tirth has locked a crucial spellbook inside his magically sealed strongbox, but he cannot recall the...",sec={{t="A Magus and His Memory",b="Magus Tirth is an eccentric spellcaster dwelling on the cracked salt bed of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles. While he possesses the esoteric knowledge and tomes that advancing mages desperately seek, dealing with him requires patience. Tirth relies heavily on an assistant to manage mundane details, including the spoken passwords guarding his arcane repositories. When tasked with retrieving a book of power, visiting practitioners quickly learn that Tirth has locked the volume away behind magic words that have slipped his mind entirely.",sp=0},{t="Fowl Play",b="Tracking down Tirth's apprentice, Johnson, is not a matter of simply wandering the paddocks of the Mirage Raceway. After asking around the goblins and gnomes running the track, one discovers that Johnson has suffered the quintessential occupational hazard of serving an erratic wizard: transfiguration. Cursed by his master into the form of a common chicken, Johnson wanders the salt flats, unable to speak until a passing traveler draws near and breaks the magical haze long enough for him to squawk out the missing password.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Magus Tirth?",a="Magus Tirth is a reclusive human wizard stationed near the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles. He possesses advanced arcane lore sought out by mages looking to hone their craft.",al={"tirth lore","who is magus tirth","tirth shimmer flats"}},{q="Why does Tirth need the password to his own box?",a="Tirth magically locked his strongbox using a spoken phrase, relying on his assistant to remember mundane details like passwords. True to his absent-minded nature, he forgot the words as soon as his apprentice vanished.",al={"why tirth forgot","tirth strongbox password"}},{q="Where did the apprentice go?",a="Johnson did not flee far. He is wandering near the racetrack east of Tirth's camp, though locating him is complicated by the fact that Tirth turned him into a chicken.",al={"find tirth assistant","where is apprentice johnson","johnson location"},sp=1},{q="Why was the apprentice turned into a chicken?",a="Tirth placed a curse on Johnson before forgetting he had done so. Upon learning the fate of his assistant, Tirth vaguely assumes the apprentice deserved it for being an ungrateful pupil.",al={"why johnson chicken","tirth polymorph apprentice"},sp=1},{q="What is inside Tirth's strongbox?",a="The magically sealed chest holds a book containing rituals and instructions essential for a mage's continuing education and magical implements.",al={"tirth strongbox contents","what book is in the chest"}},{q="Who can undertake this task?",a="This errand is part of a dedicated trial meant exclusively for mages seeking specialized instruction and materials to craft a potent wand.",al={"can non mages do get the scoop","is this quest mage only"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Dealing with Tirth offers a humorous yet cautionary glimpse into the perils of polymorph curses and the absent-mindedness that can afflict powerful scholars."},kw={"get the scoop","johnson","magus tirth","mirage raceway","shimmering flats","strongbox","thousand needles","wand quest"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:drag"},m={start="Magus Tirth",level="30",faction="Neutral",id=1950},src={"Get the Scoop"}}
E["quest:4542"] = {t="quest",n="Message to Freewind Post",z="thousandneedles",s="Message to Freewind Post is a Horde quest tasking travelers with carrying urgent dispatches from Brave Moonhorn near the border lifts down into Thousand Needles. The missive warns Cliffwatcher Longhorn of intensifying centaur raids against local caravans. It also raises early concerns regarding the suspicious, standoffish behavior of the neighboring Grimtotem clan.",h="Message to Freewind Post is a Horde quest tasking travelers with carrying urgent dispatches from Brave...",sec={{t="A Warning Down the Canyon",b="Standing watch near the canyon's western approaches, Brave Moonhorn keeps a vigil over the roads leading down into Thousand Needles. With centaur aggression abruptly spiking, communication between border sentries and the regional leadership is vital. Moonhorn entrusts passing Horde adventurers with carrying an urgent dispatch southeast to Cliffwatcher Longhorn, the commander stationed atop the mesa settlement of Freewind Post.",sp=0},{t="Rising Perils and Uneasy Kin",b="Upon receiving the message, Longhorn confirms the dire situation: a recent supply caravan was intercepted and slaughtered by marauding centaur, leaving Freewind Post in desperate need of retaliation and defense. Just as concerning is Moonhorn's parting caution to avoid the local Grimtotem tauren, whose uncharacteristically bizarre and hostile demeanor hints at deeper rifts brewing across the arid flats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the message to Freewind Post?",a="Brave Moonhorn, a tauren scout keeping watch along the western entrance to Thousand Needles, gives you the urgent missive to deliver.",al={"quest giver","who starts message to freewind post","brave moonhorn"}},{q="Who receives the urgent message?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn receives the message atop the towering mesa settlement of Freewind Post, located southeast of the Great Lift.",al={"where to turn in","cliffwatcher longhorn location","freewind post leader"}},{q="What does the urgent message report?",a="The message alerts Freewind Post to a sudden increase in centaur attacks and caravan harassment along the trails below.",al={"message contents","what is the message about"}},{q="Why is Brave Moonhorn worried about the Grimtotem?",a="Moonhorn notes that the nearby Grimtotem clan members have been acting strange and distant toward other tauren, advising travelers to steer clear of them.",al={"grimtotem warning","why avoid grimtotem"}},{q="What happens after Longhorn reads the message?",a="Enraged by the slaughter of a recent supply caravan, Cliffwatcher Longhorn immediately orders retaliatory action against the local centaur in the follow-up mission, Pacify the Centaur.",al={"next quest","after message to freewind post"}},{q="How do you reach Freewind Post from the canyon floor?",a="Follow the main canyon road east until you reach the base of the massive needle mesa, then ride the wooden platform lift directly up into the village.",al={"getting to freewind post","how to get up freewind post"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren, the centaur have been ancestral, bitter rivals for generations. Moonhorn's warning serves as a grim reminder that their ancient enemies still hunt the trails of Kalimdor, even as tensions with the reclusive Grimtotem clan simmer.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post serves as the Horde's vital lifeline across the expanse of Thousand Needles. Keeping the communication lines open between outpost watchers and the settlement's leadership is critical to securing the desert trade routes."},kw={"brave moonhorn","centaur","cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","grimtotem","message to freewind post","thousand needles","urgent message"},rel={"npc:brave-moonhorn","npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","subzone:freewind-post","quest:4841","quest:5064","topic:centaur","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Brave Moonhorn",["end"]="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",level="25",faction="Horde",id=4542},src={"Message to Freewind Post"}}
E["quest:4767"] = {t="quest",n="Wind Rider",z="thousandneedles",s="Wind Rider is a Horde quest offered by Elu atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Aspiring to become a wind rider himself, Elu tasks adventurers with climbing into the craggy heights of Highperch to gather wild wyvern eggs to bolster the Horde's aerial mount reserves.",h="Wind Rider is a Horde quest offered by Elu atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="The Call of the Sky",b="Across Kalimdor, the Horde relies heavily on wind riders to ferry couriers, scouts, and warriors across vast distances. At Freewind Post, a young tauren named Elu aspires to join their esteemed ranks. With the demands of the expanding Horde outpacing the availability of mounts, Elu has been charged with helping procure new wyverns to supply the master wind riders, offering eager travelers a chance to assist in this vital effort.",sp=0},{t="Ascending Highperch",b="Highperch rises atop the towering mesas of Thousand Needles, serving as a prime nesting ground for wild wyverns. Gathering viable eggs requires braving the cliffs and facing the fiercely protective adults that patrol the roosts. By securing these clutches, Elu hopes to prove his dedication and begin the rigorous process of hand-raising and training wyverns for the Horde's flight masters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="The quest is given by Elu, an aspiring wind rider located atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",al={"wind rider quest giver","who starts wind rider","elu location"}},{q="What does Elu need?",a="Elu asks you to bring him ten Highperch Wyvern Eggs gathered directly from the nests in Highperch.",al={"wind rider objectives","what do i collect","wyvern eggs"}},{q="Where is Highperch located?",a="Highperch is an elevated mesa plateau located northwest of Freewind Post, or just south of Whitereach Post. A natural ramp marked by a totem pole leads up from the canyon floor to the nesting grounds.",al={"how to get to highperch","highperch entrance","where are wyvern eggs"}},{q="Why is the Horde gathering wild wyvern eggs?",a="The Horde's master wind riders are facing growing demand for aerial mounts across their outposts, and captive breeding alone cannot keep up. Raising wyverns from wild clutches allows handlers to train fresh mounts to meet their transport and scouting needs.",al={"why harvest wyvern eggs","lore behind wyvern eggs"}},{q="Are the wild wyverns hostile?",a="Yes. Wild wyverns are fiercely territorial and protective of their broods, readily attacking anyone who approaches their clutches on Highperch.",al={"will wyverns attack","wyvern danger"}},{q="What does Elu intend to do with the eggs?",a="Elu hopes that delivering the eggs will allow him to begin formal wind rider training, raising and bonding with the creatures to serve the Horde in the skies.",al={"elu wyverns","what happens to the eggs"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Wyverns form the backbone of the Horde's transit network in Kalimdor, making the replenishment of their stables critical for frontier communication and defense.",["race:Tauren"]="The wind riders of Freewind Post take pride in their mastery of aerial flight, viewing the stewardship and training of wyverns as an honorable pursuit.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters familiar with taming and beast temperament will appreciate the peril and precision required to snatch wild clutches directly from a territorial predator's nest."},kw={"elu","freewind post","highperch","thousand needles","wind rider","wyvern eggs"},rel={"npc:elu","subzone:highperch","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde","quest:92472"},m={start="Elu",level="29",faction="Horde",id=4767},src={"Wind Rider (quest)"}}
E["quest:4770"] = {t="quest",n="Homeward Bound",z="thousandneedles",s="Homeward Bound is a Horde quest that tasks adventurers with rescuing Pao'ka Swiftmountain, a young tauren naturalist stranded in the wyvern nesting grounds of Highperch. After getting separated and lost while studying the dangerous beasts, Pao'ka must be escorted safely down the cliffs back toward Whitereach Post.",h="Homeward Bound is a Horde quest that tasks adventurers with rescuing Pao'ka Swiftmountain, a young tauren...",sec={{t="A Naturalist in Over His Head",b="Pao'ka Swiftmountain accompanied the elder Motega Firemane from Mulgore to Thousand Needles to study the unique wildlife of the canyon floor and its towering stone pillars. Driven by curiosity and overconfidence, Pao'ka crept alone into the heights of Highperch to observe the local wyverns firsthand. The territorial beasts drove him off, leaving the young scholar stranded, terrified, and hiding among the crags for days.",sp=0},{t="The Path Down the Crags",b="Highperch is thick with aggressive wyverns fiercely guarding their clutches and high roosts. Escorting Pao'ka back to level ground requires carving a path straight through the nesting predators. Unprepared for open combat, the panicked youth relies entirely on passing Horde travelers to fend off the swarming wyverns until he reaches the relative safety of the canyon path leading east.",sp=0},{t="Relief and Reckoning",b="Reaching the base of the cliffs allows Pao'ka to scramble safely home to Whitereach Post. His guardian, Motega Firemane, is stunned to learn what transpired. Motega had promised Pao'ka's hesitant father that he would look after the boy during their field studies. Relieved that Pao'ka survived his foolish expedition, Motega rewards his saviors while privately lamenting that he did not chain the reckless apprentice to a totem.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Pao'ka Swiftmountain?",a="Pao'ka Swiftmountain is a young tauren apprentice who traveled to Thousand Needles with Motega Firemane to document and study wild creatures. His youthful enthusiasm led him to wander into Highperch unsupervised.",al={"paoka","pao'ka","who is the escort npc"}},{q="Why was Pao'ka hiding in Highperch?",a="He ventured into the roosts alone to get a closer look at the native wyverns and their nests. The aggressive beasts attacked him, forcing him into hiding and leaving him trapped on the high mesa.",al={"why is paoka in highperch","what happened to paoka","why is he stuck"}},{q="Who is Motega Firemane?",a="Motega Firemane is a tauren naturalist stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. He was entrusted by Pao'ka's father to oversee the youth's safety during their scientific expedition.",al={"motega","who is motega firemane","quest turn in npc"}},{q="Where is Highperch located?",a="Highperch is an elevated mesa and wyvern nesting ground situated in the western expanse of Thousand Needles, just west of Whitereach Post and south of Freewind Post.",al={"highperch location","where is highperch","where do i escort him from"}},{q="Where is Whitereach Post?",a="Whitereach Post is a small Horde encampment located east of Highperch in Thousand Needles, serving as a field base for tauren naturalists studying the canyon's fauna.",al={"whitereach location","where is whitereach post"}},{q="Does Motega know Pao'ka was missing?",a="No. Pao'ka snuck away to Highperch on his own without telling Motega, which is why Motega was completely unaware of the danger his apprentice was in until you report the rescue.",al={"did motega know","why didn't motega search for him"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The bond between tribes and elders is paramount among the tauren; Motega's deep responsibility to Pao'ka's father highlights the close communal obligations that guide their expeditions.",["faction:Horde"]="Wyverns are essential allies and mounts for the Horde across Kalimdor, making the wild specimens of Highperch an area of great natural and strategic curiosity."},kw={"escort","highperch","homeward bound","motega firemane","pao'ka swiftmountain","thousand needles","whitereach post","wyvern"},rel={"npc:pao-ka-swiftmountain","npc:motega-firemane","subzone:highperch","subzone:whitereach-post","quest:4767","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren"},m={start="Pao'ka Swiftmountain",["end"]="Motega Firemane",level="29",faction="Horde",id=4770},src={"Homeward Bound"}}
E["quest:4821"] = {t="quest",n="Alien Egg",z="thousandneedles",s="Rumors among the tauren of Freewind Post speak of a bizarre, foreign egg guarded fiercely by wild serpents on the canyon floor. Hagar Lightninghoof tasks Horde adventurers with tracking down and retrieving the specimen before whatever lurks inside breaks free.",h="Rumors among the tauren of Freewind Post speak of a bizarre, foreign egg guarded fiercely by wild serpents on...",sec={{t="A Strange Nest",b="Word reached Freewind Post of an unusual egg spotted deep in the serpent dens that dot the canyon floor beneath the towering stone needles. The serpents native to the canyon watch over the egg as though it were their own brood, striking out at any traveler who ventures too close. Intrigued and wary of what might threaten the local hunting grounds, Hagar Lightninghoof asks brave scouts to locate the clutch, bypass the slithering sentries, and secure the oddity for study.",sp=0},{t="The Hatchling Awakens",b="Upon inspecting the retrieved egg closely, Hagar discovers far more than an ordinary reptilian clutch. The shell fractures immediately upon handling, unleashing a juvenile winged monstrosity known as a Young Arikara. Rather than attacking, the newborn creature bursts skyward, fleeing the wooden platforms of Freewind Post and signaling that far deeper primordial forces stir within the canyon winds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can the Alien Egg be found?",a="The egg rests within one of several serpent nests scattered along the cliff bases of Thousand Needles, particularly to the south and northeast of Freewind Post. It sits directly on the canyon floor, surrounded by hostile native serpents.",al={"alien egg location","where is alien egg","egg spawn thousand needles"}},{q="Why are the local serpents guarding it?",a="Though the egg belongs to a distinct flying serpent known as Arikara, the canyon's common serpents instinctively protect it as if it were a member of their own clutch, aggressively defending the nest from any curious intruders.",al={"why do serpents protect the egg","serpent behavior alien egg"},sp=1},{q="Who is Hagar Lightninghoof?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof is a tauren scout and warden stationed high atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. He keeps watch over unusual movements and ecological threats across the canyon floor, coordinating Horde efforts to manage local beasts.",al={"hagar lightninghoof lore","who is quest giver hagar"}},{q="What happens when you deliver the egg?",a="When Hagar begins to examine the egg, it cracks open to reveal a Young Arikara. The winged serpent briefly startles Hagar before taking flight and escaping into the skies of Thousand Needles.",al={"what hatches from alien egg","what is inside the egg"},sp=1},{q="What does this quest lead to?",a="Delivering the egg begins the Arikara chain, immediately leading to the quest 'Serpent Wild', where Hagar seeks to understand the nature of the strange winged serpents rising in the canyon.",al={"next quest after alien egg","arikara chain next step"},sp=1},{q="Is the egg literally from outer space?",a="In this context, 'alien' refers to something wholly foreign, unnatural, and unfamiliar to the local ecology of Thousand Needles rather than a star-traveling organism. It belongs to the legendary wind serpent Arikara.",al={"is alien egg extraterrestrial","is egg alien"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Living above the canyon floor on Freewind Post, the tauren rely on understanding the delicate balance of the wildlife below; an invasive or unnatural serpent brood poses a direct disruption to their home.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters familiar with the beasts of Kalimdor will immediately recognize that the brood nests in the canyon harbor something far more primordial than common desert serpents.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post serves as the Horde's primary outpost in Thousand Needles, making the containment of emerging apex predators a key priority for defending supply lines."},kw={"alien egg","arikara","freewind post","hagar lightninghoof","serpent den","serpent wild","serpents","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:hagar-lightninghoof","quest:4865","quest:5088","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Hagar Lightninghoof",level="26",faction="Horde",id=4821},src={"Alien Egg (quest)"}}
E["quest:4841"] = {t="quest",n="Pacify The Centaur",z="thousandneedles",s="Pacify the Centaur is a retaliatory hunting mission issued by Cliffwatcher Longhorn atop Freewind Post. Charged with clearing the threat gathering beneath the canyon spires, Horde adventurers strike deep into the Galak centaur encampments of Splithoof Crag.",h="Pacify the Centaur is a retaliatory hunting mission issued by Cliffwatcher Longhorn atop Freewind Post.",sec={{t="A Threat on the Canyon Floor",b="Perched upon its precarious desert mesa, Freewind Post grants the tauren a commanding vantage over the canyon floor of Thousand Needles. However, that high ground offers little peace when hostile enemies mass directly beneath the ropes and elevators. The Galak centaur have established a sprawling war camp nestled directly north along the canyon wall at Splithoof Crag, directly menacing supply lines and tauren movement through the needles.",sp=0},{t="Retaliation and Bloodshed",b="To counter the growing danger, Cliffwatcher Longhorn sends capable Horde travelers to thin the Galak ranks through unsparing violence. Rather than merely defending the access lifts, the tauren believe the only way to safeguard Freewind Post is to break the centaur vanguard in their own camp. Taking down their scouts, beast-wranglers, and windchaser mystics is meant to blunt any concerted assault on the post before it can begin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Pacify the Centaur?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn gives the quest atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. He serves as one of the post's key defenders, monitoring the dangers lurking across the surrounding salt flats and canyons.",al={"quest giver","who starts pacify the centaur","cliffwatcher longhorn"}},{q="Where are the Galak centaur located?",a="The Galak centaur are encamped directly north of Freewind Post up against the northern cliff wall of Thousand Needles, in an area designated as Splithoof Crag.",al={"galak camp location","where is splithoof crag","centaur location"}},{q="Why do the tauren want the centaur killed?",a="The centaur have long waged a brutal, genocidal war against the nomadic tauren across central Kalimdor. With the Galak clan establishing a forward camp right at the foot of Freewind Post, Cliffwatcher Longhorn demands swift retribution to ensure the safety of the Horde's desert stronghold.",al={"why kill centaur","tauren centaur conflict","why revenge"}},{q="What kinds of centaur need to be slain?",a="The quest tasks you with hunting down twelve Galak Scouts, ten Galak Wranglers, and six Galak Windchasers from their encampment at Splithoof Crag.",al={"galak targets","which centaur to kill","quest objectives"}},{q="What comes after completing Pacify the Centaur?",a="Once the Galak ranks are thinned, Cliffwatcher Longhorn turns his attention toward other regional threats, directing you into the follow-up mission Grimtotem Spying.",al={"next quest","what follows pacify the centaur","quest chain after centaur"}},{q="What pre-requisite leads into this mission?",a="The mission opens up following the delivery quest Message to Freewind Post, which directs travelers to report directly to Cliffwatcher Longhorn.",al={"prereq","previous quest","how to unlock pacify the centaur"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the shu'halo, the sight of centaur camps encroaching upon a settlement triggers memories of generational slaughter. Thinning the Galak is a matter of pure cultural survival.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post is the Horde's vital lifeline connecting the Southern Barrens and the shimmering salt flats of the Great Lift. Leaving aggressive centaur beneath its towers endangers every caravan traversing the zone."},kw={"cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","galak scout","galak windchaser","galak wrangler","pacify the centaur","splithoof crag","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:splithoof-crag","zone:thousandneedles","quest:4542","quest:5064","topic:centaur"},m={start="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",level="25",faction="Horde",id=4841},src={"Pacify the Centaur"}}
E["quest:4865"] = {t="quest",n="Serpent Wild",z="thousandneedles",s="Serpent Wild is a Horde quest in Thousand Needles that connects the discovery of strange alien eggs to ancient tauren legends. Following an unsettling revelation at Freewind Post, Hagar Lightninghoof dispatches adventurers northwest to Motega Firemane at Whitereach Post to confront the awakening of Arikara.",h="Serpent Wild is a Horde quest in Thousand Needles that connects the discovery of strange alien eggs to...",sec={{t="A Legend Made Flesh",b="When strange, unnatural eggs began appearing in Thousand Needles, local tauren feared an ecological disaster. However, inspecting the artifacts reveals something far older and more ominous than ordinary predators: signs pointing to the vengeance spirit Arikara. Stunned by the horrifying confirmation, Hagar Lightninghoof realizes the canyon faces a mythical threat long thought relegated to fireside lore.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Whitereach",b="Recognizing that the threat surpasses simple physical defense, Hagar urges immediate council with Motega Firemane. Stationed northwest along the canyon floor at Whitereach Post, Motega serves as a watcher and spiritual guide versed in the traditional omens of the Needles. His guidance is essential if the Horde hopes to understand and appease or destroy the rising vengeance spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Serpent Wild?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof, located high atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, offers the quest immediately after you investigate the strange alien eggs found throughout the canyon.",al={"who gives serpent wild","serpent wild questgiver","hagar lightninghoof quest"}},{q="Where is Motega Firemane located?",a="Motega Firemane resides at Whitereach Post, a small tauren camp situated along the road northwest of Freewind Post, past the fork that leads toward the Great Lift.",al={"where is motega firemane","motega firemane location","find motega"}},{q="Who or what is Arikara?",a="Arikara is a legendary wind serpent spirit embodying vengeance in tauren mythology, whose rumored presence in Thousand Needles poses a dire spiritual and physical threat to the local tribes.",al={"what is arikara","arikara lore","legend of arikara"}},{q="What prerequisite must be finished before taking this quest?",a="You must complete the quest Alien Egg, wherein you recover an unusual egg from the wild beasts of the canyon and deliver it to Hagar Lightninghoof for inspection.",al={"prereq for serpent wild","alien egg quest chain","serpent wild unlock"}},{q="What happens after reaching Motega Firemane?",a="Speaking with Motega unlocks the quest Sacred Fire, starting the ritual preparations necessary to confront the spirit Arikara.",al={"what comes after serpent wild","serpent wild follow up","sacred fire quest"}},{q="Why is Hagar Lightninghoof so alarmed?",a="Hagar believed the tales of Arikara were mere stories. Actually seeing evidence of the vengeance spirit's manifestation in the canyon terrifies him, prompting him to send for elder wisdom immediately.",al={"why is hagar scared","hagar wiping brow","hagar reaction"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The awakening of Arikara turns folklore into urgent crisis, testing the spiritual stewardship of the tauren defending Thousand Needles.",["class:Shaman"]="Disturbances of vengeful spirits like Arikara highlight the delicate balance of elemental and spiritual forces inhabiting the canyon mesas.",["faction:Horde"]="Keeping the supply lines open through Thousand Needles requires resolving mystical threats that could terrorize the road between the Great Lift and Feralas."},kw={"arikara","freewind post","hagar lightninghoof","motega firemane","sacred fire","serpent wild","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"npc:hagar-lightninghoof","npc:motega-firemane","subzone:whitereach-post","subzone:freewind-post","quest:5062","quest:5088","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:great-lift"},m={start="Hagar Lightninghoof",["end"]="Motega Firemane",level="26",faction="Horde",id=4865},src={"Serpent Wild"}}
E["quest:4881"] = {t="quest",n="Protect Kanati Greycloud",z="thousandneedles",s="Protect Kanati Greycloud is a Horde quest at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. After discovering that centaur marauders have targeted the tauren scout, adventurers must make a stand beside him and repel a squad of Galak assassins.",h="Protect Kanati Greycloud is a Horde quest at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="An Ambush Revealed",b="While stationed among the towering sandstone spires of Whitereach Post, the tauren scout Kanati Greycloud uncovers evidence of an assassination plot directed squarely at his life. The Galak tribe of centaur, relentless in their hostility toward the nomadic tauren and their Horde allies, are not content merely raiding supply paths; they seek to eliminate key sentries and scouts watching their movements.",sp=0},{t="Defending Whitereach Post",b="Realizing the attack is imminent and suspecting the enemy forces might outnumber his initial estimates, Kanati asks travelers at the post to fight alongside him. When the Galak assassins strike, Kanati stands his ground, relying on allied blades and spells to break the ambush before the centaur can claim their prize.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kanati Greycloud?",a="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren scout stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. He keeps watch over the canyon floor and monitors the movements of hostile native threats, particularly the local centaur clans.",al={"who is kanati","kanati greycloud lore","who is the quest giver"}},{q="Why are the centaur trying to assassinate him?",a="The local Galak centaur view the tauren and their Horde encampments as encroaching enemies on their canyon territory. By targeting Kanati, the centaur hope to remove an observant scout who tracks their activities and interferes with their plans.",al={"why do centaur attack kanati","centaur assassination reason","assassination plot why"}},{q="Where does this defense take place?",a="The ambush takes place directly at Whitereach Post, a small Horde-affiliated outpost situated along the canyon paths of Thousand Needles.",al={"where is this quest","protect kanati location","where does the ambush happen"}},{q="Which centaur clan attacks Kanati Greycloud?",a="The assassins belong to the Galak tribe, the prominent centaur clan inhabiting the canyons and ravines of Thousand Needles.",al={"what tribe attacks","who are the assassins","which centaur"}},{q="What happens after the assassins are defeated?",a="With the Galak assassins slain, Kanati's life is preserved and Whitereach Post remains secure. Kanati thanks his defenders for standing with him through the surprise assault, successfully concluding the defensive chain.",al={"what happens next","quest follow up","after protecting kanati"},sp=1},{q="Does Kanati Greycloud fight in the battle?",a="Yes. Kanati does not cower or flee; he actively joins the fray alongside whoever answers his plea, fighting to repel the assassins that came to end his vigil.",al={"does kanati help","kanati fighting","is kanati passive"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The blood feud between the tauren and the centaur runs deep, making the defense of a fellow tribesman from cowardly assassination a matter of survival and honor.",["faction:Horde"]="Whitereach Post serves as a critical vantage point in Thousand Needles, and keeping sentries like Kanati alive is vital to securing Horde operations throughout the canyon."},kw={"assassination plot","assassins","centaur","galak","kanati greycloud","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"npc:kanati-greycloud","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Kanati Greycloud",level="28",faction="Horde",id=4881},src={"Protect Kanati Greycloud"}}
E["quest:4904"] = {t="quest",n="Free At Last",z="thousandneedles",s="Free at Last is a rescue mission atop the windswept spires of Darkcloud Pinnacle. Lakota Windsong, a tauren woman held captive by Arnak Grimtotem, needs protection as she flees her captor's stronghold and returns to her friend Thalia Amberhide at Freewind Post.",h="Free at Last is a rescue mission atop the windswept spires of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",sec={{t="A Brutal Abduction",b="The Grimtotem clan's aggressive presence in Thousand Needles is not limited to skirmishes over land. Arnak Grimtotem sought to take Lakota Windsong as his bride, but when she refused his advances, he chose violence. Arnak returned in the night, struck down Lakota's brother when he tried to defend her, and dragged her away to Darkcloud Pinnacle.",sp=0},{t="Escape from Darkcloud Pinnacle",b="Perched across the high wooden suspension bridges above Thousand Needles, Darkcloud Pinnacle is swarming with hostile Grimtotem warriors. Escorting Lakota requires navigating the descent while fighting off waves of Grimtotem bandits intent on recapturing her before she reaches the canyon floor.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Homecoming",b="Once safely down from the pinnacle, Lakota makes her way back to the safety of Freewind Post. Her companion, Thalia Amberhide, receives the news with immense relief but deep mourning for Lakota's fallen brother, offering his remaining belongings as a token of gratitude to those who brought her home alive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Lakota Windsong captured?",a="Arnak Grimtotem intended to marry Lakota Windsong. After she refused his proposal, he raided her home at night, murdered her protective brother, and dragged her against her will to Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"why is lakota captured","who kidnapped lakota","why did arnak take lakota"}},{q="Where is Darkcloud Pinnacle located?",a="Darkcloud Pinnacle is a cluster of towering rock spires linked by bridges in northern Thousand Needles, situated just southeast of the Great Lift and south of Razorfen Downs.",al={"darkcloud pinnacle location","how to get to darkcloud pinnacle","where is lakota"}},{q="Who is Arnak Grimtotem?",a="Arnak is a ruthless member of the Grimtotem tribe stationed on Darkcloud Pinnacle. Besides kidnapping Lakota and slaying her brother, he is also an outlaw marked for death by the Horde authorities at Freewind Post.",al={"arnak lore","who is arnak","wanted arnak"}},{q="Who should you speak to after the rescue?",a="Once Lakota is safely escorted off the spires to the canyon floor, you must return to Freewind Post atop the high bluffs and speak with Thalia Amberhide.",al={"where to turn in free at last","who is thalia amberhide","turn in free at last"}},{q="Why do the Grimtotem attack during the escape?",a="Arnak's Grimtotem bandits patrol the heights of Darkcloud Pinnacle and aggressively ambush anyone trying to help his intended captive reach freedom.",al={"why do bandits spawn","grimtotem bandits escort"}},{q="What happens to Lakota's brother?",a="Lakota's brother was killed trying to defend her from Arnak Grimtotem during the initial kidnapping. His heirlooms are later given away by Thalia as a reward for rescuing his sister.",al={"lakotas brother","who died saving lakota","what happened to lakota brother"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem clan continues to show their disregard for the peace and unity of the tauren people, demonstrating their brutality through forced kidnappings and fratricide right under the gaze of Freewind Post.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde holds Freewind Post as an essential fortress in southern Kalimdor, making the lawlessness and kidnappings by the Grimtotem at Darkcloud Pinnacle an intolerable threat to the road."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","darkcloud pinnacle","escort","free at last","freewind post","lakota windsong","thalia amberhide","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:lakota-windsong","npc:thalia-amberhide","quest:5147","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","quest:5064","topic:tauren","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Lakota Windsong",["end"]="Thalia Amberhide",level="29",faction="Horde",id=4904},src={"Free at Last (Thousand Needles)"}}
E["quest:5064"] = {t="quest",n="Grimtotem Spying",z="thousandneedles",s="Cliffwatcher Longhorn tasks Horde champions with infiltrating Darkcloud Pinnacle to discover what the elusive Grimtotem clan is plotting. Three unknown couriers were spotted visiting the mesa, leaving guarded correspondence scattered across their mountaintop village. Uncovering these secret notes exposes a brewing scheme that threatens the tauren settlements of Thousand Needles.",h="Cliffwatcher Longhorn tasks Horde champions with infiltrating Darkcloud Pinnacle to discover what the elusive...",sec={{t="Eyes in the Wind",b="Freewind Post sits precariously on high spires, but its defenders must constantly look over their shoulders at their hostile cousins. The Grimtotem clan has long maintained a tense, resentful stance toward the Horde, clinging to their isolationist strongholds atop Darkcloud Pinnacle. Cliffwatcher Longhorn noticed a shift in their behavior when three mysterious agents arrived over successive weeks, conferring with clan leadership in secret. Longhorn suspects these emissaries carried marching orders or alliances meant to undermine Thunder Bluff's presence in the canyon.",sp=0},{t="Infiltration of Darkcloud Pinnacle",b="Darkcloud Pinnacle is a fortified network of sheer mesas connected by wooden rope bridges. Penetrating the village requires braving dense patrols of hostile Grimtotem warriors and shamans. Longhorn's scouts confirmed that the mysterious messages were locked away in separate chests spread across the outpost's central dwellings and outer bluffs. Securing the three secret notes requires sneaking or fighting across the entire settlement to snatch the clan's private communications from under their watchful eyes.",sp=0},{t="Dire Portents",b="Returning the three retrieved notes to Cliffwatcher Longhorn validates Freewind Post's darkest fears. The correspondence reveals that the Grimtotem are not merely posturing; they are actively coordinating with outside agents for an impending move. While the full extent of their machinations remains shrouded, Longhorn immediately begins drafting contingencies to protect the canyon posts from sudden betrayal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is sending agents to meet with the Grimtotem?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn only knows that three agents of unknown origin were seen visiting Darkcloud Pinnacle over recent weeks. The exact identity of their backers is kept strictly under wraps within the guarded notes.",al={"who visited grimtotem","grimtotem secret agents","who sent the notes"}},{q="Where is Darkcloud Pinnacle located?",a="Darkcloud Pinnacle is situated in western Thousand Needles, southeast of the Great Lift. A marked path with a blue totem leads up the mesa cliffs into the village, where wooden bridges connect several high pinnacles.",al={"where is darkcloud pinnacle","how to get to darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle entrance"}},{q="Why are the Grimtotem hostile to other tauren?",a="The Grimtotem believe the tauren are superior to all other races and fiercely reject Cairne Bloodhoof's alliance with the Horde. While some Grimtotem reside under a fragile peace in Thunder Bluff, clans like those on Darkcloud Pinnacle operate with open hostility toward both the Horde and the Alliance.",al={"why do grimtotem hate horde","grimtotem vs thunder bluff","are grimtotem evil"}},{q="Who gives the quest Grimtotem Spying?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn offers the quest at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, but only after you have proven your reliability by completing earlier tasks for the post.",al={"who starts grimtotem spying","grimtotem spying quest giver"}},{q="What prerequisite quests are required before this one?",a="You must complete 'Message to Freewind Post' and 'Pacify the Centaur' before Cliffwatcher Longhorn trusts you enough to entrust you with the espionage mission against the Grimtotem.",al={"prereqs for grimtotem spying","how to unlock grimtotem spying","grimtotem spying chain"}},{q="What happens when you turn in the three secret notes?",a="Upon reading the contents, Cliffwatcher Longhorn reacts with shock, declaring the news to be dire. He acknowledges that Freewind Post must urgently prepare defenses for whatever scheme the Grimtotem are preparing.",al={"grimtotem spying completion","what do the notes say"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem clan's treachery strikes deeply at the tauren, whose society values harmony and family honor. Discovering that kin are meeting secretly with unknown conspirators threatens everything Cairne Bloodhoof has built.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post is a critical Horde lifeline through southern Kalimdor. Any subversive plotting among the Grimtotem at Darkcloud Pinnacle endangers the tenuous supply lines running between the Barrens and Tanaris.",["class:Rogue"]="Recovering the three chests across Darkcloud Pinnacle's suspended bridges and heavily patrolled buildings is an ideal covert operation, rewarding stealth over outright confrontation."},kw={"cliffwatcher longhorn","darkcloud pinnacle","freewind post","grimtotem","secret notes","spying","tauren","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","quest:4841","quest:4542","quest:5147","npc:lakota-windsong","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",level="28",faction="Horde",id=5064},src={"Grimtotem Spying"}}
E["quest:5147"] = {t="quest",n="Wanted - Arnak Grimtotem",z="thousandneedles",s="Wanted: Arnak Grimtotem is a Horde bounty posted at Freewind Post demanding the execution of a violent Grimtotem exile. Arnak is targeted by the local authorities for murder and kidnapping on the mesas above the canyon.",h="Wanted: Arnak Grimtotem is a Horde bounty posted at Freewind Post demanding the execution of a violent...",sec={{t="A Gruesome Crime",b="While tensions between the mainstream tauren of the Horde and the reclusive Grimtotem tribe are perpetually strained, Arnak took matters far beyond political friction. Branded an outcast, Arnak murdered a tauren and abducted the victim's sister, Lakota Windsong. In response to these heinous acts, Cliffwatcher Longhorn of Freewind Post sanctioned an open bounty calling for the rogue tauren's death.",sp=0},{t="Darkcloud Pinnacle",b="Arnak took refuge upon the high crags of Darkcloud Pinnacle, an extensive network of rope bridges and mesa encampments occupied by the Grimtotem clan near the entrance to Razorfen Downs. Trapped upon these windswept heights alongside Arnak is his captive, Lakota Windsong, awaiting rescue from anyone brave enough to fight across the Grimtotem bridges.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Arnak Grimtotem?",a="Arnak Grimtotem is a notorious tauren outcast who committed murder and kidnapped Lakota Windsong. His violent crimes prompted Freewind Post to put a bounty on his head.",al={"who is arnak","arnak grimtotem lore","who is the wanted tauren"}},{q="Where can Arnak Grimtotem be found?",a="He is located high up on the northern cliff mesas of Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles, accessible by ascending the winding path south of the Great Lift and crossing the high wooden bridges toward Razorfen Downs.",al={"where is arnak","arnak grimtotem location","how to find arnak"}},{q="Who is Lakota Windsong?",a="Lakota Windsong is a tauren captive held by Arnak on Darkcloud Pinnacle. Her brother was murdered by Arnak during her abduction, and she remains stranded on the mesa until Arnak is dealt with.",al={"who is lakota","lakota windsong story"}},{q="Who offers the bounty reward?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post manages the bounty. He rewards travelers who present Arnak's severed hoof as proof that the rogue tauren has been brought to justice.",al={"who turns in arnak","bounty turn in","cliffwatcher longhorn reward"}},{q="Is Arnak officially working for the Grimtotem tribe?",a="The bounty specifically describes Arnak as an outcast, indicating he has acted beyond any tribal law. Nevertheless, he has taken refuge within the Grimtotem stronghold of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"is arnak with grimtotem","arnak tribe status"}},{q="What proof is required to claim the bounty?",a="Hunters must sever and return Arnak's Hoof to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post to verify his death and receive the bounty.",al={"what do i bring cliffwatcher longhorn","arnak proof","arnaks hoof"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren loyal to Cairne Bloodhoof, tracking down Arnak is an act of tribal justice, punishing a kinslayer who dishonored their traditions by abducting Lakota Windsong.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post serves as the Horde's vital lifeline through Thousand Needles, and eliminating ruthless renegades on Darkcloud Pinnacle secures the heights along the canyon floor."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","bounty","cliffwatcher longhorn","darkcloud pinnacle","freewind post","lakota windsong","outcast","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","npc:lakota-windsong","quest:4904","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","quest:5064","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren"},m={start="Wanted Poster - Arnak Grimtotem",["end"]="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",level="29",faction="Horde",id=5147},src={"Wanted - Arnak Grimtotem"}}
E["quest:5151"] = {t="quest",n="Hypercapacitor Gizmo",z="thousandneedles",s="Following a deadly centaur ambush on a merchant caravan in Thousand Needles, the goblin tinkerer Wizlo Bearingshiner was left as the sole survivor. Desperate to reclaim his prized invention, he hires adventurers to breach the wreckage, unlock an iron cage, and wrest the gizmo from the neck of a fearsome caged predator.",h="Following a deadly centaur ambush on a merchant caravan in Thousand Needles, the goblin tinkerer Wizlo...",sec={{t="Ambush in the Needles",b="Caravans venturing beneath the towering sandstone spires of Thousand Needles run a perilous gauntlet. Hostile centaur prowl the canyon floor, fiercely guarding their territory and raiding any travelers bold enough to pass through. When one such trade caravan was overrun just north of Whitereach Post, the centaur slaughtered the travelers and plundered the wagons, leaving only the goblin Wizlo Bearingshiner to limp back to safety.",sp=0},{t="An Unlikely Guardian",b="In the chaos of the raid, the centaur looted nearly every valuable scrap, but they gave one ruined wagon a wide berth. Bound inside a sturdy transport cage was a ferocious, enraged panther with Wizlo's prized hypercapacitor gizmo fastened directly around its neck. Daunted by the predator's snarling fury, the centaur abandoned the cage intact, forcing Wizlo to entrust its key to brave mercenaries capable of slaying the beast and reclaiming his gadget.",sp=0},{t="Tinkerer's Ambition",b="True to goblin fashion, Wizlo's passion for mechanical wonder often outpaces practical understanding. Despite hailing the hypercapacitor gizmo as his finest creation and risking lives to retrieve it from the clutches of an apex predator, he admits upon its return that he still has to tinker with it to figure out what it actually does.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Wizlo Bearingshiner?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner is a goblin tinkerer and merchant who took refuge at Whitereach Post after his caravan was ambushed and destroyed by centaur on the canyon floor of Thousand Needles.",al={"who is wizlo","wizlo bearingshiner lore","quest giver wizlo"}},{q="Why is the gizmo around the panther's neck?",a="During the transport or the chaos of the centaur ambush, the device ended up secured around the captive beast's neck. Because the panther was so terrifying, the raiding centaur refused to touch the cage, inadvertently making the predator the device's guardian.",al={"why does the panther have the gizmo","panther necklace","collar gizmo"}},{q="Where is the wrecked caravan located?",a="The wrecked caravan lies just north of Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles, sitting among shattered wagons surrounded by hostile centaur camps.",al={"caravan location","where to find panther cage","cage location"}},{q="Why didn't the centaur loot the cage?",a="According to Wizlo, the enraged panther is so ferocious that even the ruthless centaur marauders trembled in its presence and chose to leave the beast locked in its cage rather than risk opening it.",al={"why centaur left panther","centaur afraid of panther","why is cage untouched"}},{q="What does the Hypercapacitor Gizmo actually do?",a="Wizlo proclaims it his finest gizmo, though upon having it returned, he confesses he still has to spend time studying and tinkering with it to discover what function it actually performs.",al={"what does gizmo do","hypercapacitor function","what is the gizmo"},sp=1},{q="Who controls Whitereach Post?",a="Whitereach Post is a tauren settlement allied with the Horde, perched amidst the canyon mesas to monitor centaur activity and provide safe harbor to Horde travelers.",al={"whitereach post faction","is whitereach horde"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizlo's frantic pursuit of an invention whose purpose he cannot quite recall exemplifies the chaotic, trial-and-error philosophy of classic goblin engineering.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating out of Whitereach Post, Horde scouts and travelers continually battle the predatory centaur clans that menace transit routes through central Kalimdor.",["class:Hunter"]="The enraged panther held in the wrecked caravan is an unusually formidable beast, fierce enough to terrify a full warband of centaur marauders."},kw={"centaur caravan","enraged panther","goblin engineering","hypercapacitor gizmo","panther cage key","thousand needles","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Wizlo Bearingshiner",level="30",faction="Horde",id=5151},src={"Hypercapacitor Gizmo (quest)"}}
E["quest:5762"] = {t="quest",n="Hemet Nesingwary Jr.",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, the merchant dwarf Kravel Koalbeard seeks a courier to carry an overdue shipment of specialized munitions across the seas. The recipient is Hemet Nesingwary Jr., a wealthy dwarven marksman who has set up an expedition deep in the perilous jungles of Stranglethorn Vale.",h="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, the merchant dwarf Kravel Koalbeard seeks a courier to carry...",sec={{t="A Courier Across Continents",b="Amid the roar of rocket engines and the dust of the Shimmering Flats, the opportunistic merchant Kravel Koalbeard often finds himself juggling unorthodox shipments. One delayed delivery belongs to Hemet Nesingwary Jr., a wealthy dwarf who had already departed Kalimdor weeks prior. Ever eager to remain in good standing with prosperous clients, Kravel enlists travelers to carry the heavy crate all the way east to the untamed jungles of Stranglethorn Vale.",sp=0},{t="Ammunition for the Hunt",b="Upon reaching the hunting camp nestled along the northern riverways of Stranglethorn Vale, Nesingwary Jr. welcomes the package with open arms. The crate holds custom, special-gauge ammunition favoured by his legendary father. Out in the dense wilderness where raptors, panthers, and crocolisks stalk the undergrowth, regular powder and shot simply will not suffice for the dangerous safari the expedition has begun.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hemet Nesingwary Jr.?",a="Hemet Nesingwary Jr. is a wealthy dwarven hunter and the son of the famous big game huntsman Hemet Nesingwary. He travels to Stranglethorn Vale to hunt dangerous beasts and lead a camp of fellow marksmen.",al={"hemet jr","who is hemet jr","junior nesingwary"}},{q="What is inside Kravel's Crate?",a="The crate contains special-gauge ammunition that Hemet Nesingwary Jr. and his father swear by, designed specifically for bringing down the massive and ferocious beasts of the wild.",al={"kravel crate contents","what is in the package","kravel cargo"}},{q="Why is Kravel Koalbeard sending a package so far away?",a="The crate arrived weeks late after Hemet had already left the Mirage Raceway. Because Nesingwary Jr. is a wealthy customer who prepaid handsomely, Kravel is eager to protect his business reputation by ensuring it reaches him.",al={"why kravel delivers","kravel motivation"}},{q="Where is Hemet Nesingwary Jr. located?",a="He can be found at an expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, situated along the river just west of the main road, north of Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"nesingwary camp location","where is junior","stranglethorn camp"}},{q="Why is Nesingwary in Stranglethorn Vale?",a="He traveled to Stranglethorn Vale to follow in his father's footsteps, hunting the ferocious predators that prowl the southern jungle and testing his expedition's skill against the wilderness.",al={"why nesingwary stranglethorn","hemet expedition purpose"}},{q="How does Kravel recognize where you have arrived from?",a="When you deliver the crate to Nesingwary Jr., he catches the scent of desert salt clinging to your clothes from your time spent crossing the Shimmering Flats.",al={"desert salt dialogue","shimmering flats smell"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Delivering this crate introduces you directly to the Nesingwary expedition, a renowned gathering of big game trackers who make their living hunting the world's most dangerous fauna.",["race:Dwarf"]="This task connects you to two very different dwarves: Kravel, an industrious and slightly shady desert swindler, and Nesingwary Jr., heir to a famed lineage of dwarven riflemen.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance pathfinders, reaching Nesingwary's camp means traveling south into Stranglethorn past the Rebel Camp in Duskwood's shadow, stepping right into hostile frontier territory.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers can access the remote jungle easily by taking a zeppelin to Grom'gol Base Camp and heading north into the wild river valley to deliver the goods."},kw={"ammunition","hemet","koalbeard","kravel","mirage raceway","nesingwary","shimmering flats","stranglethorn"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","quest:788","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1110","subzone:rebel-camp"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary Jr.",level="31",faction="Neutral",id=5762},src={"Hemet Nesingwary Jr. (quest)"}}
E["quest:6627"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="The Test of Lore is a trial of intellect and historical memory set by the hermit Braug Dimspirit in the Stonetalon Mountains. After retrieving the ancient tome Legacy of the Aspects, travelers must demonstrate their understanding of ancient history by answering Braug's inquiry. Those who fail to heed the text find themselves abruptly banished across Kalimdor.",h="The Test of Lore is a trial of intellect and historical memory set by the hermit Braug Dimspirit in the...",sec={{t="A Trial of Wisdom",b="Part of a broader series of trials originating with Dorn Plainstalker at the Weathered Nook, the Test of Lore shifts focus away from martial survival or blind trust toward understanding the world's ancient past. Braug Dimspirit, residing in the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains, requires seekers to recover ancient texts and genuinely absorb the knowledge held within their pages.",sp=0},{t="Legacy of the Aspects",b="The lesson centers upon the creation and division of the Dragon Aspects, specifically the fateful pact made long before the Great Sundering. Braug tests the seeker's recall regarding the Earth Warder, Neltharion, whose descent into madness and betrayal reshaped the surface of Azeroth. Those who do not respect history are not allowed to proceed along the path of wisdom.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Guesswork",b="Braug does not tolerate idle guessing. A seeker who provides an incorrect answer is instantly expelled by mystic means, finding themselves teleported miles away to Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. Reclaiming one's standing requires a long trek back up into Stonetalon to face the hermit's scrutiny a second time.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the answer to Braug Dimspirit's question?",a="Braug asks about the identity of the Earth Warder detailed in the tome Legacy of the Aspects. The correct answer is Neltharion, the Black Aspect who would later turn against his fellow dragons.",al={"braug question answer","test of lore answer","legacy of the aspects question"}},{q="What happens if you answer incorrectly?",a="Giving Braug the wrong name causes an immediate magical banishment, teleporting you directly to Camp Taurajo in the Barrens. You must travel all the way back to his perch in the Stonetalon Mountains to attempt the trial again.",al={"wrong answer test of lore","failed test of lore","teleported to taurajo"}},{q="Who is Braug Dimspirit?",a="Braug Dimspirit is an elder hermit dwelling in the Stonetalon Mountains who administers tests of knowledge and lore for the Horde, continuing the series of spiritual trials initiated in Thousand Needles.",al={"braug dimspirit","who gives test of lore"}},{q="How does this connect to the trials in Thousand Needles?",a="The trial began with Dorn Plainstalker at the Weathered Nook in Thousand Needles with the Test of Faith. Dorn tests physical and spiritual trust, then sends worthy initiates across Kalimdor to have their intellect, resolve, and strength vetted by other wise elders.",al={"dorn plainstalker connection","test of faith chain"}},{q="What book is Braug quizzing you about?",a="The quiz tests your comprehension of the Legacy of the Aspects, an ancient treatise detailing the blessing of the five Great Dragon Aspects by the titans to guard Azeroth.",al={"what book braug","legacy of the aspects"}},{q="Where does this quest chain lead next?",a="Passing Braug's quiz on the Dragon Aspects leads into further investigative trials of ancient history, requiring seekers to scour distant regions for more lost records and ancestral knowledge.",al={"what is after test of lore","next quest in test of lore"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's trials in Kalimdor demand more than brute force; warriors and shamans alike are expected to understand the ancient scars and draconic powers that shaped the continent.",["race:Tauren"]="The trial embodies the tauren respect for ancestral wisdom and ancient history, ensuring young champions do not march blindly without knowing the balance of the world.",["class:Mage"]="Mages will find Braug's teleportation ward both impressive and punitive, demonstrating that Stonetalon's hermits wield ancient magic to discipline careless scholars."},kw={"aspects","braug dimspirit","earth warder","neltharion","stonetalon","taurajo","test of faith","weathered nook"},rel={"quest:1152","quest:1149","npc:dorn-plainstalker","zone:stonetalon","subzone:camp-taurajo","subzone:weathered-nook","zone:barrens","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Braug Dimspirit",level="30",faction="Horde",id=6627},src={"Test of Lore (3)"}}
E["quest:6628"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="This trial marks the intellectual examination in a broader series of spiritual tests originating in Thousand Needles. After scouring the world for historical texts, initiates present themselves to Parqual Fintallas in the Undercity to prove they understand the darker histories that shape Azeroth.",h="This trial marks the intellectual examination in a broader series of spiritual tests originating in Thousand...",sec={{t="A Trial of Knowledge",b="While many trials among the Horde test martial strength or raw endurance, the Test of Lore demands scholarly dedication. Originating from Dorn Plainstalker's spiritual regimen at the Weathered Nook, the journey carries candidates far from the wind-carved canyons of Thousand Needles into the shadowed halls of the Undercity. Parqual Fintallas serves as the examiner, holding seekers to an exacting standard of historical literacy.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge's Genesis",b="To satisfy Parqual, an initiate must study 'Beginnings of the Undead Threat,' a text detailing the cursed origins of the Scourge in Lordaeron. The core of his interrogation concerns the origin of the entity reigning on the Frozen Throne: the former elder shaman Ner'zhul, whose essence was forged by the Burning Legion into the Lich King. Knowing this grim lineage is considered essential for understanding the Forsaken's existence and the dangers facing Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms alike.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the answer to Parqual's question?",a="Parqual Fintallas asks for the original name of the Lich King. The correct answer is Ner'zhul, the ancient orc shaman whose spirit was bound to the Frozen Throne.",al={"lich king answer","parqual question","test of lore answer"}},{q="What happens if you answer the question wrong?",a="Answering incorrectly saddles you with the Mark of Shame debuff, forcing you to wait out the penalty before Parqual will permit you to attempt the examination again.",al={"mark of shame","wrong answer test of lore"}},{q="Where does this quest chain begin?",a="The overarching trial begins with Dorn Plainstalker at the Weathered Nook, located within the towering spires of Thousand Needles.",al={"where does test of lore start","dorn plainstalker questline"}},{q="Where is Parqual Fintallas located?",a="Parqual Fintallas resides in the Undercity, lingering among the Forsaken's subterranean libraries and corridors where he interrogates prospective students.",al={"find parqual","parqual fintallas location"}},{q="What text is this trial based on?",a="The test is based upon the tome 'Beginnings of the Undead Threat', which details the origins of the Plague of Undeath and the creation of the Lich King.",al={"which book for test of lore","beginnings book"}},{q="Why is a Thousand Needles quest sending people to Undercity?",a="The trials established by the tauren are designed to challenge every facet of an adventurer. To test lore, candidates are sent across the sea to seek out scholarly records preserved in the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"why go to undercity","thousand needles undercity"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Initiated through elder tradition, this test pushes tauren travelers to learn the grim histories of their northern Forsaken allies and the world beyond Kalimdor.",["race:Undead"]="The subject matter strikes at the heart of Forsaken identity: the tragedy of Ner'zhul's creation and the genesis of the curse that bound them before Sylvanas broke the Lich King's grip.",["faction:Horde"]="The trial strengthens ties between Kalimdor's tribes and the kingdom beneath Lordaeron, reminding champions that wisdom is as vital to the Horde's survival as raw strength."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","lich king","mark of shame","nerzhul","parqual fintallas","test of lore","thousand needles","undercity","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:parqual-fintallas","quest:1599","quest:1149","npc:dorn-plainstalker","zone:undercity","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:weathered-nook","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Parqual Fintallas",level="30",faction="Horde",id=6628},src={"Test of Lore (6)"}}
E["quest:788"] = {t="quest",n="Hemet Nesingwary",z="thousandneedles",s="This errand sends travelers across the sea from the salt pans of Kalimdor to the steaming jungles of Stranglethorn Vale. Kravel Koalbeard, an opportunistic merchant at the Mirage Raceway, tasks adventurers with delivering a long-overdue package of specialty supplies to the renowned big-game hunter Hemet Nesingwary.",h="This errand sends travelers across the sea from the salt pans of Kalimdor to the steaming jungles of...",sec={{t="A Transcontinental Delivery",b="Out in the blinding expanse of the Shimmering Flats, commerce moves fast, but shipments sometimes lag behind. Kravel Koalbeard eventually receives a delayed crate earmarked for one of his wealthy patrons, Hemet Nesingwary. Having departed the Thousand Needles long before the parcel arrived, Hemet paid in advance to have it forwarded along to his wilderness hunting camp in Stranglethorn Vale. Rather than make the arduous trek himself, Kravel enlists roving adventurers willing to bridge the ocean divide.",sp=0},{t="Ammunition for the Hunt",b="Tracking down Nesingwary's expedition north of Grom'gol Base Camp reveals the contents of the heavy crate: specialized heavy-gauge ammunition vital for bringing down the dangerous predators prowling the jungle. Hemet immediately recognizes the distinctive white crust of the salt flats clinging to the courier's gear, pleased that his old ties with the wily Kravel yielded the firepower his safari desperately needed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this delivery begin and end?",a="The delivery begins with Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, located in southern Thousand Needles. It finishes halfway across the world at Hemet Nesingwary's expedition camp, nestled in northern Stranglethorn Vale just north of Grom'gol.",al={"quest start and end","where is hemet","where do i go"}},{q="What is inside Kravel's Crate?",a="The crate contains special-gauge ammunition tailored for big-game firearms. Hemet Nesingwary ordered the bespoke shot to pierce the thick hides of Stranglethorn's fiercest beasts.",al={"whats in the crate","crate contents","kravel package"}},{q="Why didn't Kravel deliver the crate himself?",a="Kravel is an enterprising goblin-associated merchant busy overseeing his investments and schemes at the Mirage Raceway. He prefers to hire passing adventurers with the coin Nesingwary provided in advance rather than abandon his post to cross the seas.",al={"why kravel hire someone","why does kravel need help"}},{q="How does Hemet know where the courier came from?",a="Upon receiving the parcel, Hemet immediately smells and identifies the distinct salt crust clinging to the courier's garments, noting it came straight off the Shimmering Flats rather than standard desert dust.",al={"desert salt","hemet dialogue salt"}},{q="What kind of relationship do Kravel and Hemet have?",a="Hemet is an old, lucrative customer of Kravel's. While Kravel respects Hemet's deep pockets, Hemet fondly regards Kravel as a 'crusty old' rogue who is perpetually up to no good.",al={"kravel and hemet history","do they know each other"}},{q="Who is Hemet Nesingwary?",a="Hemet Nesingwary is a celebrated dwarven marksman, author, and big-game hunter who leads an ongoing safari through the perilous depths of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who is hemet","nesingwary lore"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Carrying specialized ammunition directly to Hemet Nesingwary introduces trackers to Azeroth's most famous big-game safari.",["race:Dwarf"]="Delivering custom munitions between two roguish dwarven acquaintances shows how far Ironforge expatriates scatter to pursue coin and quarry."},kw={"ammunition","hemet nesingwary","kravel koalbeard","kravel's crate","mirage raceway","shimmering flats","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary",level="31",id=788},src={"Hemet Nesingwary (quest)"}}
E["quest:8682"] = {t="quest",n="Skyseer the Elder",z="thousandneedles",s="Skyseer the Elder is an honored ancestral spirit residing atop Freewind Post during the Lunar Festival. Travelers seek out his presence high above Thousand Needles to pay their respects to the ancestors and receive his ancient blessing.",h="Skyseer the Elder is an honored ancestral spirit residing atop Freewind Post during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Needles",b="Perched upon the lofty wooden bluffs of Freewind Post, Elder Skyseer appears bathed in a radiant pillar of celestial light. Positioned near the bridges leading toward the massive mechanical lifts, his ghostly presence offers a quiet sanctuary amid the windswept mesas of Thousand Needles.",sp=0},{t="The Ancestral Path",b="Elder Skyseer receives visiting adventurers who come to honor the past during the celebration of the Lunar Festival. Beyond acknowledging their homage, the venerable elder can guide travelers toward his kin scattered across Kalimdor, including Elder Morningdew and Elder Runetotem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Elder Skyseer located?",a="Elder Skyseer stands on the upper mesa of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, situated near the suspension bridges close to the cliffside lifts.",al={"skyseer location","where is skyseer","freewind post elder"}},{q="What is the purpose of seeking out Elder Skyseer?",a="During the Lunar Festival, travelers visit ancestral spirits like Elder Skyseer to pay their respects, receive a Coin of Ancestry, and hear guidance regarding the locations of other elders.",al={"why visit skyseer","skyseer quest objective","lunar festival skyseer"}},{q="Why is Elder Skyseer glowing?",a="Like other honored spirits visiting during the festival, Elder Skyseer is illuminated from the heavens by a bright shaft of moonlight, marking him as an ancestor communing with the living.",al={"why is skyseer in light","elder light beam"}},{q="Which other elders does Skyseer provide directions for?",a="Elder Skyseer provides guidance on how to find nearby ancestral spirits, including Elder Morningdew, Elder Runetotem, Elder Dreamseer, and Elder Wildmane.",al={"other elders","who does skyseer mention","skyseer directions"}},{q="Can Alliance travelers speak with Elder Skyseer?",a="Yes, although Freewind Post is a heavily fortified Horde settlement. Alliance adventurers must tread carefully around the guards to approach the elder without inciting bloodshed.",al={"can alliance talk to skyseer","alliance freewind post elder"}},{q="What happens when you speak to Elder Skyseer?",a="Upon greeting him and paying homage, Elder Skyseer commends your spirit and grants a token of ancestral blessing, completing the brief encounter.",al={"skyseer reward","completing skyseer the elder"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Elder Skyseer rests inside the Horde stronghold of Freewind Post, requiring Alliance pilgrims to navigate the perilous heights and hostile guards to pay their respects.",["race:Tauren"]="Greeting an honored elder atop one of your people's most iconic mesa aeries embodies the deep reverence the Shu'halo hold for their ancestral lineage.",["class:Druid"]="Communing with the ancient spirits under the moonlight aligns closely with the teachings of Cenarius and honoring those who walked the land before."},kw={"ancestor","coins of ancestry","elder skyseer","freewind post","lunar festival","skyseer","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:elder-skyseer","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","npc:elder-morningdew","npc:elder-runetotem","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Skyseer",id=8682},src={"Skyseer the Elder"}}
E["quest:8724"] = {t="quest",n="Morningdew the Elder",z="thousandneedles",s="Morningdew the Elder is an honored ancestral spirit visited during the Lunar Festival in Thousand Needles. Illuminated by a radiant beam of starlight, she offers ancient wisdom and directs pilgrims toward other elders scattered across Kalimdor.",h="Morningdew the Elder is an honored ancestral spirit visited during the Lunar Festival in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Celestial Presence in the Canyons",b="During the Lunar Festival, the spirits of ancient ancestors manifest across Azeroth to share their blessings with travelers. Elder Morningdew appears bathed in a shaft of lunar light, standing out starkly against the dusty red stone and noisy industrial hubbub of Thousand Needles. She reminds mortal travelers to look beyond earthly concerns to the starry expanse above.",sp=0},{t="Wisdom of the Heavens",b="When approached, Morningdew encourages seekers to look toward the countless stars for answers to earthly mysteries. Beyond her contemplative greetings, she serves as a guide for festival pilgrims, sharing knowledge of the locations of other venerated spirits walking the lands, including Elder High Mountain, Elder Grimtotem, Elder Mistwalker, Elder Moonwarden, and Elder Windtotem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Morningdew?",a="Elder Morningdew is an ancestral spirit who manifests during the Lunar Festival. Bathed in starlight, she offers wisdom and guidance to passing adventurers seeking to honor the elders.",al={"elder morningdew","morningdew lore","who is morningdew"}},{q="Where can Elder Morningdew be found?",a="She is located in Thousand Needles, visibly marked by a radiant pillar of light descending from the sky.",al={"morningdew location","where is elder morningdew","find elder morningdew"}},{q="What is the purpose of visiting Elder Morningdew?",a="Travelers visit her during the Lunar Festival to pay their respects to the ancestors, receive ancestral blessings, and learn the whereabouts of other elders throughout the region.",al={"why visit morningdew","morningdew purpose","lunar festival elder"}},{q="Which other elders does Morningdew know about?",a="Elder Morningdew provides directions to five other honored spirits: Elder High Mountain, Elder Grimtotem, Elder Mistwalker, Elder Moonwarden, and Elder Windtotem.",al={"morningdew other elders","elders list morningdew","who does morningdew mention"}},{q="Why is there a pillar of light shining down on her?",a="Every ancestral spirit during the Lunar Festival is illuminated by a beam of celestial starlight, highlighting their ethereal presence and connection to the heavens above.",al={"morningdew light beam","shaft of light elder","why does elder glow"}},{q="What does Morningdew teach pilgrims?",a="Morningdew teaches that the heavens and their countless stars hold answers to earthly mysteries, encouraging those who are wise and fortunate to gaze upward to find truth.",al={"morningdew advice","morningdew dialogue","what does morningdew say"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The Lunar Festival and its celestial elders embody deep connections to Elune, nature, and ancestral communion held sacred by Cenarion circles.",["class:Shaman"]="Communing with honored spirits like Elder Morningdew is central to understanding the balance of ancestors and elements throughout the world.",["race:NightElf"]="Elders illuminated by starlight evoke the ancient traditions of honoring the heavens and the ancient wisdom woven throughout Kalimdor's history.",["race:Tauren"]="Revering the wisdom of ancestral elders is a pillar of tauren culture, making the pilgrimage to spirits like Morningdew deeply meaningful."},kw={"ancestor","elder morningdew","elders","lunar festival","morningdew the elder","shimmering flats","starlight","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:elder-morningdew","zone:thousandneedles","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Morningdew",id=8724},src={"Morningdew the Elder"}}
E["quest:9431"] = {t="quest",n="A Different Approach",z="thousandneedles",s="Magistrix Elosai, an exiled blood elf researcher residing at Freewind Post, seeks to develop an unconventional cure for her people's devastating addiction to magic. Rather than relying on fel or arcane siphoning, she aims to synthesize an alternative remedy using raw elemental reagents. She tasks Horde travelers with harvesting purifying earth from the thundering boulderkin wandering Thousand Needles and delivering it to a goblin tinkerer at Whitereach Post.",h="Magistrix Elosai, an exiled blood elf researcher residing at Freewind Post, seeks to develop an...",sec={{t="An Exile's Heresy",b="Following the destruction of the Sunwell, the blood elves suffered intensely from their severed magical connection, driving many to embrace harsh or predatory methods to sate their hunger. Magistrix Elosai dared to propose a radically different path: natural cures derived from elemental and environmental forces. Her peers in Quel'Thalas branded her work as heresy, burning every copy of her treatise and driving her from the halls of Silvermoon. Finding shelter high above Thousand Needles at Freewind Post, Elosai resolved to continue her work in secret far away from her disapproving kin.",sp=0},{t="Purifying Earth",b="To build her prototype remedy, Elosai requires potent purifying agents capable of cleansing corrupt or erratic magical energies. She identifies the thundering boulderkin, massive earth elementals prowling the crags of western Thousand Needles, as an ideal source. Once subdued, their elemental remains yield purifying earth imbued with stabilizing terrestrial resonance. Rather than preparing the mixture herself, she directs travelers to ferry the harvested soil to Wizlo Bearingshiner, an eccentric goblin engineer stationed nearby at Whitereach Post.",sp=0},{t="The Goblin's Blueprint",b="Wizlo Bearingshiner agrees to assist Elosai purely for profit, despite having misgivings about her methods. While inspecting the delivered earth, the tinkerer reveals that Elosai kept the full scope of her experiment hidden: the purifying earth is intended to line a specialized vessel designed to harvest and store water drawn from a night elf moonwell. Despite recognizing how dangerous it is to sneak into Kaldorei lands to pilfer their sacred waters, Wizlo happily agrees to craft the vessel so long as the magistrix's gold keeps flowing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Magistrix Elosai in Thousand Needles instead of Silvermoon?",a="Elosai was cast out by her fellow blood elves after publishing a controversial treatise advocating for natural remedies to cure their magical withdrawal. Her peers rejected her theories and burned every copy of her work. She fled to Kalimdor to conduct her unconventional research in peace at Freewind Post.",al={"why is elosai in thousand needles","elosai backstory","who is magistrix elosai"}},{q="What is the purpose of collecting Purifying Earth?",a="Purifying earth is gathered from thundering boulderkin elementals in Thousand Needles. Magistrix Elosai intends to use its stabilizing properties as an ingredient and lining material for an experimental remedy designed to purge or alleviate magical addiction.",al={"what does purifying earth do","why harvest purifying earth","purifying earth purpose"}},{q="Who is Wizlo Bearingshiner?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner is a goblin tinkerer residing at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. Hired by Magistrix Elosai, he uses the reagents gathered from the canyon's elementals to craft specialized containment vessels for her ongoing alchemy experiments.",al={"who is wizlo","wizlo bearingshiner whitereach"}},{q="Where can the thundering boulderkin be found?",a="Thundering boulderkin roam the canyon floor along the far western reaches of Thousand Needles, as well as further east near Ironstone Camp before the canyon opens into the Shimmering Flats.",al={"where are thundering boulderkin","thundering boulderkin location","boulderkin locations"}},{q="What is Elosai trying to cure?",a="Elosai is attempting to treat the profound addiction and withdrawal afflicting the blood elves after the loss of the Sunwell. Instead of turning to darker magical sources, she is searching for a natural, herbal and elemental alternative.",al={"what is elosai curing","blood elf addiction cure","elosai research goal"}},{q="Why did Elosai keep the moonwell plan a secret initially?",a="Sneaking into night elf territory to siphon water from a moonwell is an incredibly reckless and hostile undertaking. Elosai avoided mentioning it upfront to ensure travelers would first agree to gather the purifying earth needed to fashion the containment vessel.",al={"why did elosai hide moonwell","secret moonwell plan"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Assisting Elosai represents an early encounter with the struggles facing the sin'dorei as they seek survival and allies across Azeroth.",["class:Mage"]="Mages intimately understand the agonizing pangs of arcane dependency, lending personal weight to Elosai's quest for an alternative path.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman will recognize the intrinsic cleansing power of earthen spirits, though using them alongside night elf moonwell water is an unorthodox fusion.",["profession:Engineering"]="Wizlo's role showcases classic goblin ingenuity: improvising a stabilized containment canister out of raw elementals and spare mechanical parts."},kw={"a different approach","blood elf","freewind post","magical addiction","magistrix elosai","purifying earth","thousand needles","thundering boulderkin","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"npc:magistrix-elosai","npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","quest:9433","quest:9434","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},m={start="Magistrix Elosai",["end"]="Wizlo Bearingshiner",level="28",faction="Horde",id=9431},src={"A Different Approach (BC Classic)"}}
E["quest:9433"] = {t="quest",n="A Dip in the Moonwell",z="thousandneedles",s="A Dip in the Moonwell is a Horde task in Thousand Needles where the goblin tinkerer Wizlo Bearingshiner devises an underhanded scheme to gather sacred water. Rather than asking an adventurer to charge blindly into an Alliance garrison, he arranges the remote hijacking of a delivery automaton to burglarize Thalanaar's moonwell.",h="A Dip in the Moonwell is a Horde task in Thousand Needles where the goblin tinkerer Wizlo Bearingshiner...",sec={{t="A Matter of Discretion",b="Approaching an Alliance border bastion in broad daylight with a ladle is practically suicidal for any Horde scout. Thalanaar sits proudly at the boundary separating Feralas from the canyon, guarded by sentinel archers and hip-deep in night elven sacred ground. To bypass the garrison's scrutiny, Wizlo Bearingshiner at Whitereach Post opts for espionage over bloodshed, setting his sights directly on the outpost's luminous moonwell.",sp=0},{t="The Robotron 3000",b="Wizlo's scheme relies on equipment he has no legal right to touch. Tasked with hauling cargo for a customer, the enterprising goblin quietly broke the factory seal on a Robotron 3000 unit. Setting up a hidden command relay in the brush across the rim from Thalanaar, he provides a portable remote control so an operative can pilot the mechanical contraption into the shrine unnoticed, scoop a vial of lunar water, and retreat before the sentinels or his client catch on.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Wizlo need water from Thalanaar?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner needs pure moonwell water to brew an experimental tonic. Because the night elves jealously guard their sacred fonts, he cannot trade for it directly and must resort to theft.",al={"why steal moonwell water","wizlo moonwell quest","thalanaar water purpose"}},{q="Where is the moonwell located?",a="The moonwell sits directly inside Thalanaar, the night elf outpost stationed along the forested ramp that connects the western rim of Thousand Needles to the lush highlands of Feralas.",al={"thalanaar moonwell location","where is the well"}},{q="What is the Robotron 3000?",a="The Robotron 3000 is an advanced mechanical unit manufactured for a third-party client. Wizlo was hired merely to transport it, but he cracked open the shipping crate without permission to use its remote operations for his heist.",al={"what robot is this","robotron explained"}},{q="Where is the Concealed Command Console hidden?",a="The console is tucked inside a thick cluster of brush along the mesa rim opposite Thalanaar, overlooking the western approach into Feralas.",al={"console location","where to use remote","concealed console spot"}},{q="How does the remote control work?",a="Standing near the concealed console on the mesa rim activates the link, transferring the operator's awareness directly into the mechanical chassis to guide it through the sentinels and into the well's basin.",al={"how to pilot robotron","robotron control unit"}},{q="Who owns the Robotron 3000 originally?",a="Wizlo keeps the client's identity quiet, admitting only that whoever paid for the freight would hang him by his oversized ears if they discovered the automaton was unboxed and driven through the dust.",al={"wizlos client","who hired wizlo"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The mission showcases typical goblin workshop ethics: bypassing danger entirely through unauthorized field-testing of fine-tuned client freight.",["faction:Horde"]="Whitereach Post relies on low-profile tactics to skirt the heavy night elf sentinel watch guarding the transit corridor between Thousand Needles and Feralas."},kw={"engineering","moonwell","robotron","thalanaar","thousand needles","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"quest:9431","quest:9434","npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","subzone:whitereach-post","subzone:thalanaar","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Wizlo Bearingshiner",level="28",faction="Horde",id=9433},src={"A Dip in the Moonwell"}}
E["quest:9434"] = {t="quest",n="Testing the Tonic",z="thousandneedles",s="Testing the Tonic is the culmination of Magistrix Elosai's research in Thousand Needles to find a remedy for the blood elves' magic addiction. Players deliver the final crate of assembled reagents from the goblin engineer Wizlo Bearingshiner at Whitereach Post to Freewind Post so the concoction can be tested.",h="Testing the Tonic is the culmination of Magistrix Elosai's research in Thousand Needles to find a remedy for...",sec={{t="The Goblin's Contribution",b="Wizlo Bearingshiner at Whitereach Post packs the final components of Magistrix Elosai's request into a single crate. Alongside earth collected from local boulderkin and specialized samples gathered across the canyons, the crate includes moonwell water secured by a mechanical diver. With his mechanical task accomplished, the goblin hands off the package, sending his regards and best wishes to the elven scholar high atop Freewind Post.",sp=0},{t="A Desperate Quest for a Cure",b="At Freewind Post, Magistrix Elosai eagerly receives the crate. Ever since the destruction of the Sunwell in Quel'Thalas, her people have suffered from a debilitating craving for arcane energy. Elosai believes that combining primordial earthen reagents with purified moonwell water may yield a restorative tonic capable of dampening or curing the magical withdrawal plaguing the blood elves, treating this trial run as a potential turning point in history.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is in the Crate of Reagents?",a="The crate holds an assortment of exotic materials gathered throughout Thousand Needles, including boulderkin earth, miscellaneous local reagents, and purified moonwell water gathered via Wizlo's mechanical submersible.",al={"crate contents","what did wizlo give me","tonic ingredients"}},{q="Who is Magistrix Elosai?",a="Magistrix Elosai is a blood elf researcher staying at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. She is investigating experimental alchemical methods to ease the crippling magical addiction afflicting her kin after the fall of the Sunwell.",al={"magistrix elosai lore","who is elosai","blood elf at freewind"}},{q="Why does Magistrix Elosai need moonwell water?",a="Moonwells hold pristine, potent magic nurtured by nature and the cosmos. Elosai hopes that blending this purest form of untainted water with primordial earth will yield a stabilizing tonic to satisfy or suppress arcane withdrawal.",al={"why moonwell water","moonwell tonic"}},{q="Where do I take the crate?",a="Take the crate to Magistrix Elosai, who can be found high atop the mesa of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, overlooking the canyon floor.",al={"turn in location","where is elosai","deliver crate"}},{q="Who is Wizlo Bearingshiner?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner is a goblin engineer stationed at Whitereach Post who assisted Elosai by building and operating mechanical apparatuses to retrieve rare water samples.",al={"wizlo","goblin engineer whitereach"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Although blood elves are distant travelers navigating their own hardships, Horde adventurers assist Elosai's research atop Freewind Post as part of broader cooperation across Kalimdor.",["class:Mage"]="Arcanists understand all too well the gnawing hunger of arcane dependence and the profound stakes behind Elosai's experimental tonic."},kw={"blood elf tonic","crate of reagents","freewind post","magic addiction","magistrix elosai","testing the tonic","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"quest:9433","quest:9431","npc:magistrix-elosai","npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},m={start="Wizlo Bearingshiner",["end"]="Magistrix Elosai",level="28",faction="Horde",id=9434},src={"Testing the Tonic"}}
E["subzone:camp-e-thok"] = {t="subzone",n="Camp E'thok",z="thousandneedles",s="Camp E'thok is a Galak centaur settlement located in northwestern Thousand Needles. The aggressive centaur tribe uses this canyon encampment as a base to stage ambushes against passing caravans traveling through the riverbed below.",h="Camp E'thok is a Galak centaur settlement located in northwestern Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Galak Stronghold",b="Tucked into the rugged northwestern reaches of Thousand Needles, Camp E'thok serves as a key settlement for the hostile Galak centaur. Like their kin across Kalimdor, the Galak are relentlessly predatory, preying upon any travelers wandering into the canyon shadows. The camp is notorious for orchestrating raids against merchant caravans, notably ambushing the goblin Wizlo Bearingshiner and seizing his goods—though his prized gadget managed to slip beyond their grasp, guarded by his fierce pet panther.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Camp E'thok?",a="The encampment is occupied by the Galak clan of centaur, an aggressive tribe dominating parts of northwestern Thousand Needles.",al={"who is in camp ethok","camp ethok inhabitants","who controls camp ethok"}},{q="What happened to Wizlo Bearingshiner here?",a="A merchant caravan containing the goblin Wizlo Bearingshiner was ambushed by the Galak centaur from Camp E'thok. While they ransacked the caravan, they failed to take Wizlo's prized gadget because it was secured around the collar of his fierce pet panther.",al={"wizlo bearingshiner raid","goblin caravan attacked","what did centaur steal from wizlo"}},{q="Where is Camp E'thok located?",a="Camp E'thok is situated in northwestern Thousand Needles, nestled along the base of the canyon walls near Splithoof Heights.",al={"camp ethok location","where is camp ethok","camp ethok map"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The relentless aggression of the Galak centaur at Camp E'thok is a constant reminder of the ancestral war between the tauren and centaur throughout southern Kalimdor."},kw={"camp e'thok","centaur","ethok","galak","thousand needles","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","subzone:splithoof-heights","topic:goblin"},src={"Camp E'thok"}}
E["subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkcloud Pinnacle",z="thousandneedles",s="Darkcloud Pinnacle is a fortified tauren settlement perched atop several interconnected mesas east of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles. Held by the aggressive Grimtotem clan, the aerial stronghold serves as a base of operations for regional disruption and shady dealings.",h="Darkcloud Pinnacle is a fortified tauren settlement perched atop several interconnected mesas east of the...",sec={{t="A Clifftop Stronghold",b="Spanning three main mesas joined by rope bridges, Darkcloud Pinnacle commands the canyon basin below. The heights are accessible only by a steep natural slope leading from the canyon floor across wooden bridges, or via a high crossing near Razorfen Downs. From these windswept rocks, the Grimtotem watch the valley, safe from casual assault and isolated from the broader tauren tribes.",sp=0},{t="Schemes on the Mesas",b="Commanded by leaders such as Arnak Grimtotem and Harb Foulmountain, the settlement is more than a simple outpost. Secret correspondence discovered on the mesa suggests the Grimtotem are actively coordinating with dark and unknown powers, pursuing ambitions far removed from the peace forged by Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Darkcloud Pinnacle?",a="The stronghold belongs to the Grimtotem clan, an aggressive and reclusive tauren faction openly hostile to most outsiders and deeply suspicious of the Horde.",al={"who lives at darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle owners","who is at darkcloud pinnacle"}},{q="How do you reach Darkcloud Pinnacle?",a="The pinnacle can be accessed by climbing a natural ramp up an adjacent mesa from the canyon floor and crossing wooden rope bridges, or via a bridge situated near Razorfen Downs.",al={"how to get up darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle path","entrance to darkcloud pinnacle"}},{q="Who leads the Grimtotem here?",a="The settlement's operations are overseen by prominent Grimtotem figures, including Arnak Grimtotem and Harb Foulmountain.",al={"darkcloud pinnacle leaders","who leads darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem bosses"}},{q="What are the Grimtotem plotting here?",a="The Grimtotem at the pinnacle maintain secret communications with an unknown dark influence, working toward shadowy goals that threaten the stability of Thousand Needles.",al={"what is happening at darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem conspiracy"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem's treacherous behavior on these mesas stands in stark opposition to the unity and peace Cairne Bloodhoof strives to maintain among the tribes.",["faction:Horde"]="The Grimtotem occupying this mesa act as hostiles, menacing travelers passing from the Great Lift deeper into Thousand Needles."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem","harb foulmountain","mesa","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:great-lift","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","topic:tauren"},src={"Darkcloud Pinnacle"}}
E["subzone:fizzle-pozzik-s-speedbarge"] = {t="subzone",n="Fizzle & Pozzik's Speedbarge",z="thousandneedles",s="Fizzle & Pozzik's Speedbarge is a massive floating installation in Thousand Needles, serving as a joint haven for rival gnome and goblin tinkerers. Sponsored by the Mechanical Engineers' Guild of Azeroth, this artificial island allows both races to push the boundaries of extreme engineering and racing despite the world's broader political tensions.",h="Fizzle & Pozzik's Speedbarge is a massive floating installation in Thousand Needles, serving as a joint haven...",sec={{t="A Monument to Engineering Rivalry",b="Constructed by engineers including Jinky Twizzlefixxit and Razzeric, the Speedbarge is a chaotic fusion of gnome ingenuity and goblin bombast. Anchored in the waters of Thousand Needles, this city-sized vessel bristles with strange contraptions, pulsating pipes, docks, and attached sub-barges. Named after its prominent leaders, Fizzle Brassbolts and Pozzik, the craft provides a staging ground for experimental watercraft testing and relentless speed trials overseen by the Mechanical Engineers' Guild of Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Tenuous Neutrality",b="What makes the Speedbarge truly distinct is that it operates as a cooperative venture between Alliance-leaning gnomes and Horde-friendly goblins without a formal third-party peacekeeper enforcing harmony. While full-scale war is avoided for the sake of science and competition, the peace remains volatile. Down below deck in the barge's tavern, heated arguments over blueprints, piston tolerances, and faction loyalties routinely boil over into raucous brawls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Speedbarge?",a="It is a massive artificial island and floating workshop in Thousand Needles run jointly by gnome and goblin engineers. It serves as a testing hub, racing marina, and social outpost.",al={"what is this place","speedbarge info","floating barge"}},{q="Who actually built the barge?",a="Although named for Fizzle Brassbolts and Pozzik, builders such as Jinky Twizzlefixxit and Razzeric claim primary credit for the barge's construction and dispute who deserves the honor of its name.",al={"who made the speedbarge","speedbarge builders"}},{q="Why aren't the gnomes and goblins here fighting each other to the death?",a="The tinkerers have worked alongside each other for so long that their shared obsession with engineering and racing eclipses outright warfare, leading to an informal and unmonitored truce.",al={"why peace on speedbarge","gnome goblin alliance here"}},{q="Who sponsors the races here?",a="Speedboat trials and vehicle contests are sponsored by the Mechanical Engineers' Guild of Azeroth (MEGA), in which both Fizzle and Pozzik hold prominent membership.",al={"speedbarge races","who runs the races"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, the barge is a vital stage to demonstrate precision engineering and intellectual superiority over crude goblin craftsmanship.",["profession:Engineering"]="Any practicing engineer will find the barge an eccentric masterpiece of experimental propulsion, schematics, and fierce trade rivalry."},kw={"engineering","fizzle","mega","pozzik","razzeric","speedbarge","thousand needles","twizzlefixxit"},rel={"npc:fizzle-brassbolts","npc:pozzik","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:speedbarge-bar","subzone:shimmering-deep","topic:gnome","topic:goblin"},src={"Fizzle & Pozzik's Speedbarge"}}
E["subzone:freewind-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Freewind Post",z="thousandneedles",s="Freewind Post is the primary Horde outpost in Thousand Needles, perched high atop one of the canyon's dramatic stone mesas. Accessible primarily by tauren lift and winding rope bridges, it serves as a defensive refuge against centaur warbands and a vital frontier staging ground.",h="Freewind Post is the primary Horde outpost in Thousand Needles, perched high atop one of the canyon's...",sec={{t="A Fortress in the Sky",b="Built directly upon the canyon mesas, Freewind Post relies on ingenuity and height to safeguard its people. The Galak centaur dominate the arid canyon floor below, but they cannot effectively scale the towering cliffs or breach the heavy wooden elevators that haul Horde travelers up into the sky. A labyrinth of rope and plank bridges connects Freewind to neighboring spires, forming a secure aerie. Beyond keeping centaur raiding parties at bay, the outpost also helps manage the screeching harpies nesting along the bluffs and tends to the nearby wyvern grounds at Highperch, where wild eggs are culled and trained as loyal wind rider mounts for the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Shadows from Darkcloud Pinnacle",b="Despite its impregnable height, Freewind Post faces growing tension with its neighbors to the northwest: the Grimtotem tribe stationed at Darkcloud Pinnacle. Once tolerated as stubborn traditionalists, the Grimtotem under Chieftain Arnak have increasingly turned to violence, kidnapping, and murder. Suspicious rituals and whispers of dark power surround the nearby peaks. The local tauren watch the skies and rope bridges with growing dread, conscious that their most dangerous enemies do not prowl the salt flats below, but sit entrenched across the canyon winds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Freewind Post built so high up on a mesa?",a="The vertical layout keeps the settlement safe from the hostile Galak centaur warbands patrolling the canyon bottom. Centaur excel on flat terrain but cannot scale sheer cliff faces or easily breach the mechanical wooden lifts used by the tauren.",al={"why is freewind post in the sky","why mesa","freewind post elevation"}},{q="How do you get up and down from the post?",a="Most travelers use the large mechanical wooden lifts stationed at the base of the main mesa. There is also a back route consisting of a precarious series of rope bridges and wooden ramps winding between neighboring rock pillars, though a careless step can mean a lethal plunge to the canyon floor.",al={"how to get up freewind post","freewind post elevator","freewind entrance"}},{q="What is the relationship between Freewind Post and the Grimtotem?",a="Relations are deeply strained. The Grimtotem occupying Darkcloud Pinnacle northwest of Freewind Post are accused of murders, kidnappings, and unprovoked hostility toward other tauren, leaving the outpost's defenders in a state of quiet vigilance against their neighboring kin.",al={"grimtotem freewind post","darkcloud pinnacle freewind","why are grimtotem bad here"}},{q="What importance does Highperch have to the post?",a="Highperch is an ancestral nesting ground for wild wyverns just across the canyon. The tauren of Freewind Post monitor these beasts and cull eggs from their nests, which are then nurtured and raised to serve as wind rider mounts throughout the Horde.",al={"why highperch","highperch wyverns freewind"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Freewind Post displays the architectural ingenuity of the shu'halo, adapting mesa heights to shut out traditional centaur marauders while tending the ancestral wyverns of the bluffs.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post is the sole major Horde sanctuary and flight connection between the Southern Barrens and Tanaris, providing essential logistical support across central Kalimdor."},kw={"darkcloud pinnacle","elevator","freewind post","galak","highperch","mesa","tauren","thousand needles","wyverns"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:highperch","topic:grimtotem-tribe","topic:centaur","topic:tauren","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Freewind Post"}}
E["subzone:great-lift"] = {t="subzone",n="Great Lift",z="thousandneedles",s="The Great Lift is a massive, tauren-engineered elevator system perched on the southern edge of the Barrens. It serves as the primary route lowering travelers and supplies hundreds of feet into the sheer canyon basin of Thousand Needles. Despite its strategic value, aggressive quilboar encroaching through the southern wastes have made approaching the rim increasingly perilous.",h="The Great Lift is a massive, tauren-engineered elevator system perched on the southern edge of the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Gateway Carved from Wood and Rope",b="Spanning the sheer cliff edge between the southern Barrens and the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, the Great Lift stands as a marvel of practical tauren construction. Built using heavy timber, braided rope, and counterweighted pulleys, its paired platforms carry caravans, couriers, and warriors safely across a vertical precipice that would otherwise break any wagon. At the top and bottom platforms, tauren like Brave Moonhorn and Grish Longrunner maintain watch, keeping travelers informed of the road ahead and ensuring cargo passes smoothly.",sp=0},{t="Dangers at the Rim",b="Operating the lift has become increasingly hazardous due to the hostile territory above it. Aggressive quilboar tribes in the southern Barrens have expanded aggressively southward, choking the road toward the lift and threatening to cut off Thousand Needles from the northern trails entirely. Those who make the long journey south must constantly fend off razorfen raiders before they can ever step foot onto the wooden platforms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built the Great Lift?",a="The Great Lift was designed and constructed by the tauren to bridge the massive vertical gap between the arid plateaus of the Barrens and the deep canyon floor of Thousand Needles.",al={"who made the great lift","great lift builders","tauren elevator origin"}},{q="Why is traveling to the lift dangerous?",a="The encroaching quilboar of the southern Barrens have aggressively expanded their territory toward the rim. Their raiding parties prowl the approaches, often harassing or outright ambushing supply caravans and couriers bound for the elevator platforms.",al={"why are there quilboar here","southern barrens danger","lift road blocked"}},{q="Who watches over the Great Lift?",a="Brave Moonhorn and Grish Longrunner are stationed at the lift to watch the routes, assist Horde travelers, and keep an eye on the surrounding wilderness.",al={"who guards the lift","lift keepers","tauren at the lift"}},{q="Where does the Great Lift lead?",a="Riding the platforms down brings travelers onto the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, while ascending leads straight into the southern Barrens.",al={"where does lift go","what is below the lift","lift destination"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The lift is a vital Horde arterial link connecting central Kalimdor to the isolated reaches of Thousand Needles and Shimmering Flats.",["race:Tauren"]="Constructed with sturdy timber and counterweights, the lift showcases your people's ingenious ability to overcome rugged landscape obstacles without scarring the earth."},kw={"brave moonhorn","elevator","great lift","grish longrunner","quilboar","the barrens","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens","npc:brave-moonhorn","npc:grish-longrunner","topic:tauren","topic:quilboar"},src={"Great Lift"}}
E["subzone:highperch"] = {t="subzone",n="Highperch",z="thousandneedles",s="Highperch is an elevated plateau in western Thousand Needles, towering high above the canyon floor. It is renowned as a primary nesting ground for wild wyverns and wind riders. The roost is home to fierce prides defending their young among the windswept crags.",h="Highperch is an elevated plateau in western Thousand Needles, towering high above the canyon floor.",sec={{t="Aerie of the Wyverns",b="Rising sharply out of the canyon floor, Highperch is a rugged sanctuary for Kalimdor's native wyverns. The plateau provides natural defense against predators and an unobstructed launch point for their hunting flights across Thousand Needles. Within its reaches, wyvern prides live under the protection of watchful patriarchs and matriarchs, tending to nests filled with pridelings. The beasts fiercely defend their territory against any intruders who manage to climb into their high domain.",sp=0},{t="A Refuge in the Heights",b="While hostile to outsiders, the high cliffs occasionally attract travellers and hunters willing to brave the dangerous ascent. The tauren scout Pao'ka Swiftmountain once found himself trapped on these perilous heights before being rescued, leaving him with an enduring respect for the roost and the beasts that dwell within it. For adventurers journeying through the canyon, scaling the ramp to Highperch means contending with dozens of razor-sharp talons and venomous tails.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live at Highperch?",a="Highperch is inhabited exclusively by wild wyverns and wind riders. You will encounter protective patriarchs, consorts, soaring adults, and young pridelings defending their clifftop nests.",al={"highperch beasts","what is at highperch","highperch mobs"}},{q="Where is Highperch located?",a="Highperch is situated in western Thousand Needles, accessible via a winding ramp that leads up from the southern wall of the canyon floor.",al={"highperch location","how to find highperch","where is highperch"}},{q="Why is Highperch significant to the Horde?",a="Wyverns, also known as wind riders, are the vital flying mounts of the Horde, having allied with the orcs during the Third War. Natural roosts like Highperch represent the wild heritage and thriving population of these loyal beasts.",al={"horde connection to highperch","wyverns and horde","why do orcs care about highperch"}},{q="Who is Pao'ka Swiftmountain?",a="Pao'ka Swiftmountain is a tauren scout who became stranded amidst the deadly wyvern nests on Highperch. After surviving the ordeal, he dedicated himself to monitoring and ensuring the well-being of the roost.",al={"paoka swiftmountain","tauren at highperch","who got trapped at highperch"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The wind riders nesting upon Highperch are close kin to the noble flying mounts that carry the Horde across Kalimdor, making the sanctuary an awe-inspiring sight for Horde champions.",["class:Hunter"]="The sprawling aerie offers seasoned hunters a firsthand look at wild wyverns hunting and guarding their nests in their natural, untamed habitat."},kw={"aerie","highperch","nest","pao'ka swiftmountain","prideling","thousand needles","wind rider","wyvern"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","npc:pao-ka-swiftmountain","quest:4767"},src={"Highperch"}}
E["subzone:ironstone-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Ironstone Camp",z="thousandneedles",s="Ironstone Camp is an outpost established by the Horde along the western border of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles. Originally deployed to expel Alliance dwarven excavators from the nearby digsite, the encampment's forces now face a deadly threat after subterranean silithid overran the excavation.",h="Ironstone Camp is an outpost established by the Horde along the western border of the Shimmering Flats in...",sec={{t="A Change of Mission",b="Ironstone Camp sits directly on the threshold between the high pillars of Thousand Needles and the blazing salt expanse of the Shimmering Flats. The Horde detachment stationed here was initially dispatched with a clear and singular objective: dislodge the Prospector Stormpike Expedition digging at the Rustmaul Digsite. However, their military confrontation was cut short when a swarm of voracious silithid burst forth from a nearby cavern, violently engulfing the dig and attacking both sides. Led by Moktar Krin, the surviving camp defenders have diverted their efforts to combating the insectoid infestation before the swarm spreads unchecked across the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Ironstone Camp?",a="Ironstone Camp was set up as a forward Horde staging point to drive Alliance dwarven excavators out of the Rustmaul Digsite. However, an unexpected swarm of subterranean silithid erupted into the area, shifting the encampment's priority to survival and containment of the insect menace.",al={"why is ironstone camp here","ironstone camp purpose","horde camp shimmering flats"}},{q="Who leads the forces at Ironstone Camp?",a="Moktar Krin directs the Horde fighters stationed here. With the original mission disrupted by the insect outbreak, he coordinates patrols and tasks travelers with culling the aggressive silithid infesting the neighboring digsite.",al={"ironstone camp leader","moktar krin","who runs ironstone camp"}},{q="Where is Ironstone Camp located?",a="The camp is situated in Thousand Needles right on the western edge of the Shimmering Flats, resting close to the path leading out of the canyon floor toward the blinding salt flats.",al={"ironstone camp location","where is ironstone camp","how to find ironstone camp"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The camp offers a strategic stopping point before heading out onto the open salt flats, though the local commanders are hard-pressed to eliminate the silithid swarm threatening their position.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance explorers heading toward the Shimmering Flats should keep their distance from the camp, which was originally established specifically to harass and purge the Bael'dun dwarven diggers."},kw={"horde outpost","ironstone camp","moktar krin","rustmaul digsite","shimmering flats","silithid","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},src={"Ironstone Camp"}}
E["subzone:mirage-abyss"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirage Abyss",z="thousandneedles",s="Mirage Abyss refers to the submerged trench and canyon formations situated in Thousand Needles where dry salt flats once stood. Now submerged deep beneath the waves, this drowned basin attracts salvagers seeking sunken treasures and herbalists searching the ocean floor.",h="Mirage Abyss refers to the submerged trench and canyon formations situated in Thousand Needles where dry salt...",sec={{t="The Sunken Trench",b="Beneath the surface of the Shimmering Deep lies the Mirage Abyss, a network of drowned gorges resting where Weazel's Crater once marked the parched desert. What was once an arid basin baked by the sun is now flooded with saltwater, blanketed in thick beds of stranglekelp and prowled by oceanic predators like giant whale sharks.",sp=0},{t="Depths of Salvage",b="The flooded canyon has become an opportunistic dive site for Southsea treasure hunters. Following the sinking of pirate vessels torn apart by deep-sea monsters, salvagers brave the crushing water to drag chests from the ocean floor, competing with local scavengers and dangerous aquatic life nestled in the murky depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Mirage Abyss?",a="The Mirage Abyss is a deep underwater canyon network situated in the Shimmering Deep of Thousand Needles. It occupies the sunken floor of the valley where dry landmarks like Weazel's Crater once stood.",al={"what is mirage abyss","mirage abyss lore","where is mirage abyss"}},{q="Why are pirates diving here?",a="Southsea treasure hunters explore the trench to recover sunken chests and valuable cargo lost when a colossal whale shark attacked and destroyed one of their vessels in the flooded basin.",al={"southsea pirates shimmering deep","why are treasure hunters here","mirage abyss pirates"}},{q="What flora grows in the abyss?",a="The submerged floor of the canyon provides fertile ground for rich thickets of stranglekelp, making it a prominent harvesting spot for underwater gatherers.",al={"mirage abyss plants","stranglekelp mirage abyss","thousand needles herbs"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The flooded gorges of the Mirage Abyss are laden with dense patches of stranglekelp, offering underwater harvesters ample gathering opportunities away from coastal shores."},kw={"mirage abyss","shimmering deep","southsea","stranglekelp","thousand needles","weazel's crater","whale shark"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-deep","subzone:weazel-s-crater","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Mirage Abyss"}}
E["subzone:mirage-raceway"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirage Raceway",z="thousandneedles",s="The Mirage Raceway is an impromptu engineering proving ground situated in the shimmering salt flats of Thousand Needles. Founded on the heated rivalry between goblin tinkerer Pozzik and gnome engineer Fizzle Brassbolts, it pits high-speed rocket cars against one another across the baked earth. The track serves as a neutral gathering place where members of both the Alliance and Horde come to wager, tinker, and cheer on their favored machines.",h="The Mirage Raceway is an impromptu engineering proving ground situated in the shimmering salt flats of...",sec={{t="Speed, Salt, and Rivalry",b="Sprawled across the vast white desert floor of the Shimmering Flats, the Mirage Raceway was born out of an unrelenting grudge match between two master tinkerers: the goblin Pozzik and the gnome Fizzle Brassbolts. Determined to settle once and for all whose race possesses superior technical ingenuity, the two constructed custom rocket-powered drag cars and recruited rival crews to pit them against each other in daily high-velocity showdowns. The relentless competition has turned the barren flats into a bustling hub of invention, sabotage, and testing as each crew desperately looks for any mechanical advantage.",sp=0},{t="A Neutral Crossroads",b="Because both teams need supplies, fuel, and test pilots, the raceway maintains an uneasy truce between the Horde and Alliance. Spectators gather from across Kalimdor to cheer on either gnome precision or goblin firepower, while gamblers and shady opportunists thrive on the constant wagers placed on the results. Beyond the roar of rocket thrusters, the camps serve as a busy trading depot for travelers journeying between Thousand Needles and the blazing sands of Tanaris.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Mirage Raceway?",a="The Mirage Raceway is an open-air rocket-car drag strip laid across the salt flats of Thousand Needles. It was built by rival engineers seeking to prove whether goblin or gnome mechanics are superior.",al={"what is mirage raceway","raceway purpose","shimmering flats track"}},{q="Who runs the races here?",a="The track is maintained jointly by the gnome engineer Fizzle Brassbolts and the goblin tinkerer Pozzik. Each operates a dedicated crew and workshop along the raceway to field competing rocket cars.",al={"who leads raceway","fizzle and pozzik","who built this track"}},{q="Can Horde and Alliance both use this area?",a="Yes. The raceway operates under an informal neutral truce so that both factions can visit the camps, place wagers, aid the rival engineering crews, and purchase supplies without interference.",al={"is mirage raceway neutral","can alliance visit","can horde visit"}},{q="Why race out in the salt flats?",a="The flat, wide expanse of the Shimmering Flats provides a smooth, unobstructed surface ideal for rocket-propelled vehicles that require miles of room to reach top speeds and safely slow down.",al={"why thousand needles","why race on salt","why in shimmering flats"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For tinkerers of any faction, the Raceway represents the ultimate clash between goblin risk-taking and gnomish meticulous design, offering field tests of raw speed, volatile fuel, and experimental vehicle parts.",["race:Gnome"]="Fizzle Brassbolts flies the banner of Gnomeregan here, relying on fellow gnomes and allies to prove that disciplined innovation easily outperforms reckless goblin combustion."},kw={"fizzle brassbolts","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:pozzik","npc:fizzle-brassbolts","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome","topic:goblin","subzone:gadgetzan"},src={"Mirage Raceway"}}
E["subzone:raceway-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Raceway Ruins",z="thousandneedles",s="The Mirage Raceway sits on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles, a wide salt flat where gnome and goblin pit crews test experimental rocket cars. Across these cracked salt pans, racers compete fiercely, frequently leaving scattered rocket car parts and twisted chassis behind in the dust.",h="The Mirage Raceway sits on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles, a wide salt flat where gnome and goblin...",sec={{t="A Boneyard of High Speeds",b="Speed and explosive ambition drive everything on the Shimmering Flats. Gnomes and goblins have established a sprawling raceway over the dried salt bed, testing volatile engines in a race for engineering bragging rights. Between crashes, mechanical mishaps, and relentless rivalries, pieces of shattered rocket cars litter the outskirts of the track, often salvaged by scavengers, scorpids, and passing opportunists.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Raceway?",a="The Mirage Raceway is an expansive racing track set on the dried salt beds of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles. It was founded as neutral ground where goblin and gnome engineers pit their fastest, most volatile rocket cars against each other.",al={"what is raceway","mirage raceway purpose","who built the raceway"}},{q="Why are there broken car parts scattered around?",a="Gnomish and goblin engineering favors extreme performance over basic safety. High-speed collisions, catastrophic engine detonations, and chaotic trial runs constantly shed parts across the salt flats, leaving valuable scrap scattered for scavengers.",al={"rocket car parts","why are parts everywhere","broken cars"}},{q="Who works and races out here?",a="Rival teams of gnomes and goblins dominate the flats, supported by pit crews, grease monkeys, and neutral vendors. While their respective factions may be hostile elsewhere, here the shared pursuit of raw horsepower creates a tenuous, noisy peace.",al={"who is here","raceway factions","gnomes and goblins"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The salt flats are a showcase of peak engineering madness, featuring experimental rocket propulsion, mechanical superchargers, and the wreckage to prove it.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, the raceway is a proving ground to demonstrate precise craftsmanship over crude goblin volatile mixtures, though both often end in explosions."},kw={"gnome","goblin","mirage raceway","raceway","rocket car","salvage","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1110"},src={"Raceway Ruins"}}
E["subzone:razorfen-downs"] = {t="subzone",n="Razorfen Downs",z="thousandneedles",s="Razorfen Downs is the ancestral capital and sacred burial labyrinth of the quilboar, carved deep into the colossal brambles bordering the Southern Barrens and Thousand Needles. Once their holiest sanctuary, it has fallen under the sway of the undead Scourge, transforming into a festering bastion of necromancy.",h="Razorfen Downs is the ancestral capital and sacred burial labyrinth of the quilboar, carved deep into the...",sec={{t="A Sacred City Corrupted",b="Long revered as the ancestral capital city and burial grounds of the quilboar race, Razorfen Downs rests within the colossal petrified briars sprung from the fallen demigod Agamaggan. Legend holds that its arched entryway was carved directly from the Great Boar's very maw. For centuries, the high priests of the Death's Head tribe tended these deep, winding burrows and honored their revered dead. Yet despite its sacred standing among the boar-folk, the maze of bone and bramble has recently suffered a catastrophe far darker than any squabble over Barrens water.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge Reaches Kalimdor",b="Following the devastation of the Third War, the tendrils of the undead Scourge reached silently into southern Kalimdor. Led by the frost-wielding lich Amnennar the Coldbringer, agents of death infiltrated the thorn maze and subverted the Death's Head priesthood. Instead of honoring their ancestors, the quilboar now harbor rotting ghouls, skeletons, and necromancers within their sacred pens. The corruption here threatens to fester outward across the Barrens, turning the quilboar's holiest ground into a launchpad for the Scourge's ambitions in the west.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Razorfen Downs?",a="Razorfen Downs is the ancestral capital city and burial grounds of the quilboar race. Grown from the enormous thorn brambles formed by the fallen Ancient Agamaggan, it serves as the spiritual heart of quilboar culture and the headquarters of their high priesthood, the Death's Head tribe.",al={"what is the downs","razorfen downs lore","who lives in razorfen downs"}},{q="Why is the Scourge inside Razorfen Downs?",a="The lich Amnennar the Coldbringer arrived following the Third War to establish a Kalimdor stronghold for the Lich King. By corrupting the Death's Head priesthood and raising quilboar dead, Amnennar turned the labyrinthine thorn city into a hidden nest of necromantic power.",al={"why are there undead in razorfen downs","amnennar razorfen downs","scourge in razorfen"}},{q="How does Razorfen Downs differ from Razorfen Kraul?",a="Razorfen Kraul is the primary military redoubt and living warren of the quilboar, ruled directly by the crone Charlga Razorflank. In contrast, the Downs is their traditional capital and sacred burial ground, deeper south, which has fallen under the sway of necromancy and Scourge control.",al={"difference between kraul and downs","downs vs kraul","kraul or downs"}},{q="Where is the entrance located?",a="The Downs is situated at the very southern border of the Barrens, overlooking the great drop into Thousand Needles. Its entrance is a natural arched fissure nestled into the towering, tangled brambles, reputed in myth to be carved from Agamaggan's gaping maw.",al={"downs entrance","where is razorfen downs","how to get into razorfen downs"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The quilboar are a constant thorn in the side of the Crossroads, but an outpost of the Lich King right on the edge of the Barrens is an existential menace that the Horde cannot afford to ignore.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, discovering a Scourge lich operating covertly on Kalimdor is a chilling reminder of the master they rebelled against, demanding swift and decisive eradication."},kw={"agamaggan","amnennar","coldbringer","death speaker blackthorn","death's head","downs","quilboar","razorfen downs","scourge"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:quilboar","topic:scourge","topic:agamaggan","zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens","topic:horde","quest:5052"},src={"Razorfen Downs"}}
E["subzone:roguefeather-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Roguefeather Den",z="thousandneedles",s="Roguefeather Den is a cavern nestled in the south-central reaches of Thousand Needles. Infested with ferocious screeching harpies, the cave serves as a fortified roost where the flock hoards scavenged provisions deep within its shadowed recesses.",h="Roguefeather Den is a cavern nestled in the south-central reaches of Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Roost in the Canyons",b="Carved into the sheer sandstone bluffs of southern Thousand Needles, Roguefeather Den is the foul nesting ground of local harpies. Known for their feral screeching and aggressive territorialism, the harpies treat the cavern as both a secure haven and a storehouse, vigilantly guarding the gathered food and stolen supplies they pile in the dark recesses at the back of the cave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Roguefeather Den?",a="It is a small cavern located along the southern cliffs of Thousand Needles, serving as a roost and supply stockpile for the territorial Roguefeather harpies.",al={"what is this cave","roguefeather den info","where is roguefeather"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the cave?",a="The cavern is infested with hostile, screeching harpies who fiercely defend their nesting grounds and gathered food against any intruders.",al={"who lives in roguefeather den","mobs in roguefeather den"}},{q="What is kept deep inside Roguefeather Den?",a="Deep in the back of the cavern, the harpies hoard stores of scavenged and stolen food, which they protect with relentless aggression.",al={"what is in the back of the cave","roguefeather food"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde travelers making the long trek toward the Shimmering Flats, the aggressive flock inhabiting Roguefeather Den represents a persistent aerial and ambush threat along the southern canyon floor."},kw={"cavern","harpies","roguefeather","roguefeather den","roost","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","quest:1089"},src={"Roguefeather Den"}}
E["subzone:rustmaul-dig-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Rustmaul Dig Site",z="thousandneedles",s="The Rustmaul Dig Site is a ruined excavation in the southern reaches of the Shimmering Flats. Originally established by the dwarven Explorers' League to unearth ancient ruins, the camp fell into tragedy when a Horde war party slaughtered the miners, only to inadvertently awaken a subterranean silithid swarm. Now abandoned by mortals, the site crawls with hostile insectoids emerging from the caverns below.",h="The Rustmaul Dig Site is a ruined excavation in the southern reaches of the Shimmering Flats.",sec={{t="A Slaughter in the Salt",b="Prospectors from the Ironforge Explorers' League set up the Rustmaul Dig Site hoping to uncover forgotten artifacts buried beneath the salt flats. Their efforts were brutally cut short when an aggressive Horde war party, led by Moktar Krin, fell upon the camp and wiped out the dwarven excavators. However, the conquerors enjoyed no triumph. The violent clash and deep digging disturbed a dormant cave network beneath the site, releasing an endless horde of silithid insects that quickly overwhelmed and drove off the battered survivors.",sp=0},{t="The Awakening Swarm",b="Today, Rustmaul stands entirely lost to the surface races. What remains of the mining equipment and scaffolds is buried under skittering mandibles and alien carapaces. The surviving members of Moktar Krin's war party retreated north to Ironstone Camp, terrified by the unrelenting tide of insectoids they accidentally unleashed upon the Shimmering Flats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rustmaul Dig Site?",a="It is an excavation camp in the Shimmering Flats within Thousand Needles. Dwarven explorers originally founded it to unearth ancient ruins, but it has since been overrun by deadly silithid swarms.",al={"what is rustmaul","rustmaul lore","shimmering flats dig site"}},{q="Who used to live and work here?",a="Prospectors and excavators from the dwarven Explorers' League originally operated the dig, uncovering artifacts and ruins buried beneath the salt flats.",al={"who dug rustmaul","who owned rustmaul","dwarves at rustmaul"}},{q="Why is the dig site abandoned and full of bugs?",a="A Horde war party led by Moktar Krin assaulted the camp and slaughtered the dwarves. The commotion disturbed a subterranean nest of silithid insects within the mine cave, unleashing a swarm that drove the surviving attackers away.",al={"what happened at rustmaul","why are there bugs at rustmaul","who attacked rustmaul"}},{q="Where did the surviving attackers go?",a="The battered remnants of Moktar Krin's Horde war party fled north across the flats to recuperate at Ironstone Camp, with messengers carrying warnings as far as Orgrimmar.",al={"where is moktar krin","survivors of rustmaul","ironstone camp connection"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, Rustmaul is a tragic reminder of the hazards facing the Explorers' League, whose scholars were slaughtered here before the earth itself gave way to monstrous insects.",["faction:Horde"]="Though Moktar Krin's war party claimed victory over the dwarven excavators, their reckless violence stirred an ancient, creeping silithid menace that now threatens the entire region."},kw={"explorers' league","ironstone camp","moktar krin","rustmaul dig site","shimmering flats","silithid","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:ironstone-camp","topic:explorers-league","topic:horde","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Rustmaul Dig Site"}}
E["subzone:shimmering-deep"] = {t="subzone",n="Shimmering Deep",z="thousandneedles",s="The Shimmering Deep is a region synonymous with the Shimmering Flats in eastern Thousand Needles. While the canyon floor remains a parched salt flat today, subterranean water tables beneath the crusted salt give the deep basin its ancient, shimmering character.",h="The Shimmering Deep is a region synonymous with the Shimmering Flats in eastern Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="The Dried Basin",b="Sprawling across the eastern reaches of Thousand Needles, the vast depression known historically across local charts as the Shimmering Deep or Shimmering Flats is an immense salt pan cut off from the sea. White alkali dust blankets the earth beneath towering canyon walls, creating an unforgiving expanse where little green survives. Despite the dryness of the surface, deep underground reservoirs and the proximity to the surrounding sea wall define the geology of this vast basin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shimmering Deep?",a="The Shimmering Deep is the geographic depression encompassing the salt flats of eastern Thousand Needles, commonly referred to as the Shimmering Flats. It forms an expansive salt pan nestled between the jagged mesas and the high coastal bluffs.",al={"shimmering deep lore","what is this place","shimmering deep location"}},{q="Is there water in the Shimmering Deep?",a="No. In the current era, the basin remains an arid, sun-bleached expanse of salt and alkali. Deep subterranean waters lie below, and ocean waters lap against the high ridge dividing it from the coast, but the basin floor itself is dry land.",al={"is shimmering deep underwater","water in shimmering deep","is it flooded"}},{q="Who inhabits this part of Thousand Needles?",a="The surrounding cliffs and margins are prowled by scorpids, basilisks, and hyenas, along with aggressive indigenous Galak centaur and encroaching Southsea pirates along the eastern boundaries.",al={"who lives here","shimmering deep enemies","creatures in shimmering deep"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The dry, flat expanse of the dried basin floor provides an ideal proving ground for experimental high-speed vehicular trials and rocket testing."},kw={"basin","galak","salt flat","salvage","shimmering deep","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:goblin","topic:gnome","topic:pirate"},src={"Shimmering Deep"}}
E["subzone:shimmering-flats"] = {t="subzone",n="Shimmering Flats",z="thousandneedles",s="The Shimmering Flats is an expansive salt flat lying at the southeastern tip of Thousand Needles, bordering the desert of Tanaris. Once the bed of an ancient lake, this sun-baked expanse is now famous for the high-speed mechanical rivalries of the Mirage Raceway and a harsh population of desert beasts.",h="The Shimmering Flats is an expansive salt flat lying at the southeastern tip of Thousand Needles, bordering...",sec={{t="A Bed of Salt and Speed",b="Stretching out under the blinding southern sun, the Shimmering Flats is a vast dried lakebed devoid of vegetation, dotted with the sun-bleached bones of turtles and even the wooden wreck of an ancient sailing vessel. Its sheer, unbroken level surface makes it the premier testing ground on Kalimdor for experimental vehicles. At the center of the flats lies the Mirage Raceway, where gnome and goblin tinkerers constantly clash to see whose rocket cars, gyrocopters, and engines can achieve the highest speeds—often resulting in fiery crashes and smoking craters across the white crust.",sp=0},{t="Hazards of the Salt",b="Beyond the roaring engines of the raceway, the basin is far from peaceful. Hardened basilisks, aggressive scorpids, and circling vultures prey upon anything that slows down on the open expanse. Further south, the ground grows treacherous around the Rustmaul Dig Site. Originally excavated by dwarven prospectors before being contested by the Horde, the quarry was entirely abandoned when picks cracked into subterranean tunnels, unleashing a swarm of vicious silithid into the southern edge of the flats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a ruined ship out in the middle of the desert?",a="The Shimmering Flats was once a massive inland lake that dried up long ago. The wrecked vessel resting in the northern stretch of the flats is a remnant of that ancient body of water, left behind when the lake evaporated into the vast salt pan seen today.",al={"ship in shimmering flats","boat in salt flats","wrecked boat thousand needles"}},{q="Why are gnomes and goblins here together?",a="The unbroken, flat salt crust provides the perfect terrain for testing rocket cars and cutting-edge mechanical contraptions. Rather than fighting over territory, local gnomes and goblins established the Mirage Raceway to fuel their technological rivalry, endlessly trying to outdo each other in speed, engineering, and reckless bravado.",al={"raceway lore","why are they racing","gnomes and goblins salt flats"}},{q="What happened to the dwarven dig site in the south?",a="The Rustmaul Dig Site was initially established by dwarven archaeologists and soon raided by a Horde strike force. However, both groups were forced to flee when the excavations broke into subterranean silithid tunnels, releasing swarms of insectoid horrors that overrun the southern flats.",al={"rustmaul dig site lore","what happened to rustmaul","bugs in salt flats"}},{q="Where does the road through the Shimmering Flats lead?",a="Following the tracks southeast across the salt pan leads directly to the mountain pass that opens into the vast desert of Tanaris and the neutral port of Gadgetzan.",al={"where does shimmering flats go","how to get to tanaris","exit to tanaris"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The salt flats are a pilgrimage site for engineers, littered with scrap, fuel experiments, and high-speed vehicular trial runs fueled by the endless rivalry between goblin and gnomish machinists.",["race:Gnome"]="Out on the Mirage Raceway, gnomish pilots and mechanostriders boldly defend gnomish engineering pride against the volatile, explosive designs of the Bilgewater and Steamwheedle cartels."},kw={"mirage raceway","pozzik","rustmaul","salt flats","shimmering flats","silithid","tanaris","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","zone:tanaris","subzone:rustmaul-dig-site","npc:pozzik","quest:1179","quest:788"},src={"Shimmering Flats"}}
E["subzone:southsea-holdfast"] = {t="subzone",n="Southsea Holdfast",z="thousandneedles",s="Southsea Holdfast is a pirate stronghold perched high on the cliff walls overlooking the eastern reaches of Thousand Needles. From this elevated camp, Southsea Freebooters stage smuggling operations and direct attacks throughout the canyon flats. Led locally by the pirate boss Tony Two-Tusk, the holdfast serves as a fortified haven for cutthroats far inland from the open ocean.",h="Southsea Holdfast is a pirate stronghold perched high on the cliff walls overlooking the eastern reaches of...",sec={{t="A Den of Scoundrels",b="Carved into the cliffs bordering the Shimmering Flats, the Southsea Holdfast gives the Southsea Pirates commanding vantage points over the surrounding canyon. Despite being surrounded by desert stone and salt, these corsairs have established a thriving inland redoubt. They raid supply lines heading to and from Tanaris, prey on passing caravans, and stockpile stolen goods away from naval patrols.",sp=0},{t="The Admiral's Reach",b="Deep within the camp grounds lies the Admiral's Den, the personal shelter of Tony Two-Tusk. Under his leadership, the crew fiercely defends their mountain perch against meddling adventurers and encroaching competitors alike. Anyone venturing into the holdfast must contend with a tight network of sentries, cutthroats, and dockhands who treat intruders with no mercy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are pirates doing out in the middle of a desert canyon?",a="The Southsea Pirates operate throughout southern Kalimdor, maintaining hideouts where maritime authorities and major factions cannot easily project force. The cliffs of Thousand Needles allow them to overlook trade routes across the salt flats and raid travellers heading between the canyon and Tanaris.",al={"why are pirates here","southsea pirates in thousand needles","pirates inland"}},{q="Who leads the pirates at Southsea Holdfast?",a="The outpost is commanded by Tony Two-Tusk, a ruthless Southsea pirate boss who keeps watch from the Admiral's Den, a cavern tucked securely inside the holdfast.",al={"holdfast boss","who is the boss here","tony two tusk"}},{q="Where is Southsea Holdfast located?",a="It is situated high along the cliffs in the southeastern portion of Thousand Needles, bordering the path leading down toward the Shimmering Flats and Tanaris.",al={"holdfast location","where is southsea holdfast","how to find holdfast"}},{q="Are the pirates here affiliated with the Southsea Freebooters in Tanaris?",a="Yes. They belong to the broader Southsea Pirates syndicate, operating inland support outposts that connect their coastal strongholds in Tanaris and the Barrens to overland raiding networks.",al={"tanaris pirates","southsea connection","are they same pirates"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The bustling encampment offers ample opportunity for pickpockets and scoundrels to relieve pirate sentries of coin pouches and lockboxes."},kw={"admiral's den","freebooters","pirate outpost","southsea holdfast","southsea pirates","thousand needles","tony two-tusk"},rel={"topic:pirate","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin","topic:gnome"},src={"Southsea Holdfast"}}
E["subzone:speedbarge-bar"] = {t="subzone",n="Speedbarge Bar",z="thousandneedles",s="Tucked away beneath the deck of Fizzle and Pozzik's vessel, the Speedbarge Bar serves as the social heart and local tavern for the engineers and spectators of Thousand Needles. Run by the barkeep Daisy alongside Hotfix, it offers a sheltered retreat where travelers can escape the glaring desert sun and share a strong drink.",h="Tucked away beneath the deck of Fizzle and Pozzik's vessel, the Speedbarge Bar serves as the social heart and...",sec={{t="Below the Decks",b="While engineers tinker and race above, the underdeck of the massive floating barge houses a cozy tavern. Managed by the welcoming Daisy with assistance from Hotfix, the Speedbarge Bar provides lodging and sustenance to adventurers traveling through the canyon. With bottles of stiff grog flowing freely, the tavern balances the chaotic camaraderie of rival goblin and gnomish tinkerers with the occasional spirited scuffle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Speedbarge Bar located?",a="The bar is situated below deck aboard Fizzle and Pozzik's Speedbarge, the large waterborne platform located in Thousand Needles.",al={"speedbarge bar location","where is speedbarge inn","speedbarge tavern"}},{q="Who runs the Speedbarge Bar?",a="Daisy tends bar and oversees innkeeping duties for visitors, while Hotfix works alongside her below deck to keep the establishment running.",al={"speedbarge innkeeper","who is the barkeep","daisy speedbarge"}},{q="Can travelers rest and stay at the bar?",a="Yes, Daisy serves as both tavernkeeper and innkeeper, offering weary adventurers a place to rest their heads and bind their hearthstones away from the elements.",al={"is speedbarge an inn","speedbarge hearthstone","can you bind at speedbarge"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The tavern serves as a handy local waterhole, where cooks and adventurers can grab a mug of grog and take inspiration from tavern fare.",["profession:Engineering"]="Located right below the bustling craft tables and launch bays of the barge, it is the natural gathering spot to toast successful inventions or mourn catastrophic malfunctions."},kw={"daisy","fizzle and pozzik","grog","hotfix","inn","speedbarge bar","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","npc:pozzik"},src={"Speedbarge Bar"}}
E["subzone:splithoof-crag"] = {t="subzone",n="Splithoof Crag",z="thousandneedles",s="Splithoof Crag is a fortified settlement of the Galak centaur, tucked along the northern cliffs of Thousand Needles. It serves as one of the tribe's major enclaves alongside the high mesas, guarding the entrance to Splithoof Hold. Travelers traversing the canyon floor must contend with aggressive Galak patrols roaming near the bluffs.",h="Splithoof Crag is a fortified settlement of the Galak centaur, tucked along the northern cliffs of Thousand...",sec={{t="A Galak Stronghold",b="Nestled against the sheer northern rock face of Thousand Needles, Splithoof Crag sits just east of the towering Darkcloud Pinnacle. It is an established enclave of the Galak centaur, complete with crude tent encampments and dirt pathways cutting through the crags. At the heart of the village against the cliffside lies Splithoof Hold, a subterranean cavern holding the Cloven Hoof, an ancient relic of the centaur safeguarded by a sacred brazier.",sp=0},{t="Defending the Caverns",b="The Galak fiercely contest this corner of the canyon, clashing with any travelers, Horde expeditions, or tauren scouting parties wandering beneath their bluffs. While the Grimtotem occupy the soaring pinnacles nearby, the centaur hold firm control of this canyon ravine and the caverns burrowed deep beneath the stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Splithoof Crag?",a="The settlement belongs to the Galak centaur tribe, one of the prominent clans inhabiting Thousand Needles alongside the hostile Grimtotem tauren.",al={"who is at splithoof crag","splithoof crag mobs","centaur in splithoof crag"}},{q="Where is Splithoof Crag located?",a="It lies along the northern canyon wall of Thousand Needles, situated directly east of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"where is splithoof crag","splithoof crag location"}},{q="What is inside Splithoof Hold?",a="Splithoof Hold is the central cavern of the village. Deep within its chambers, the Galak guard the Cloven Hoof, an ancient tribal artifact shielded by a sacred flame burning in an ancient brazier.",al={"what is splithoof hold","cave in splithoof crag"}},{q="Are the centaur here allied with the nearby Grimtotem?",a="No. The Galak centaur and the Grimtotem tauren on Darkcloud Pinnacle are bitter territorial rivals, fighting for dominance over this stretch of the canyon.",al={"grimtotem and galak","centaur and tauren relation"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The long-standing hostility between tauren and centaur makes Splithoof Crag an immediate concern for Horde scouts monitoring hostile activity throughout Thousand Needles.",["faction:Horde"]="Controlling the passage beneath the crags is vital for ensuring secure travel between the southern Barrens, Freewind Post, and the Shimmering Flats."},kw={"centaur","cloven hoof","darkcloud pinnacle","galak","splithoof crag","splithoof hold","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:splithoof-hold","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle"},src={"Splithoof Crag"}}
E["subzone:splithoof-heights"] = {t="subzone",n="Splithoof Heights",z="thousandneedles",s="Splithoof Heights refers to the elevated mesas bordering the northern cliffs of Thousand Needles, overlooking the jagged riverbed canyons below. The heights are heavily frequented by the ferocious Galak centaur, whose warbands roam the cliffs between their strongholds at Splithoof Hold and Splithoof Crag. Travelers passing through the needles must constantly watch the high ridges for charging centaur raiding parties.",h="Splithoof Heights refers to the elevated mesas bordering the northern cliffs of Thousand Needles, overlooking...",sec={{t="Territory of the Galak",b="Rising along the sheer canyon walls of northern Thousand Needles, these lofty plateaus sit above the arid canyon floor. The area serves as elevated roaming grounds for the brutal Galak tribe of centaur, who use the commanding terrain to keep watch over the surrounding trails. From these ridges, sentries maintain sightlines linking strongholds such as Splithoof Hold, Splithoof Crag, and Camp E'thok, making any trespass into the northern cliffs extremely dangerous for travelers.",sp=0},{t="A Hostile Watchpost",b="The Galak tribe has contested the canyon reaches of Thousand Needles for generations, fiercely defying the tauren of Freewind Post and raiding anyone entering the region. The heights provide them with natural defensive bastions, sheltered from the flash floods and dust storms of the valley floor. Anyone journeying beneath the bluffs should keep their eyes turned upward, as Galak scouts rarely hesitate to descend upon the unprepared.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Splithoof Heights?",a="The heights are dominated by the Galak centaur, a belligerent tribe native to Thousand Needles. They patrol the rocky plateaus and maintain ties to nearby settlements like Splithoof Hold and Splithoof Crag.",al={"who lives at splithoof heights","splithoof heights mobs","who controls splithoof"}},{q="Why is this area important to the centaur?",a="The high vantage point allows the Galak tribe to watch the canyon pathways below, safeguarding their strongholds while positioning scouts to spot approaching threats or vulnerable caravans traversing the needles.",al={"why are centaur on the heights","centaur heights purpose"}},{q="Where is Splithoof Heights located?",a="Splithoof Heights encompasses the high northern ridges of Thousand Needles, perched directly above the arid canyon floor and near the major Galak centaur fortifications.",al={"splithoof heights location","where is splithoof heights"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Galak tribe has long harassed tauren travelers moving between the Barrens and Freewind Post, making these centaur-held heights an enduring threat to your people.",["faction:Horde"]="Controlling the canyon approaches means keeping the Galak centaur on the cliffs from ambushing supply lines and caravans passing through Thousand Needles."},kw={"camp e'thok","centaur","galak","splithoof crag","splithoof heights","splithoof hold","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:splithoof-hold","subzone:splithoof-crag","subzone:camp-e-thok","topic:centaur"},src={"Splithoof Heights"}}
E["subzone:splithoof-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Splithoof Hold",z="thousandneedles",s="Splithoof Hold is a deep cavern stronghold carved into the stone of Splithoof Crag in Thousand Needles. Held by the Galak centaur tribe, the cavern serves as a fortified den and houses the Ancient Brazier, a site holding an eternally burning sacred flame.",h="Splithoof Hold is a deep cavern stronghold carved into the stone of Splithoof Crag in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Centaur Bastion",b="Tucked away inside Splithoof Crag, Splithoof Hold serves as a fortified redoubt for the Galak centaur. Unlike the windswept canyon floor, this enclosed cave offers them shelter, defensible chokepoints, and a secure sanctuary from rival tribes and travelers passing through the Needles.",sp=0},{t="The Sacred Flame",b="Deep within the shadowed recesses of the hold lies an ancient brazier cradling the Sacred Flame. This mystic fire burns incessantly, serving as a focal point of power and ritual reverence for the centaur and an object of deep curiosity for spiritual wanderers across the canyon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Splithoof Hold located?",a="Splithoof Hold is situated within the crags and ramparts of Splithoof Crag, along the southern cliffs of Thousand Needles. It is entered through a cave opening nestled inside the main centaur settlement.",al={"splithoof hold location","where is splithoof hold","how to find splithoof hold"}},{q="Who controls Splithoof Hold?",a="The cavern is held by the Galak centaur tribe, who aggressively defend the cave against outsiders, beast incursions, and the nearby tauren of Freewind Post.",al={"who lives in splithoof hold","splithoof hold mobs","who owns splithoof hold"}},{q="What is inside the hold?",a="Beyond hostile Galak centaur defenders, the cave houses the Ancient Brazier, an artifact that keeps the mystical Sacred Flame burning eternally within the depths of the rock.",al={"what is in splithoof hold","ancient brazier location","sacred flame splithoof"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Galak centaur remain sworn blood enemies of the tauren, making any stronghold they maintain in Thousand Needles an immediate threat to the peace of Freewind Post.",["class:Shaman"]="The existence of an eternal flame burning deep within a dark stone cavern draws the attention of any spiritualist attuned to the primal mysteries of elemental fire."},kw={"ancient brazier","galak centaur","sacred flame","splithoof crag","splithoof hold","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:splithoof-crag","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","quest:1195"},src={"Splithoof Hold"}}
E["subzone:sunken-dig-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Sunken Dig Site",z="thousandneedles",s="In the arid canyon of Thousand Needles, the excavation known across later eras as the Sunken Dig Site is currently the dry, silithid-infested Rustmaul Dig Site. Adventurers who explore the canyon floor find an active prospecting ground overrun by alien insectoids rather than floodwaters. Any notion of flooded shafts belongs strictly to tales of distant, speculative futures.",h="In the arid canyon of Thousand Needles, the excavation known across later eras as the Sunken Dig Site is...",sec={{t="A Dry and Infested Excavation",b="Before any great deluge altered southern Kalimdor, the southern canyons of Thousand Needles remained baking, dust-choked stone. Here, dwarven prospectors sought subterranean minerals and Titan remnants, only to disturb the ravenous silithid lurking beneath the earth. The site was rapidly overrun by insectoid horrors, transforming the dig shafts and nearby rock outcroppings into a lethal hive colony rather than an underwater curiosity.",sp=0},{t="Prospects Cut Short",b="While later rumors speak of gnomish ice cream operations and submerged wreckage, the harsh present reality in year 25 ADP is much more grounded. The area remains known as the Rustmaul Dig Site, an active danger zone where surface miners struggle against aggressive burrowers and chitinous hunters that threaten anyone traversing the southern passes toward Tanaris.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Is the Sunken Dig Site flooded right now?",a="No. In the present era of 25 ADP, Thousand Needles is entirely dry rock, salt flats, and canyon floor. The flooded Sunken Dig Site exists only in accounts of possible cataclysms yet to come; right now, it is the dry, bug-infested Rustmaul Dig Site.",al={"is it underwater","sunken dig site water","why isn't it flooded"}},{q="What is the site called in this era?",a="Currently, travelers know this excavation as the Rustmaul Dig Site. It was an ambitious prospecting venture that met a violent end when the workers dug straight into a silithid hive.",al={"rustmaul dig site","dig site name","what is this place called"}},{q="Who occupies the dig site currently?",a="The excavation is completely overrun by the silithid—chitinous, insectoid predators that tunnel under Kalimdor. Any miners who originally worked the claims were either killed or driven off.",al={"monsters here","who lives at rustmaul","silithid in thousand needles"}},{q="Where is the gnome Brivelthwerp and his ice cream boat?",a="Brivelthwerp and his tugboat are not here. Without a massive body of water filling the canyon, there is nowhere for a boat to float, and his ill-fated refrigeration venture has not taken place.",al={"where is brivelthwerp","ice cream quest","tugboat location"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The abandoned tools and exposed stone around the excavation are tempting, but the silithid infestation makes prospecting here suicidal for all but the most heavily armed miners.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven excavation teams pushed deep into the canyon floor seeking archaeological riches, only to discover that unearthing ancient horrors is an occupational hazard in Kalimdor."},kw={"brivelthwerp","excavation","rustmaul dig site","silithid","sunken dig site","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:rustmaul-dig-site","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},src={"Sunken Dig Site"}}
E["subzone:tahonda-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Tahonda Ruins",z="thousandneedles",s="The Tahonda Ruins are the sun-bleached remnants of an ancient tauren settlement swallowed by the salt and sand of the Shimmering Flats. Little is remembered of the villagers who once lived here, and dangerous Saltstone basilisks now stalk among the decaying tent poles and shredded leather.",h="The Tahonda Ruins are the sun-bleached remnants of an ancient tauren settlement swallowed by the salt and...",sec={{t="Sunken beneath the Salt",b="Situated in the southern reaches of the Shimmering Flats near the pass into Tanaris, the Tahonda Ruins stand as a somber monument to an abandoned tauren past. The village fell long ago, its weathered structures gradually engulfed by shifting white salt crusts. While some suspect the local Saltstone basilisks drove the inhabitants away, odd clues linger on the surviving structures. Two distinct sets of three parallel tears cut through the leather of a ruined lodge, suggesting the village met a violent end at the claws of powerful predators or hostile invaders before the desert claimed what remained.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were the Tahonda Ruins originally?",a="Tahonda was once a tauren village built upon the dry expanse of the Shimmering Flats. Over time, the village fell into ruin and was gradually swallowed by shifting sands and salt crusts.",al={"what is tahonda ruins","who built tahonda","tahonda ruins history"}},{q="Why was the village abandoned?",a="No written history preserves the exact fate of the village. The ruins are currently overrun by vicious Saltstone basilisks, which may have driven the settlers out. However, deep three-clawed tears raked across the surviving leather lodges suggest a sudden, violent attack.",al={"why is tahonda ruined","what destroyed tahonda","what happened to tahonda"}},{q="What creatures live in the ruins now?",a="The remnants of the village are thoroughly infested with hostile Saltstone basilisks that sun themselves among the rotting wooden poles and tattered hide shelters.",al={"tahonda mobs","what is at tahonda ruins","tahonda beasts"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Finding a forgotten tauren settlement sinking beneath the salt of Thousand Needles is a poignant reminder of the dangers your nomadic ancestors faced wandering Kalimdor."},kw={"saltstone basilisks","shimmering flats","tahonda","tahonda ruins","tauren village","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","zone:tanaris"},src={"Tahonda Ruins"}}
E["subzone:tirth-s-haunt"] = {t="subzone",n="Tirth's Haunt",z="thousandneedles",s="Tirth's Haunt is a lonely, peculiar campsite located in the arid flatlands of Thousand Needles, situated just south of the Southsea Holdfast. It serves as the refuge of the eccentric hermit Magus Tirth and his unusual companion, a polymorphed chicken named \"Plucky\" Johnson. Adventurers, particularly wandering mages, occasionally cross the scorched salt flats to consult the eccentric spellcaster.",h="Tirth's Haunt is a lonely, peculiar campsite located in the arid flatlands of Thousand Needles, situated just...",sec={{t="A Magus in the Salt Flats",b="Perched in the harsh, sun-baked landscape of Thousand Needles, Tirth's Haunt is little more than a spartan camp just south of the Southsea Holdfast. The camp is dominated by the unpredictable Magus Tirth, a mage of considerable talent who has isolated himself far from the arcane towers of civilization. Instead of scholarly peers, Tirth shares his solitary haunt with an unfortunate polymorphed human named \"Plucky\" Johnson, whom the magus relentlessly badgers. Despite his erratic temperament and bizarre isolation, Tirth remains an arcane practitioner of genuine skill, drawing travelers seeking odd spells, strange ingredients, or ancient warlock and mage lore across the desert dust.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tirth's Haunt located?",a="Tirth's Haunt is situated in the eastern reaches of Thousand Needles, right on the fringes of the Shimmering Flats and just south of the pirate stronghold known as Southsea Holdfast.",al={"tirth location","where is tirth haunt","where is magus tirth"}},{q="Who lives at Tirth's Haunt?",a="The camp is inhabited by the eccentric human mage Magus Tirth and a chicken named \"Plucky\" Johnson. Tirth keeps to himself out in the desert, though his sanity is somewhat dubious and he spends much of his time tormenting his feathered companion.",al={"who is at tirth haunt","tirth camp resident","who is tirth"}},{q="What is the deal with the chicken named Plucky?",a="\"Plucky\" Johnson is not a natural bird, but rather a human who ran afoul of arcane magic and was permanently polymorphed into a chicken. Magus Tirth keeps Plucky around his campsite, frequently zapping and berating him.",al={"who is plucky","plucky chicken","why is plucky a chicken"}},{q="Why would adventurers visit this campsite?",a="Mages and spellcasters often seek out Tirth as part of their arcane training and trials. Despite his bizarre demeanor, Tirth possesses specialized knowledge of wandmaking, rare reagents, and ritual magics.",al={"why go to tirth haunt","tirth quests","what does tirth do"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Mages wandering Thousand Needles may find business with Tirth, an eccentric peer living in isolation whose arcane mastery remains formidable despite his peculiarities."},kw={"magus tirth","plucky","polymorph","shimmering flats","southsea holdfast","thousand needles","tirth's haunt"},rel={"npc:mad-magus-tirth","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:southsea-holdfast"},src={"Tirth's Haunt"}}
E["subzone:twilight-bulwark"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Bulwark",z="thousandneedles",s="Perched upon the high canyon shelves of southern Thousand Needles, the Twilight Bulwark serves as an entrenched redoubt for the doomsday cult known as the Twilight's Hammer. From this elevated bastion overlooking the gorge, cultists conduct insidious rituals and guard captive prisoners away from prying eyes. Their menacing presence threatens travelers and poses an active danger to nearby settlements across the Needles.",h="Perched upon the high canyon shelves of southern Thousand Needles, the Twilight Bulwark serves as an...",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Needles",b="The Twilight Bulwark is a fortified outpost carved into the craggy shelves of southern Thousand Needles. Occupied by cultists loyal to the Twilight's Hammer, this outpost is thoroughly fortified against outside intrusion. The enclave is overseen by an entrenched leadership that coordinates cult activity across the area, coordinating dark elemental experiments while maintaining tight security along the rugged cliffs.",sp=0},{t="Hostages and Infiltration",b="Beyond mere territorial ambitions, the Bulwark functions as a high-security holding camp for enemies of the cult. The Grimtotem matriarch Magatha has been captured and bound within the eastern perimeter by specialized cult wards. Recognizing the strategic threat, infiltrators seeking to disrupt the cult's plans have lurked at the outpost's approaches, donning captured cultist vestments to slip past watchful eyes and bypass the garrison's formidable defenses.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Twilight Bulwark?",a="The Twilight Bulwark is a fortified encampment belonging to the Twilight's Hammer cult, situated high on the southern cliff shelves of Thousand Needles.",al={"twilight bulwark","what is twilight bulwark","twilight bulwark thousand needles"}},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="The stronghold is commanded by key figures of the Twilight's Hammer hierarchy, specifically Commander Fastfuse, Codemaster Deethuk, and Elementalist Starion, who manage the cultist forces and their captives.",al={"who runs twilight bulwark","bulwark leaders","twilight bulwark bosses"}},{q="Who is being held prisoner here?",a="Magatha Grimtotem is held prisoner in the eastern part of the Bulwark, bound by specialized security bindings that require an exact code to dismantle.",al={"twilight bulwark prisoner","magatha captive","who is locked up at twilight bulwark"},sp=1},{q="Who is Lakota Windsong and what is she doing near the Bulwark?",a="Lakota Windsong is an operative who positions herself near the approach to the outpost, having slain a cult member to wear their robes as an undercover disguise to infiltrate the stronghold.",al={"lakota windsong","tauren in disguise","disguised cultist lakota"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Twilight's Hammer operations so close to Freewind Post pose a direct security hazard to the Horde's hold over Thousand Needles, particularly with Magatha Grimtotem held captive in their clutches.",["class:Shaman"]="The presence of Elementalist Starion demonstrates the cult's relentless corruption and coercion of elemental forces, a grave offense that every servant of the elements must oppose."},kw={"deethuk","fastfuse","lakota windsong","magatha grimtotem","starion","thousand needles","twilight bulwark","twilight's hammer"},rel={"topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:freewind-post","npc:magatha-grimtotem","npc:lakota-windsong","subzone:roguefeather-den"},src={"Twilight Bulwark"}}
E["subzone:twilight-withering"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Withering",z="thousandneedles",s="The Twilight Withering is an elevated outpost held by the sinister Twilight's Hammer cult in Thousand Needles. Perched southeast of Freewind Post and east of the Twilight Bulwark, it serves as a staging ground for the cult's apocalyptic elemental rituals.",h="The Twilight Withering is an elevated outpost held by the sinister Twilight's Hammer cult in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Looming Catastrophe",b="Situated atop the arid mesas southeast of Freewind Post, the Twilight Withering represents a dire threat to Thousand Needles. Here, the nihilistic zealots of the Twilight's Hammer labor over dark elemental sorcery. Within the camp, cultists seek to harness raw primordial fury, binding and feeding elemental energies into unstable monstrosities designed to scour the surrounding canyon floor.",sp=0},{t="Dark Rituals on the Heights",b="The camp operates in concert with the nearby Twilight Bulwark, securing the cult's presence overlooking the needle-rock spires. Amid their ritual circles and altars, cultists employ dark artifacts to subjugate primal powers, indifferent to the devastation such unchecked magic poses to the delicate balance of the arid landscape.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Twilight Withering?",a="The Twilight Withering is a fortified encampment belonging to the Twilight's Hammer cult, located on an elevated shelf southeast of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",al={"twilight withering","what is this place","cultist camp needles"}},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="The camp is inhabited and defended by zealots, geomancers, and summoners of the Twilight's Hammer cult alongside their bound elemental servants.",al={"who is here","twilight withering mobs","enemies here"}},{q="What are the cultists doing here?",a="The cultists are conducting dangerous elemental rituals, attempting to subjugate and combine disparate elemental forces into volatile weapons of mass devastation.",al={"what are they doing","twilight withering goal","cultist ritual"}},{q="How does this site connect to the Twilight Bulwark?",a="The Twilight Withering lies just east of the Twilight Bulwark, forming an interconnected network of ritual encampments that overlook the canyons of Thousand Needles.",al={"twilight bulwark connection","bulwark to withering","nearby camp"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The blatant subjugation, binding, and corruption of primal elementals by the Twilight's Hammer cultists here represents a grave affront to the natural harmony of the elements.",["faction:Horde"]="Cultist encampments perched so close to Freewind Post pose an intolerable threat to the Tauren settled on the neighboring bluffs."},kw={"cultists","elementals","freewind post","thousand needles","twilight bulwark","twilight withering","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:twilight-bulwark","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:freewind-post","npc:magatha-grimtotem","quest:5088"},src={"Twilight Withering"}}
E["subzone:weathered-nook"] = {t="subzone",n="Weathered Nook",z="thousandneedles",s="Tucked away along the northern cliffside of Thousand Needles, the Weathered Nook is a secluded cleft and shelter perched high above the canyon floor. Overlooking the vast sea of stone spires, it serves as a modest home and retreat for solitary tauren dwellers seeking quiet contemplation away from bustling settlements.",h="Tucked away along the northern cliffside of Thousand Needles, the Weathered Nook is a secluded cleft and...",sec={{t="Haven on the Cliffs",b="Carved into the sheer sandstone wall north of Freewind Post, the Weathered Nook is easily missed by travelers passing along the canyon basin below. A natural ramp winds up the cliff face, leading to a sheltered ledge and cave out of the prevailing winds. Rather than housing a military outpost or large settlement, the nook serves as a humble homestead for solitary wanderers like Dorn Plainstalker and Prate Cloudseer, offering safety, seclusion, and a sweeping view across the windswept needle plateaus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Weathered Nook located?",a="The nook is nestled along the northern cliff wall of Thousand Needles. From Freewind Post, travel north until you reach the towering rock face, then follow the cliffs east until you find a winding ramp leading up the mesa wall.",al={"how to find weathered nook","weathered nook location","where is nook"}},{q="Who lives in the Weathered Nook?",a="The shelter is home to Dorn Plainstalker and Prate Cloudseer, solitary tauren who have chosen this remote ledge above the canyon rather than dwelling atop the crowded towers of Freewind Post.",al={"who is here","weathered nook residents","npcs in nook"}},{q="Is the Weathered Nook affiliated with the Horde?",a="While the residents are tauren and align naturally with their kindred, the nook is not a formal Horde garrison. It is a humble personal camp and dwelling tucked quietly into the wilderness.",al={"is this a horde camp","horde weathered nook"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, the Weathered Nook represents the quiet spirit of self-reliance, offering a peaceful vantage point across the canyon to commune with the elements away from the busy bridges of Freewind Post.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde wanderers exploring the heights of the canyon walls will find friendly kindred sheltering here along the northern cliffs."},kw={"cave","cliff","dorn plainstalker","freewind post","prate cloudseer","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:freewind-post"},src={"Weathered Nook"}}
E["subzone:weazel-s-crater"] = {t="subzone",n="Weazel's Crater",z="thousandneedles",s="Weazel's Crater is a deep gouge carved into the hard salt of the northern Shimmering Flats. Named after someone who either discovered the hollow or violently created it, the pit is a stark reminder of the reckless experiments and high-speed crashes common to the local speedway.",h="Weazel's Crater is a deep gouge carved into the hard salt of the northern Shimmering Flats.",sec={{t="A Volatile Legacy",b="Across the blinding white expanse of the Shimmering Flats, experimental goblin and gnome rocket-cars constantly push the boundaries of mechanical sanity. Debris, scorched earth, and impact hollows litter the plains, but Weazel's Crater stands out for its sheer size and depth. While records do not specify exactly what went wrong, the crater's name strongly hints at a spectacularly failed test run or an explosive mechanical catastrophe. Today, the mechanical wreckage has largely settled, and the hollow has been claimed as a sunning pit by aggressive Saltstone basilisks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What caused Weazel's Crater?",a="Its exact origin is not formally recorded, but it is widely believed to be the result of a catastrophic explosion or a high-speed crash involving unstable goblin or gnomish rocket vehicles on the flats.",al={"how was weazel's crater formed","weazels crater origin","why is there a crater here"}},{q="Who is Weazel?",a="The crater is named after an individual named Weazel, though it remains a mystery whether Weazel was the unfortunate inventor whose experiment violently excavated the hole or simply the explorer who discovered it.",al={"who was weazel","who is weazel named after"}},{q="What lives in the crater now?",a="The depression is currently inhabited by dangerous Saltstone basilisks, which lurk along the rocky edges and bottom of the pit.",al={"weazels crater mobs","what is inside the crater"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The massive blast mark serves as a cautionary tale—or a monument of pride—for engineers testing rocket fuel and high-speed contraptions out on the flats."},kw={"gnome engineering","goblin raceway","saltstone basilisks","shimmering flats","thousand needles","weazel's crater"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin","topic:gnome"},src={"Weazel's Crater"}}
E["subzone:westreach-summit"] = {t="subzone",n="Westreach Summit",z="thousandneedles",s="Westreach Summit is a high tauren encampment situated on the northwestern rim of Thousand Needles. Perched along the borders overlooking the canyon, the settlement serves as a vital Horde foothold while facing persistent pressure from the hostile Grimtotem tribe.",h="Westreach Summit is a high tauren encampment situated on the northwestern rim of Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Watchtower on the Canyons",b="Occupying a high ridge in the northwestern corner of Thousand Needles, Westreach Summit functions as a sentinel post overlooking the towering stone pillars below. Led by Kanati Greycloud and defended by steadfast braves, this outpost maintains watchful eyes on regional threats. Its strategic perch connects Horde scouts and travelers traversing between central Kalimdor and the perilous chasms of the Needles.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Grimtotem",b="Peace is rare atop the summit. The settlement finds itself under continuous siege from marauding members of the Grimtotem tribe, who dispute the Horde's presence and seek dominion over the region's high perches. Kanati Greycloud and the Summit Defenders hold the line against these aggressors, while scouts like Motega Firemane monitor nearby water sources and pathways to ensure the encampment remains secured.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Westreach Summit?",a="It is a fortified tauren outpost belonging to the Horde, located in the northwestern heights of Thousand Needles. It acts as an observation point and defense hub for the canyon approaches.",al={"westreach summit location","what is westreach","westreach outpost"}},{q="Who leads the defense here?",a="Kanati Greycloud oversees the camp and coordinates the defense alongside the Summit Defenders to hold off enemy incursions.",al={"who is in charge of westreach","westreach summit leader","kanati greycloud"}},{q="Why is the summit being attacked?",a="Hostile members of the Grimtotem tribe frequently assault the camp, seeking to drive the Horde out and assert their own undisputed control over the bluffs.",al={"who attacks westreach","grimtotem attack westreach","why fight at westreach summit"}},{q="Can you fly from Westreach Summit?",a="Yes, the encampment maintains a flight master named Nah'te who connects travelers across Kalimdor's major regional outposts.",al={"westreach flight master","flight path westreach summit"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Westreach Summit is an indispensable waystation and defensive bastion against aggressive Grimtotem forces threatening Horde transit through the canyons.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, the summit represents the painful strife within their own kind, where loyal braves must defend their ground against the violent aggression of the Grimtotem."},kw={"grimtotem","kanati greycloud","motega firemane","nah'te","summit defenders","thousand needles","westreach summit"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:grimtotem-tribe","topic:horde","npc:kanati-greycloud","npc:motega-firemane","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:crossroads"},src={"Westreach Summit"}}
E["subzone:whitereach-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Whitereach Post",z="thousandneedles",s="Whitereach Post is a small Horde encampment nestled along the dusty canyon path in Thousand Needles. Serving as a minor waystation near Camp E'thok, it offers respite and watchful eyes over the harsh desert highway. For travelers moving between Feralas and the salt flats, it stands as an outpost of Horde safety beneath the looming sandstone pillars.",h="Whitereach Post is a small Horde encampment nestled along the dusty canyon path in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Waystation in the Canyons",b="Perched along the beaten path winding through the depths of Thousand Needles, Whitereach Post is one of several modest Horde footholds carved out of the rugged landscape. Stationed in close proximity to Camp E'thok, the post helps maintain a reliable presence along the canyon floor, monitoring travel between the windswept mesas. While not as fortified as the great lift or major tribal settlements, it serves as an indispensable stop for couriers, scouts, and adventurers traversing the contested wastes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Whitereach Post?",a="Whitereach Post is a minor Horde outpost located along the primary canyon path in Thousand Needles, situated not far from Camp E'thok.",al={"whitereach","whitereach camp","where is whitereach post"}},{q="Which faction controls Whitereach Post?",a="It is controlled by the Horde, primarily maintained by tauren scouts keeping watch over the gorge trails.",al={"is whitereach horde","whitereach faction"}},{q="Who can be found stationed here?",a="The post is manned by local Horde scouts and wanderers, including the tauren Kanati Greycloud, who watches over the canyon passage.",al={"whitereach npcs","who lives at whitereach post"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Whitereach Post represents a vital resting point and scouting presence for Horde travelers journeying through the perilous canyons of Thousand Needles.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren scouts help secure this roadside camp, ensuring that tribesfolk moving between Mulgore, Feralas, and the Shimmering Flats have a safe place to rest."},kw={"camp e'thok","horde outpost","kanati greycloud","tauren","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde","subzone:camp-e-thok","npc:kanati-greycloud"},src={"Whitereach Post"}}
E["subzone:windbreak-canyon"] = {t="subzone",n="Windbreak Canyon",z="thousandneedles",s="Windbreak Canyon is a winding gorge along the northern side of Thousand Needles, situated between Freewind Post and the Shimmering Flats. Famous for its harsh drafts and jagged stone, it is heavily infested with nesting wind serpents. Travelers passing along the main road must tread carefully near its mouth to avoid being hunted from above.",h="Windbreak Canyon is a winding gorge along the northern side of Thousand Needles, situated between Freewind...",sec={{t="A Serpent Nest in the Needles",b="Carved into the sheer northern walls of the canyon floor, Windbreak Canyon spans a large stretch of territory east of Freewind Post. Rather than offering shelter, the ravine channels whistling winds between the rock spires, creating ideal perches for feral wind serpents. The predators lay their clutches along the stone ledges and strike at unwary travelers drifting off the main road. Those braving the canyon interior will also find the winding trails that climb upward toward the Weathered Nook.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Windbreak Canyon?",a="Windbreak Canyon lies on the northern side of Thousand Needles, roughly between Freewind Post and the eastern approach to the Shimmering Flats.",al={"windbreak canyon location","where is windbreak canyon","windbreak map"}},{q="What creatures live in Windbreak Canyon?",a="The canyon is dominated by aggressive wild wind serpents that nest among the crags and defend their clutches from intruders.",al={"windbreak monsters","what is in windbreak canyon","windbreak mobs"}},{q="Where does the trail inside the canyon lead?",a="Following the canyon's rising interior trails leads travelers toward the Weathered Nook nestled in the cliffs above.",al={"windbreak path","trail in windbreak canyon","where does windbreak go"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The wind serpents nesting throughout the canyon provide wilderness hunters an ideal opportunity to study and tame agile, lightning-spitting beasts."},kw={"freewind post","thousand needles","weathered nook","wind serpents","windbreak canyon"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:weathered-nook","subzone:shimmering-flats"},src={"Windbreak Canyon"}}
E["zone:thousandneedles"] = {t="zone",n="Thousand Needles",z="thousandneedles",s="Thousand Needles is a sprawling canyon of sheer sandstone pillars and sunbaked salt pans in southern Kalimdor. Tauren tribes cling to settlements atop towering mesas to escape aggressive centaur packs, while gnomish and goblin tinkerers run high-speed rocket cars across the dried-up seabed of the Shimmering Flats.",h="Thousand Needles is a sprawling canyon of sheer sandstone pillars and sunbaked salt pans in southern Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Forest of Stone",b="Before the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, this territory was a lush river canyon fed by inland waterways flowing out toward the sea. The cataclysm tore the continent apart, thrusting the riverbed above the water table and altering the river's path until only dry stone and sandstone spires remained. Today, dozens of slender cylindrical columns rise from the canyon floor like a petrified forest. Tauren settled on the summits, stringing precarious rope bridges between peaks to establish villages out of reach of the hostile centaur marauders patrolling the shadow-draped canyon floor below.",sp=0},{t="Peril on the Mesas",b="Atop the needle-like spires, life is far from peaceful. At Freewind Post, tauren loyal to the Horde contend not only with predatory wind serpents and wyverns from Highperch, but also with their treacherous kin: the militant Grimtotem clan entrenched at Darkcloud Pinnacle. Cliffwatcher Longhorn oversees the defense of the plateau, seeking bold fighters to strike at Grimtotem agitators and secure the fragile bridges linking the peaks. To the north, the enormous mechanical winches of the Great Lift carry travelers down from the southern Barrens, though crossing the canyon floor remains a deadly gambit.",sp=0},{t="The Mirage Raceway",b="To the southeast, the canyon walls peel back into the Shimmering Flats, an enormous, desiccated salt pan sitting below sea level. In this harsh, blinding white expanse, gnomes and goblins maintain an uneasy neutrality around the Mirage Raceway. Rival engineers Pozzik and Fizzle Brassbolts race experimental rocket cars across the hard salt to settle which race possesses technological superiority. The pit stop attracts scoundrels, swindlers like Kravel Koalbeard, and hunters hunting the hardy scorpions, turtles, and basilisks that roam the searing basin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How did Thousand Needles get its name?",a="The zone is named after the dozens of massive, cylindrical sandstone spires that erupt from the canyon bottom. Originally carved by rushing river currents before the Great Sundering, these geological towers now resemble a forest of giant needles.",al={"why is it called thousand needles","needle pillars origin","spires lore"}},{q="How do you get down into Thousand Needles from the Barrens?",a="Travelers take the Great Lift, an immense double-car elevator operated by Horde guards on the southern border of the Barrens. Stepping off the edge is fatal, so waiting for the platform is essential. Alliance travelers can also hike in from the west via Thalanaar in Feralas.",al={"how to get to thousand needles","great lift entrance","elevator to needles"}},{q="Why do the tauren live on top of the mesas?",a="Centaur warbands once pushed the nomadic tauren nearly to extinction. Building outposts like Freewind Post atop inaccessible stone pillars kept them safe from ground charges. They connected the mesas using wooden suspension bridges, allowing high-altitude travel above the predators and raiders below.",al={"why are tauren on pillars","freewind post history","tauren high ground"}},{q="What is the Mirage Raceway?",a="The Mirage Raceway is an engineering proving ground on the Shimmering Flats salt pan. Gnomish and goblin tinkerers run experimental rocket-propelled racecars across the flat salt bed to settle their ongoing rivalry over which race builds the finest machinery.",al={"salt flats track","gnome goblin race","rocket car track"}},{q="What is the Grimtotem presence in the canyon?",a="The Grimtotem clan occupies Darkcloud Pinnacle, a fortified cluster of spires directly opposing Freewind Post. Unlike the rest of the tauren tribes who pledged to the Horde, the Grimtotem actively attack other tauren and conspire to seize dominance over the mesas.",al={"grimtotem thousand needles","darkcloud pinnacle tauren","evil tauren needles"}},{q="What are the Shimmering Flats?",a="The Shimmering Flats are a vast, dried lakebed east of the canyon mesas. The salt crust formed when the ancient inland sea evaporated after the Sundering. The searing heat, blinding white salt, and harsh predators make it an inhospitable desert used mainly for high-speed vehicular testing.",al={"salt pan","white desert needles","eastern desert"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Freewind Post stands as a reminder of how high your people had to climb to escape centaur slaughter, and a staging ground against the treacherous Grimtotem at Darkcloud Pinnacle.",["race:Gnome"]="The Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats is your faction's premier chance to demonstrate the precision and elegance of gnomish engineering over shoddy goblin contraptions.",["profession:Engineering"]="The salt flats are a pilgrimage site for tinkerers looking to study rocket fuel, vehicle parts, and high-speed propulsion at the Mirage Raceway.",["faction:Horde"]="The Great Lift links the Barrens to your stronghold at Freewind Post, serving as a strategic southern boundary against centaur clans and rebel tauren."},kw={"cliffwatcher longhorn","darkcloud pinnacle","fizzle brassbolts","freewind post","great lift","grimtotem","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","pozzik","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:great-lift","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","zone:barrens","zone:feralas","zone:tanaris"},m={levels="25-35"},src={"Thousand Needles (Classic)","Thousand Needles"}}
